(Phnom Penh): At 2:00 pm on November 18, 2023, a violent theft occurred when two suspects on a motorbike armed with swords threatened a female victim with a mobile phone. One unit while traveling on the road in front of the football table on the corner of Keo Chenda Street, Village 2, Sangkat Chroy Changva, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
At 3:30 on the same day, after receiving the complaint, the Chroy Changvar District Armed Forces searched and arrested the two suspects, Sos Arafin, 34, a Khmer Muslim, and Kang Keo alias Blog. The 28-year-old man seized the following items: a sword, a black Smas motorcycle, license plate Phnom Penh-1Y-2770, and the mobile phone confiscated from the suspect was returned to the victim by the military police.
After listening to the answers, the two suspects confessed that they actually acted with a sword and stole a mobile phone from the real victim.
The suspect, Sos Arafin, added that he had been imprisoned once in 2017 in connection with a motorcycle theft and drug use case from 2017 to the present. As for the suspect, his name is Kang Keo, also known as Blog, he also said that he had been in a correctional center once in connection with a drug use case in 2015 and had used drugs from 2010 to the present.
(Phnom Penh): Special forces from the Anti-Drug Department of the National Police General Commission cracked down on drug delivery cases from Cambodia to Vietnam by detaining three Vietnamese suspects and confiscating nearly 1 kg of drugs and drugs. Not clear more than 60 kg.
The crackdown was carried out on the orders of General Sar Thet, the National Police Commissioner, under the command of General Mak Chito, Lt. Gen. Prum Santhor, Deputy Commissioner General for Anti-Drug Planning, and under the direct leadership of Lt. Gen. Kheung Sarath. Against drug offenses.
Currently, the suspects and exhibits of the Anti-Drug Department have built a case to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court according to the procedure.
Please be informed that under the strict order of General Sar Thet, the General Commissioner of the National Police has instructed the Anti-Drug Crime Department to eradicate all drug offenders, and the Anti-Drug Crime Department led by Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath is determined to Cracking down on drugs in the capitals and provinces, like the early rain, major drug crimes were cracked down on.
Global Peace Federation (UPF) strengthens cooperation with the National Assembly of Cambodia in peacebuilding mission
On that occasion, the National Assembly President praised the UPF's good mission in finding peace for the region and the world. Cambodia has always participated and supported this mission under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the founder of peace, and was succeeded by His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the 7th legislature, who is full of ability and energy.
