(Phnom Penh): During the fireworks display to celebrate the 70th anniversary of Cambodia-Japan relations on the night of November 19, 2023, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, said that in Phnom Penh, Japanese friends have provided official development assistance on Many physical infrastructure projects, while the volume of Cambodian-Japanese trade has also steadily increased.
The development project received by Phnom Penh Capital Administration, Mr. KHOURN Sreng described that the project to prevent flood and improve the canal-drainage system, Phase 1 to Phase 4, the construction of Choeung Ek wastewater treatment plant, the project to improve capacity Firefighting through the provision of used fire trucks, traffic management system development projects, education and health assistance projects.
In addition, in the private sector, the Cambodian-Japanese trade volume has also increased steadily, in Phnom Penh, Aeon Mall (Cambodia) Co., Ltd., a company of Japanese investors, has invested a considerable amount of money. On the shopping mall development project from the first project to the third project, with strong support from Cambodians from all walks of life.
Mr. Khuong Sreng affirmed that through this event, he has really contributed to the strengthening and expansion of strategic cooperation in all aspects of "Cambodia-Japan" to be more effective and fruitful.
Prime Minister Hun Manet considers market demand and farmers' income as more important than the type of crop to be grown or raised (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): On the occasion of announcing the implementation of priority political programs related to agriculture in the morning of November 20 In 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, considers the market demand and income of farmers when harvesting more important than the type of crop selected for planting or livestock.
In this sense, Samdech President Hun Manet emphasized that for Samdech on agricultural work, it does not matter what to raise or grow, that is, as long as farmers have a market and get a lot of income at harvest time, this is a big goal that Samdech wants.
However, the Prime Minister advised not to force the people to make immediate changes, demanding a clear and concise explanation and seeing tangible results. Samdech gave the example that if people used to farm but the area has potential for growing cashews, then it must be clearly shown to them.
Samdech Hun Sen continued that in order to meet the type of modern agriculture, it must be modern in terms of budget, equipment and modernization, and more consideration in order to keep up with the current situation. In particular, for products that are difficult to compete, the agricultural team must help farmers as much as possible.
According to Hun Manet, when farmers earn more and become a common force, competition with other countries will have more opportunities. All of these are in the 5th and 6th priority policies of the Royal Government to respond urgently to the people's livelihood problems.
Please be informed that in this 7th legislature, in addition to the introduction of the Pentagon Strategy - the first phase, which is the core policy, the Royal Government led by His Majesty the King Hun Manet also launched six priority political programs to respond immediately. And people's livelihood problems.
(Phnom Penh): General Pol Ratana, Chairman of the Party Working Group for Chong Ampil Commune, and his colleagues distributed gifts to 76 poor families living in Chong Ampil Commune in Chong Ampil Commune, Kanhcheak District, Prey Veng Province.
This activity took place on November 19, 2023 at the CPP office in Chong Ampil commune, Kanhchiech district, Prey Veng province, attended by Mr. Chhoeun Phi, Deputy Governor of Kanhchiech district, Chief of Chong Ampil commune and commune councilors, village chiefs, commune clerks, district chiefs. Health and Chief of Commune Administration Post.
The donations include: 25 kg of rice per family, 1 box of noodles, 1 stick of soy sauce, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of fish.
Gen. Pol Ratana also announced the sponsorship of six houses donated by General Sar Thet, the National Police Commissioner.
