(Kampong Thom): Honorary General Dr. Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, stated that the Royal Government led by His Excellency Hun Manet continues to pay attention to the lives and livelihoods of all veterans.
General Kun Kim said this during a visit to distribute food donations from the Royal Government of Cambodia to 141 families of Cambodian veterans who are poor and vulnerable to the recent floods. The social work concession is located in Kraya commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province this morning, November 20, 2023.
On that occasion, General Kun Kim conveyed the greetings and greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia to the veterans throughout Kampong Thom Province.
The Senior Minister also thanked the Cambodian Food Reserve System and the General Department of Agriculture for arranging the transportation of food packages and vegetable seed packages for distribution to veterans and their families. Each family receives 1 package of food (25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 can of canned fish, 1 can of fish sauce, 1 can of soy sauce and 1 can of pure water) along with 1 packet of vegetable seeds (kit).
The Senior Minister highlighted the merits of every veteran in the cause of the motherland in the face of civil war. The Senior Minister asserted that all veterans have made great contributions to the cause, that is, the achievements that Cambodia has today cannot be separated from the sacrifices of veterans in the past.
In return for the merits of veterans, the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Cambodian Veterans Association, has always paid close attention to the lives of veterans. The Royal Government of Cambodia has provided a number of policies to contribute to improving the lives of all veterans.
General Kun Kim emphasized, "In response to the hardships and improving the lives of veterans, Samdech Bovathibodi, President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, advised to continue the process of building houses and preparing social land concessions for distribution to poor veterans."
General Kun Kim did not forget to call on all veterans to join in maintaining the hard-earned peace, and all veterans are well aware of the hardships caused by the flames of war. The senior minister stressed that what Cambodian veterans get today is because Cambodia is peaceful.
On that occasion, General Kun Kim also urged the leaders of the association at all levels to continue to pay attention to veterans living in communes. Divide the tasks, meet, talk and connect more closely with the veterans in the family in the back of each house.
Defense Minister announces new Rector of Defense, Lt. Gen. Dok Sopha to replace General Chea Dara
(Phnom Penh): General Tea Seiha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, on the morning of November 20, 2023, announced the appointment of Lt. Gen. Dok Sopha, Rector of the National Defense University, to replace General Chea Dara. Appointed Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense.
The ceremony was held at Russey Keo National Defense University with the participation of the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense, the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, as well as a large number of officers, deputies and soldiers.
On that occasion, General Tea Seiha praised and thanked General Chea Dara, former Rector of the National Defense University, for his efforts to implement human resources in the field of defense by making significant contributions to The Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The defense minister added that in connection with this work of defense, the military and professors should gather to keep up with the state of the world, because now there are many modernization in the world, such as new technology, weapons, weapons, etc. are to keep up to date. How to release new lessons to the participants to know and follow all the information regularly.
Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha urged the new Rector of the National Defense University to strengthen solidarity and strengthen the training of trainees to effectively participate in safeguarding peace, territorial integrity, protecting the King, the Constitution, the legitimate Royal Government of the people.
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha also instructed military officers and lecturers at the National Defense University to find new curricula to teach the trainees in response to the growing military dam in the world.
On that occasion, the Minister of Defense also mentioned that the regional and global security situation is facing the complex changes of non-traditional security issues and traditional security issues that create a series of implications that pose a serious threat to global security. .
For example, security problems caused by Kovid 19, terrorism, security issues, technology, climate change have further affected the economic, environmental and social sectors. On the other hand, the effects of the eruption and the prolongation of the Russia-Ukraine war, the war between Israel and Hamas, the geopolitical influence and the trade and technology wars have all affected the economic recovery.
On the occasion of taking office, Lt. Gen. Dok Sopha was determined to continue his efforts to strengthen his knowledge in the field of national defense, as well as to implement the policy of the Royal Government in the seventh mandate under the leadership of Samdech Hun Manet better. .
Please be informed that prior to this appointment, Lt. Gen. Dok Sopha was the Vice Chancellor and Director of the Faculty of Social Sciences and Languages of the National Defense University.
(Kampot): Two foreign assailants were arrested by Kampot provincial police after abducting and robbing a foreigner for about $ 1,500. The robbery happened on November 20, 2023 at the Tela gas station in Kampong Kes village, Trapeang Sangke commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province.
At that time, the victim was about to leave the gas station when a group of suspects got in the car and hid in front of the victim's car, then called the victim to get out of the car and took the material from the victim's pocket. The suspect fled in a car to Kampot provincial town.
(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, on November 19, 2023, laid the groundwork for the construction of a 9-meter-wide and 45-meter-long concrete bridge crossing the Cambodian Buddhist Center on the Angkor Chey River on the border of Dey Commune. Brick and Banteay Dek commune, Kien Svay district.
