(Phnom Penh): At the Fresh Talk last weekend, Lt. Col. Sam Vicheka, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, confirmed that the current crackdown on gangs in Phnom Penh is equally serious. And there are no two standards.
Such a statement is in response to the views of some individuals who say that the law enforcement authorities crack down on gangsters by the children of ordinary people or the little ones do not dare to apply to the children of adults.
Measures to prevent and crack down on gangsters are one of the three priority tasks set by Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner General and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, after he took office three months ago.
Lt. Col. Sam Vichheka further stated that the crackdown on gangsters must be carried out very strictly against any child who endangers society and there is no opening for intervention or mediation, and if the gangster is the son of a high official In addition, the law must be enforced as a model.
Please watch and listen to the remarks of the spokesperson of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police:
(Phnom Penh): In the past three months, the Phnom Penh Municipal Police has cracked down on 244 gangsters, including 233 gangsters who have been sent to court. This was confirmed by Lieutenant Colonel Sam Vicheka, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police during the Fresh Talk last weekend.
According to Lt. Col. Sam Vichheka, the gangsters who were charged in this case were the ones who committed the most serious crimes. However, during the same period, 235 gangsters, equivalent to 85 cases, were educated and contracted to return home.
Measures to crack down on gangsters are one of the three priority tasks set by Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner General and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, after taking office three months ago.
Dr. Koy Pisey: Wat Chanbach Choatnaram, also known as Wat Ta Sot, will soon become a cultural and religious tourism pagoda.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Koy Pisey, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister in charge of Border Affairs and Tourism, said that Wat Chanbach Choatnaram, also known as Wat Ta Sot, located in Pat Lang Village, Kraing Leav Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, will become a cultural and religious tourism pagoda. The near future.
The suffix collected above is a contribution to build this pagoda to become a model pagoda for tourism, culture and religion in Kampong Chhnang province as well as in Cambodia as a whole in the style of the glorious past. The future of this pagoda will not only serve the field of religion and culture, but also an attractive place for local and international tourists, good religion in the region and the world.
She added that, in fact, at Wat Chanbachot Naram, where Preah Dhammavanavasi Chanmony, the Chief Inspector, lived, a large number of Buddhists came to worship every day because he had received a clear, healthy mental health. Reduce stress, better understand sin and feast.
