This morning, Samdech Thipdey Hun Manet announced the implementation of priority political programs related to agriculture
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, November 20, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, announced the official launch of three more political programs. Involved in agriculture.
The three political programs are: 1) a policy program to promote agricultural production, market and balance agricultural prices through financing programs, 2) a policy program for the deployment of agricultural officials in communes, and 3) a policy program. Development of modern agricultural communities.
Agriculture is a core sector deeply rooted in the traditions, customs and culture of Cambodian society. To date, the agricultural sector has liberated the Cambodian people from famine and ensured food security in the harsh conditions of the 19-Kovid Crisis, as well as maintained a surplus of rice (more than required) for nearly 30 years.
However, the Royal Government of the 7th legislature, led by His Majesty the King Hun Manet, still identifies agriculture as a political priority that must be taken care of and implemented well. Among the priority policies to be implemented in 2023 are two policies related to the agricultural sector.
According to the report of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the three political programs are as follows: 1) The policy program to promote agricultural production, find markets and keep agricultural prices stable through financing programs:
The policy program to promote agricultural production, find markets and balance agricultural prices through financing programs is an important national program to stabilize agricultural prices and help the economy and livelihoods of farmers and food security.
The political program will set out a specific budget, starting at $ 100 million, and will allocate more if needed.
The Ministry stated that in order to implement this policy program successfully, it requires the participation of professional institutions and stakeholders. In addition, a number of policies need to be implemented in coordination with other policies, such as the deployment of agricultural officials in communes and policies for the development of modern agricultural communities and development projects to participate in the construction of market-linked production chains.
2) Policy program for deployment of agricultural officials in communes:
The policy program on the deployment of agricultural officials in communes is another effort by the Royal Government to bring services closer to local people in all rural communes across the country to help farmers' families improve. Agricultural productivity and income.
In Cambodia, there are 1,550 communes with agricultural activities. Most of the communes are rich in rice production (1,000 communes) and there are about 2 million farming families. In order for farmers in all communes to receive agricultural services, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries plans to deploy 1,600 commune / sangkat agriculture officials across the country.
Under the guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, when Samdech was the Prime Minister, in early 2023, the Ministry tried to deploy 10 Commune / Sangkat Agriculture Officers in 10 communes in Cheung Prey District, Kampong Cham Province.
To expedite agricultural services to farmers, Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet instructed the Ministry to deploy 250 Commune / Sangkat Agriculture Officers by 2023 and 800 by 2024 and 550 by 2025.
3) Modern Agricultural Community Development Policy Program:
The Modern Agricultural Community Development Policy Program is a vision for the implementation of large-scale joint agricultural production in the agricultural sector as part of the Sixth Priority Policy Program of the Royal Government of the Seventh Legislature of the National Assembly.
This policy program aims to transform Cambodia's agricultural sector from a family to a strong, highly integrated agricultural economy, a scale economy and competitive in both quantity and quality.
The policy program is expected to improve the living standards of farmers as well as increase the efficiency of fraternal, environmental and sustainable production.
It should be noted that in this 7th legislature, in addition to the introduction of the Pentagon Strategy - the first phase, which is the core policy, the Royal Government led by Samdech Moha Bovat Hun Sen has also launched six priority political programs to respond immediately. And people's livelihood problems.
