SEOUL, Nov. 20 (Xinhua) - North Korea on Monday condemned a US missile sale plan to Japan and South Korea, calling it a dangerous move that could escalate tensions in the region and lead to tensions. Run an arms race. This is according to a release by Reuters.
In a statement released by the state-run KCNA media, the North Korean Defense Ministry said that Pyongyang will strengthen measures to establish a deterrent and respond to instability in the region allegedly caused by the United States and Russia. America's ally.
North Korea's reaction comes after news that Japan plans to buy 400 Tomahawk missiles from the United States as part of its largest military build-up since World War II. The Pentagon also said on Friday that the State Department had approved the $ 2.35 billion deal.
