Key Remarks by Samdech Mani Hun Manet, Opportunity to Announce the Implementation of Priority Political Programs Related to Agriculture
The following are the main contents of Samdech Mani President Hun Manet's opportunity to announce the implementation of priority political programs related to the agricultural sector:
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that he was pleased to announce the implementation of the Royal Government's 5th and 6th priority political programs related to agriculture.
* Samdech Thipdey Hun Manet thanked Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Agriculture and related parties, for their joint efforts to implement the Royal Government's priority policies related to the agricultural sector with the implementation of the Royal Government less than 90.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for initiating political programs related to agriculture.
* President Hun Manet stated that while many countries were facing food crises during the 19 epidemic of Kovid and the crisis of the Russia-Ukraine war, Cambodia was able to ensure food security.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that this result was obtained due to the right policy, peace and favorable nature.
* President Hun Manet stated that during the global crisis, people can suspend travel but can not stop eating.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that agricultural technology needs to be constantly updated to increase production.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that sellers want prices, buyers want cheap. Based on this, the Royal Government has always considered to maintain a price that can be obtained by all.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet thanked the National Committee for Disaster Management for its efforts to help farmers affected by the floods in the past.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet said that he asked the business people in the agricultural sector not to compete with each other until they lose the ability with outsiders.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that a scale economy is essential to ensure competitiveness.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the unification of farmers' communities is very important to increase production and launch interventions.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet recommends using proactive farmers' interventions rather than reactions.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet supports the consolidation of agricultural communities and modernization.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet advises stakeholders to promote agricultural products on the digital market.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government's intervention measures as well as the provision of agricultural loans should not affect the competitive spirit of the free market.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet instructed the Ministry of Agriculture to take measures to eliminate all activities that cause fair loss of competition.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet advised to consider connecting the production and supply chain.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that if we just bring the finished product to them and bring back the finished product, then we need to strengthen the quality of the finished product that Cambodia has to supply factories that need raw materials such as rubber.
* President Hun Manet stated that agriculture is not important in terms of quantity, but in terms of income.
Samdech Hun Sen called on the Cambodian people to support Cambodian agriculture.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the technical officers who are selected to help farmers must select those who actually help, not just take the exam and leave it.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet calls on young people who compete to be technical officers to help farmers to work with their hearts.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that we advise farmers to unite as a community, but sometimes the relevant ministries do not cooperate.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that Samdech will check the structure in ministries and state institutions to avoid the implementation of duplication of duties.
Reuters reports, citing a plantation manager with a large rubber processing plant in Thailand, who declined to be named: "Rubber prices have not kept pace with rising costs, making it difficult for farmers to make a profit."
The rubber industry is in the peak harvest season from September to December and is the export season when companies buy stockpiled rubber to prepare for supply in the first half of each year.
"There are also structural problems as some farmers, especially small farmers, are moving to other, more profitable crops, such as durian and palm oil," she told Reuters.
The same manager told Reuters that there was a significant decrease in the standard of care for rubber crops, with farmers using less fertilizer to reduce costs, leading to lower rubber production.
