The King returns to Cambodia after a week-long visit to France
(Phnom Penh): On the night of Sunday, November 19, 2023, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, pays homage to His Holiness the King. The Highman has returned to Cambodia after a week-long royal visit to France.
After arriving in Paris, France on the afternoon of November 13, 2023, the King of Cambodia met with French President Emmanuel Macron at the Elysee Palace.
During the Royal Meeting, His Majesty the King of Life preserved the fruitful meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister of Cambodia and the President of France in December 2022. His Majesty the King expressed his deep gratitude for all the assistance provided by the French Government for the economic and social development of Cambodia. The aid shows France's concern for Cambodia.
His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej also expressed high expectations for (1) the study, renovation and expansion of the National Museum by French experts, (2) the cooperation between the National Museum and the Guimet Museum and (3) Renovation of bronze statues of Vishnu, as well as exhibitions of Khmer artifacts in France and museums.
The French President reaffirmed the commitment of the French Government to continue to assist the sectors, especially the health sector in Cambodia, through human resource training, support for animal-to-human disease prevention programs, and remote surgery. Chirurgie) and the use of artificial intelligence in this field.
The French president reaffirmed the French government's commitment to helping the cultural sector, especially the restoration and expansion of the National Museum and the restoration of the bronze statue of Vishnu to be displayed in France with a number of artifacts.
The President considered the success of the intergovernmental mechanism on the preservation of the historical site of Angkor as a model of multilateralism.
Knowing that Cambodia is willing to host a major Francophone event, the French President encouraged Cambodia to host the Francophone Summit in 2026 and pledged that France would support Cambodia's candidacy.
His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej said that Cambodia was very proud to run for the Francophonie Summit in 2026, and that he knew that France's support was invaluable because it would reflect its will. To strengthen France's important presence in Asia.
During the hearing, the President of France will invite His Majesty the King to attend the 19th Francophone Summit in Paris on October 4-5, 2024. His Majesty the King also invited the President of France and his Excellency to attend the 20th Francophone Summit in 2026 in Cambodia. The President expressed his pleasure to participate.
On November 15, 2023, His Majesty the King of Life attended the 4th Intergovernmental Conference on the Conservation of the Angkor Historic Site at the UNESCO headquarters in Paris.
In response, Ms. Audrey Azulay supported His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej's proposals and pledged to further strengthen cooperation in various fields, which is the capacity and obligation of UNESCO to promote the values of humanitarian heritage preservation. Local communities balance tourism flows through intelligent management, as well as maintaining the sacred value of Angkor temples and other heritage sites.
His Majesty the King also welcomed the decision of the Prime Minister, who expressed his strong will to prioritize education and vocational training in the Royal Government's action plan and called on To UNESCO to contribute to the development of new training programs.
The Conference also thanked all stakeholders for their joint efforts in protecting and conserving the World Heritage Site of Angkor Sambath. The conference also made a strong commitment to maintain the Angkor site as well as the Sambor Prei Kuk temple to last forever.
During this valuable mission in Paris, France, His Majesty the King of Cambodia also granted His Majesty the permission to allow Mr. Komura Masahiro, Deputy Minister for Foreign Affairs of Japan and his colleagues to pay homage.
His Majesty the King would like to express his deep gratitude to Japan for its active role as the Co-Chair of the ICC Angkor in the restoration of temples at the Angkor Historical Resort.
