China vows to support real estate and tackle local administration debt (Video inside) (Beijing) - China's central bank and financial regulator on Friday pledged to provide financial support for the real estate sector and work together to tackle risks. Local government debt. According to Reuters.
China's leaders are trying to revive the economy and curb the potential financial risks from a 92 trillion yuan ($ 12.77 trillion) loss of local government real estate and debt.
Following a meeting between the central bank and the financial regulator, the China Securities Regulatory Commission said on Friday that financial institutions will respond to the reasonable financing needs of real estate developers.
The Securities and Exchange Commission of China said recent efforts to maintain financial stability for the real estate sector through bank loans, bonds and equity securities are gaining traction.
The regulator added that China will promote steady credit expansion to support its economic growth, and financial institutions should work with local governments to address debt risk through credit expansion or credit restructuring. According to Reuters.
