(Phnom Penh): Four Cambodian companies have set out to find more cashew export markets in the United States, expecting Cambodian cashew nuts to enter the US market soon, especially next year's harvest. Starting from February to May to increase Cambodia's exports of processed cashew nuts.
He said that during the search for the cashew import market in the United States, the four Cambodian cashew processing companies showcased Cambodian cashew products to American cashew buyers, importers and retailers.
He added that the search for cashew market in the United States seems to be very positive, with some companies getting the green light to order.
However, he said that importing cashew nuts to the US market is not easy, requiring more study on import procedures and market prices.
He added: "The company he received the order from, he is studying in detail, because when we came to the United States, we learned a lot about the market price of cashews in the United States, the type of cashew nuts placed in the United States and study. About cashew import system and so on.
He said that the buyers were required to produce Cambodian cashews in accordance with the standard, the price must be competitive and large quantities, because the United States is a big market, so in terms of volume can be imported is very important. If a company does not have enough supply, they do not order.
"The federation, in coordination with the four companies that came to the exhibition, how to work together to achieve the three factors: to produce the right standard, sufficient quantity, demand and a competitive price," he said. "We want to work together to bring cashew nuts to the US market."
In addition to exhibiting Cambodian cashew products to buyers in the United States, Cambodian cashew producers and processors also visited five major markets where cashew products are sold in the United States.
"Overall, over the past few days, each company has been in contact with about 10 to 15 partner companies to discuss and promote processed cashew products to US buyers," he said.
He hopes that Cambodian processed cashews will be imported to the US market in the future, as Cambodian cashew nut producers and processors have met directly with real buyers and collaborated with consulting companies to encourage Cambodian companies to import cashew nuts. The United States will miss, especially in the upcoming harvest season, from February to May 2024.
