Photo by AFP Phos Sovann: Media plays an important role in educating and mainstreaming Cambodian-Chinese culture
The landmark meeting brought together 65 representatives from 18 political parties and 23 media representatives from 16 countries around the world to exchange knowledge and ideas on aspects of media cooperation in Asia. The forum is an important platform for political parties and local media to work together to enhance and strengthen ties to achieve ICAPP goals in building an Asian community of peace, stability and prosperity.
Fresh News is the only news outlet from Cambodia to be invited to this important forum, among 23 other media outlets from about 15 countries, including Azerbaijan, Bangladesh, Indonesia, Kazakhstan, Mongolia, Myanmar, Nepal, Pakistan, the Republic of Korea and Russia. Sri Lanka, Thailand, Turkey and Vietnam gathered in Seoul for the forum.
The International Conference of Asian Political Parties (ICAPP) was established in Manila, Philippines in September 2000 to promote exchanges and cooperation among ideological political parties in Asia and Oceania. The ICAPP aims to strengthen mutual understanding and increase regional trust and promote peace and prosperity through the unique role and network of political parties.
The ICAPP Media Forum was established in September 2015 with the aim of promoting cooperation between political parties and the media to jointly build a peaceful and prosperous community in Asia. In addition, recognizing the role of the press as a catalyst for change and cooperation among nations in the region through media outreach, this forum will contribute to raising awareness between the people and the people of the country. Be a member.
