"The first coffee has increased to 2,200 riel per kilogram, the second coffee is 1,800 riel per kilogram, and the third coffee is 1,500 riel per kilogram. According to Mr. Mam Makara, head of the coffee roasting enterprise of Coffee Company, which collects this type of coffee directly.
The director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture continued, "The factors that increase the price of fresh coffee or raw coffee beans are due to the cooperation between the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Mondulkiri Province with Coffee Company for two years to Collect fresh coffee at high prices in the market.
Not only that, maintaining the market value of fresh coffee or raw coffee products has contributed to improving the lives of farmers better and more resilient and can strengthen the cultivation to ensure the right supply chain to the standard and sustainability. .
