Mr. Khuong Sreng stated that we all have the opportunity to gather for the festival now because we have peace throughout the country under the win-win policy of the founder of peace, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and continue to the pentagonal policy of the seventh mandate. The Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet is the Prime Minister.
This Kathina Festival is also a contribution to the promotion of Buddhism, the state religion, to be more prosperous and long-lasting. On the other hand, it also shows the gathering of Buddhists near and far with transparency and increase the solidarity between the people and the authorities to contribute to the development of Phnom Penh.
The money raised from this donation was $ 157,284 to be donated to the monks in Puth Seima, Wat Prasidhirimaram to continue the construction of temples and achievements in this temple. Apart from this, the above suffix also has a suffix of 400,000 Riels, given to the Chief Bishop of Wat Sutra, 300,000 Riels to 22 monks, 200,000 Riels to each monk.
(Hong Kong) - Alibaba Group Hong Kong shares fell 10 percent on Friday after the company scrapped plans to cut off its cloud computing business from its parent company, citing uncertainty over export bans. US chip to China. According to Reuters.
The stock price drop, which could be the biggest one-day drop in more than a year, cost Alibaba about $ 20 billion.
The drop was the first market reaction in Asia since the Chinese tech giant announced a surprise strategic shift on Thursday evening. The company's U.S.-listed shares fell 9 percent at the close of trading on Friday evening.
Alibaba, once Asia's largest market capitalization, was worth about $ 830 billion in October 2020, but is now worth less than a quarter as the e-commerce company is in the throes of a technology crackdown. Of Beijing and while China's economy is slowing. According to Reuters.
