(Phnom Penh): Currently, the world is being severely affected by war or armed conflict or violence that occurs in many places and is difficult to resolve.
These hot and dangerous issues are rooted in extremist ideologies, sometimes embedded in politics and sometimes in religion. Its negative consequences are increasingly affecting the entire world.
Look at Cambodia, the hard-earned peace is being deeply rooted throughout the country under the protection and care of the leaders from the time of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the time of Samdech Manet.
Religious harmony also prevailed throughout the country, making Cambodia an admirable country and a model of peaceful coexistence between religious communities, even though Buddhism is considered the state religion. Cambodia is open to other religious beliefs. Religious harmony does not come by chance, but it comes from the leaders' ingenuity in uniting people of all religions to live together in peace.
On the political front, extremist ideology is fading and disappearing under the influence of national unity to maintain peace and social stability.
The Cambodian people, who are benefiting from the peace and religious peace on their territory, fully support the direction of eliminating extremist politics in Cambodia set by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and are continuing to be implemented by Samdech Hun Sen.
All in all, Cambodia, as well as the Cambodian people, are fortunate to be able to live in peace and religious purity, as these two sacred objects can avoid war, armed conflict and violence, and maintain stability. Socio-political and economic as the foundation of development. Therefore, peace and religious harmony are the lucky assets of Cambodia that all Cambodians must take care to prevent from being lost.
