(Phnom Penh): Prof. Chheang Ra, Minister of Health, on November 17, 2023, met with the working group of the General Secretariat of the National Council for Social Protection led by Dr. John Narith, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Economy and Finance and Secretary General. National Council for Social Protection at the Ministry.
The Minister warmly welcomed the delegation of the General Secretariat of the National Council for Social Protection to pay a courtesy call and report on the progress and direction of the social protection system in Cambodia.
Dr. John Narith presented the progress of the implementation of the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016 to 2025, which is a basic document and guide for the development of the current Cambodian social protection system based on a lifelong and focused social protection approach. On the two pillars are the social assistance system and the social security system.
He added that the Royal Government is currently implementing the National Social Assistance Program and the Social Security System in various social protection systems, including: the Health Equity Fund, the Social Security System, the Health Care System, and the Cash Support Program for pregnant women and children under the age of 18. 2 years, which has been implemented since June 1, 2019.
He also encouraged the relevant parties of the Ministry of Health to continue to cooperate more deeply with the General Secretariat of the National Council for Social Protection in the implementation of the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025 and the implementation of the nine health strategies. To link this work with the three key health sector priorities, including:
1: Strengthen the capacity of health centers through the supply of medical equipment, essential medicines, infrastructure, strengthen the capacity of health workers to ensure the provision of health services to people 24 hours a day
