According to the Royal Ceremony of the Golden Gate, published by the Buddhist Institute, Buddhists perform the Kathin ceremony in the belief in the Buddhist scriptures that the Kathina is more auspicious than all other alms. According to the Buddhist precepts, monks who can receive the Kathina mat only if they have waited for the rainy season for three months in abundance, without any obligation to enter the rainy season, can not receive the Kathina from the Buddhist monks.
The pure generosity of the Buddhists that arises from the Kathina and to dedicate merits to the souls of ancestors, parents, grandparents, relatives of the seven clans and to dedicate the souls of warriors who sacrificed their lives for the cause of the motherland.
The suffix collected from this Kathina to give to the monks in Puth Seima, Wat Prasidhi Rimaram to continue to build temples and achievements in Buddhism forever.
