The Executive Director of the Wildlife Alliance believes that the environmental chakra strategy will contribute to the restoration of the big tiger or leopard in the Cambodian natural forest.
Answering a question from a Fresh News reporter at a press conference on the evening of November 16, 2023, Dr. Suvanna Gonlet expressed her confidence: "This chakra strategy has really contributed to the planning. "Restore this big tiger because one of them is to protect the forest."
According to Sou Vanna, the big tigers planned to be brought to Cambodia next year are one male and three females. The Tiger Conservation Project is a joint project between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of India, based on the recent signing of a memorandum of understanding between the two countries to make historic strides for tiger conservation. Large.
The Environmental Chakra Strategy 2023-2028 is designed to turn the potential of the environmental sector into real benefits for the nation and the people of Cambodia of all generations. This strategy focuses on three major forces: first: policy, second: digital administration, and third: outreach, which is the driving force behind Cambodia's vision to achieve Cambodia's vision of 2050: clean, green and sustainable. Sustainability.
Dr. Sou Vanna added that the documents requesting and transporting the big tiger from India to Cambodia have already been prepared and sent to the Indian government, waiting for the Indian side to send. These four big tigers will be released in the core area of the Cardamom Mountains, which is protected and considered the safest way to rehabilitate big tigers in Cambodia.
Please note that this project to restore the big tiger after disappearing from the territory of Cambodia in 2007 by hunting for trade in bones and skins. Its presence has been found in areas such as northeast, southwest and northern Cambodia.
