Clean Energy Week 2023 officially launches with support to achieve common goals of increasing renewable energy and solar energy to increase Cambodia's energy security
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 16, 2023, Cambodia, Australia, New Zealand and the United Nations Development Program (UNDP) officially launched the Cambodia Clean Energy Week 2023 program with a call for facilitation activities on the clean energy transition from All stakeholders to jointly achieve the common goal of increasing renewable energy and solar energy to increase Cambodia's energy security.
The official launch of Clean Energy Week 2023 was attended by Mr. Kan Pharith, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Mr. Pov Maly, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, and His Excellency Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
Also present were Ambassador Justin Wyatt, Australian Ambassador to Cambodia, Allen First Secretary for Development of the New Zealand Ambassadors to Cambodia, Laos and Thailand; Cambodia and Mr. Nattarun Ngor Son, Country Director of Energy Leap.
"Cambodia's clean energy transition is an opportunity to respond to climate change and support sustainable and sustainable economic growth," said Ambassador Justin White. "Australia is committed to supporting this change, including sharing experiences in integrating renewable energy to help Cambodia achieve the expected results."
Alissar Chaker, Representative of the United Nations Development Program in Cambodia, said that adopting clean energy is not an ideological position, but an economic development opportunity for Cambodia to increase energy security, create dividends, trade and access to finance. Objects will increase resilience and environment.
She added that in the last three years, UNDP has supported key regulations such as the introduction of solar energy on roofs and energy efficiency in buildings, and connected electricity to villages that are not connected to the state grid. 21 with a small solar grid, providing access to remote communities and areas in need.
Please be informed that the program also discusses key priorities for Cambodia's clean energy transition, with keynote speakers from the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the World Bank, the Cambodia-Australia Partnership for Sustainable Economic Development (CAPRED) program. ) And Empacte. The General Department of Taxation reminds for the second time that the payment of transportation tax for 2023, which expires at the end of this month
