(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia Stock Exchange Fair is being held for the sixth time for four days from November 16 to 19, 2023 at Aeon Mall Phnom Penh to promote the securities sector in Cambodia.
The 6th Cambodia Stock Exchange Expo was presided over by Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, with the participation of Mr. Sou Socheat, Royal Government Delegate. Director of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia Mr. Hong Sohour, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Securities Exchange of Cambodia.
The Cambodia Stock Exchange 2023 is organized for the following main purposes:
1. Promote the securities sector in Cambodia through the dissemination and dissemination of awareness to the public, especially potential investors, both national and international investors, to know and understand more about the Cambodia Securities Exchange, as well as the many benefits of this market.
2. Provide opportunities for investors and the public to learn more about the securities sector in Cambodia through face-to-face meetings with regulators, operators, securities firms, issuers and other stakeholders.
4. Launched a special promotion package for new investors by promoting trading account opening by providing the public with free investor ID and trading account, 50% commission discount until the end of 2023 and Play various games to get cash prizes or shares deposited into the investment account after the investor submits and receives the account immediately.
Mr. Hong Sohour said in this exhibition that in line with the vision of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Cambodia Securities Exchange has reached a new generation, the third generation of the Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX 3.0) by opening an online trading account with an account. Trading immediately after the securities agent has verified the information.
He pointed out that before the official launch of the second generation of online trading account opening system, investors need to spend several days and complete several procedures to obtain an investor identification number and trading account. This has hindered the development of the securities market in Cambodia.
At the same time, Mr. Sou Socheat emphasized that the stock market is another important investment channel that provides opportunities for Cambodians to invest with little capital, but can expand its investment package to increase additional passive income with confidence. Trust.
"Therefore, we should learn and start investing from today, but must use the savings to invest, avoid using the daily budget to invest."
"Currently, the number of listed companies and trading is not very active, but the development of this market is moving forward vigorously through the continuous development of new products and services," he said. Promotion and training that has been applied to public investors.
He is optimistic that through the efforts of all stakeholders in the securities sector to attract publishers and investors, the development of investment products and the establishment of mechanisms to facilitate the trading process, the Cambodia Securities Exchange will find factors. New tips to drive stronger and more sustainable growth. Heng Sour urges EuroCham to help attract European companies to Cambodia
