(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Authority, representing Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Mine Authority, has confirmed that Cambodia will chair the 2024 Ottawa Convention and host the Siem Reap Summit. Angkor on a landmine-free world by the end of 2024.
In a press conference on the morning of November 16, 023, Senior Minister Ly Thuch said that for this meeting will be represented by nearly 200 countries around the world through the meeting in Siem Reap is also to attract tourists. Visit Cambodia's Angkor Wat temples.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch stated that on the occasion of chairing the Ottawa Convention and hosting the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit on a Mine-Free World, Cambodia, a country affected by anti-personnel landmines, will share special experiences. Positive points that Cambodia has made in the past, such as win-win politics, bring peace to Cambodia as well as resolve the issue of landmines in Cambodia.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch added: "Through this meeting, Cambodia will tell the world that Cambodia is smiling again, reviving and living in peace, living in peace after the decades-long war that is seen in Cambodia. "Red, see blood, see misery, see hunger, Cambodia will tell them that Cambodia is a land of smiles, a land of hope."
At the same time, Senior Minister Ly Thuch also mentioned why Cambodia became the chair of the Ottawa Convention due to many factors and especially that Cambodia has survived the war and is a peaceful country. He added that Cambodia is a country that has been very successful in eliminating war.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch said that Cambodia was the first country in Asia to chair the Ottawa Convention. Acceptance of the hammer as chair of the Ottawa Convention after Switzerland.
Please note that Cambodia has been a party to the Ottawa Convention since 2000. As a State Party, Cambodia has paid close attention to the mine sector and has been fulfilling its obligations and receiving high evaluation from all States Parties. After the meeting, Biden still considered Xi Jinping a dictator.
