(Phnom Penh): In a meeting with Ms. Seng Sopheap, Director of FHI 360 in Cambodia, Prof. Lim Dara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, encouraged FHI 360 to explore additional possibilities to contribute to achieving global health coverage.
The Secretary of State also conveyed the Minister's greetings and greetings to the International Family Health Organization, thanking FHI 360 for supporting the Ministry of Health in developing the health care system in Cambodia.
In particular, participate in the achievement of many achievements of the project to improve the quality and equity of health in Cambodia, the improvement of protocols to improve the quality of national health programs.
She said FHI 360 has a primary mission to improve the equity, health and well-being of humanity through the use of data and the search for fundamental solutions. FHI 360 in Cambodia was launched in 1998 and is currently implementing and providing technical assistance on five health-focused action plans, including:
1: Increase health education activities for the people in order to improve the health of the people
2: Fight infectious diseases
3: Prevent the spread of global infectious diseases, a public health problem
4: Prevent non-communicable diseases that affect public health while socio-economic development
5: Prevent and prevent diseases caused by the effects of climate change
6: Improve the examination and treatment of diseases in the community
7: Regulation of public and private service workers to improve health care services
8: Development of human resources, especially health skills
As well as the three health priorities are * Strengthening the capacity of health centers through the supply of medical equipment, essential medicines, infrastructure, strengthening the capacity of health workers to ensure the provision of health services to people 24 hours a day.
Strengthen the capacity of Referral Hospitals, ODs and Provinces by strengthening the capacity of emergency rooms, operating rooms, laboratories and referral systems.
