This morning, Samdech Hun Sen presided over the inauguration of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport.
(Siem Reap): Siem Reap Angkor International Airport (SAI) worth about 1.1 billion US dollars was officially inaugurated on the morning of Thursday, November 16, 2023. And. The ceremony will be presided over by His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The presence of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport is another great achievement in Siem Reap, a potential economic pole of Cambodia's tourism industry. Siem Reap Angkor International Airport has become an important air link between Siem Reap and other areas in Cambodia, as well as other potential tourism destinations.
Siem Reap Angkor International Airport is also an achievement born of the policy of steel ties and Cambodia-China diamond cooperation under the framework of the Belt and Road Initiative (BRI) and the initiative of the Cambodian-Chinese government leaders.
Siem Reap Angkor International Airport is located in Ta Pek Commune, Sot Nikum District and Kork Thlok Leu Commune, Chi Kreng District, Siem Reap Province, more than 40 km from Angkor Resort and more than 50 km from Siem Reap town.
The construction of the airport officially started in March 2020 and will be completed by the end of March 2023 in a period of 36 months equal to 3 years. The construction of this international airport employs between 2,500 and 3,700 workers, including 70% of Cambodian engineers and 30% of Chinese workers, depending on the actual workload.
At present, there are only 903 employees, engineers and workers of those related contractors, of which 346 are Cambodian engineers and 557 are Chinese workers.
