(Phnom Penh): The Fisheries Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries said that on November 15, 2023, a 7-year-old male dolphin, 1.94 meters long and 65 kilograms, died at Koh Chim village, O'Mreas commune, Siem Bok district, Stung Treng province.
An autopsy by the Fisheries Administration and WWF concluded that the dolphin had died of electric shock from bruises on its head and body.
In 2023, eight dolphins were born and five died, including two baby dolphins, two adolescents and one elderly.
In this regard, the Fisheries Administration will cooperate with the relevant authorities to carry out operations to crack down on this shock crime and severely punish the perpetrators in accordance with the law on fisheries.
The Fisheries Administration calls on fishermen and local people to provide information to the authorities when they see people using fishing tackle. The Fisheries Administration will provide incentives. Information telephone number: 097 666 4999/011 355 883/088 8355 883/012 897 943.
