(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment, together with relevant organizations, on the afternoon of November 14, 2023, officially announced the launch of the "Environmental Chakra Strategy 2023-2028" and the "Blue Sky Campaign and Zero Greenhouse Gas Emissions" campaign. 2025 in Cambodia.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, together with partner organizations working in the field of environment at the Ministry of Environment.
The Environmental Chakra Strategy 2023-2028 is designed to turn the potential of the environmental sector into real benefits for the nation and the people of Cambodia of all generations. The environmental chakra strategy focuses on three major forces: first: policy, second: digital administration, and third: outreach, which is the driving force behind Cambodia's ships towards achieving Cambodia's vision of 2050: clean, green. And sustainability.
The Environmental Chakra Strategy 2023-2028 will be used as a roadmap to implement the priority goals, provide public services to meet the needs of the public and turn the potential of the environmental sector into the best interests of all generations of Cambodians and contribute. Responding to global climate change.
The Blue Sky Campaign and Zero Emissions 2050 is a forum that helps stakeholders engage with government agencies to achieve zero emissions targets by 2050 by raising awareness of climate action. Which creates a blue sky and zero emissions. The campaign will also help provide practical solutions through partnerships between governments, local communities and other key stakeholders.
In addition, this campaign wants to highlight new and good practices that are possible, rather than following the old path (repetitive methods) that lead to air pollution.
