Minister of Information: Institutional Strengthening, Staff Capacity Building and Motivation at the Key of Public Administration Reform Process
(Phnom Penh): On November 14, 2023, Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, stated that institutional strengthening, capacity building of officers and motivation are the key points of the public administration reform process and for this reform. The Ministry of Information is involved in three areas, including public administration reform, public financial management, and decentralization and deconcentration reforms.
This statement made by the Minister during the opening ceremony of the seminar on the orientation of public administration reform on the morning of November 14, 2023 at the Ministry of Information.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra highlighted the importance of this workshop related to the process of public administration reform, a task that the Royal Government of Cambodia has made a priority in managing and leading the country in the seventh mandate.
The Minister stated that for the seventh mandate, Samdech Hun Sen emphasized that 2024 is the year that we have to apply the brakes, which means that all ministries and institutions must evaluate what their ministries and institutions have and prepare a plan. Be clear before moving on.
Meanwhile, the Royal Government of the seventh mandate also focused on six main priorities, including:
The Minister stated that for the public function is a priority in the process of institutional reform, and the management of an institution must focus on three points, including:
* First: Focus on leadership means that from the top to the bottom it is necessary to have leadership * Second: clear work structure means that we know the roles and division of roles and responsibilities. Clear * Third: Human resources, these three points lead to strong leadership.
The Minister also informed that for the Royal Government of the 7th mandate until today, it is 82 days, and in the following period, the ministries and institutions as well as the Prime Minister always hold many meetings to put down Policies, action plans for the better operation of the new government and further.
Mr. Neth Pheakdra also stated that the Prime Minister has given one year to the ministries and institutions to reform the public administration, which has three main points: institutional strengthening, capacity building of officials and incentives.
He highlighted the important points that the Ministry of Information needs to do from now on is to train and strengthen human resources to be strong by mobilizing officers to work together, including to reorganize human resources to quality and Ability to perform tasks effectively.
Mr. Neth Pheakdra emphasized that the strengthening of capacity and institutional capacity is to improve the quality of work with discipline, professional ethics, efficiency and effectiveness, and the implementation of the system to support the achievement of unity, equity, efficiency, especially what is important. Unite, unite, unite, unite.
The Secretary of State further stated that the reform of public administration is to harmonize the drafting of legal documents, the preparation and implementation of legal instruments, raise awareness and improve the effectiveness of the implementation of legal documents, as well as Provide a fair or equitable solution to disputes or complaints related to jurisdiction within the framework of the Ministry of Information, which is a priority.
