Ancient cities and thousands of homes flooded in central Vietnam
Hue, an ancient city in Vietnam and a popular World Heritage site for tourists, was submerged on Wednesday after heavy rains in central Vietnam flooded homes. Thousands of backs and highways cut off. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, November 15, 2023.
Pictures from local Vietnamese media showed Vietnamese people traveling by boat on flooded roads as houses and cars were flooded. Residents in Hue claim that the ancient city was flooded almost everywhere and that power was cut off. It has been raining heavily in some provinces in central Vietnam since Monday.
It should be noted that Vietnam always suffers from bad weather conditions during the rainy season between June and November every year. Rainfall is forecast to remain high for about two days before improving over the weekend. Natural disasters, including floods and landslides, have left 136 people dead or missing in Vietnam this year, according to official figures.
