Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presents Additional Recommendations to the General Assembly of the United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia to Achieve Success in the New Phase (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Seven Additional Recommendations were issued by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party The 6th General Assembly of the United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia on the morning of November 15, 2023 to achieve more new achievements in this new phase.
The recommendations made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen so that all levels of the Front should pay attention to implementing the decisions of the General Assembly today into practical actions include:
* First, continue to work with the Royal Government to maintain peace, political stability, security, social order and absolute protection of independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity.
* Second, the Front at all levels must strengthen and expand the Front Organizational Structure, increase the capacity to manage and lead the work, seek more sources of support to ensure the sustainability and progress of the Front's mission, structure and cause.
* Third: The Front at all levels must continue to educate and inspire the movement to mainstream awareness of the policies of the Royal Government to be widespread in society and to mobilize the masses from all walks of life to support and implement the principles and policies. That aims to contribute to the Royal Government of Cambodia to achieve the vision of Cambodia's socio-economic development, especially as a high middle income country by 2030 and a developed country by 2050.
* Fourth: Participate in the resolute struggle to prevent all the tactics and activities of national unity of the opposition groups, both inside and outside the country, which try to persuade the people to oppose the cause of building and developing the beloved homeland of We.
* Fifth: Strengthen and maintain strong internal unity and solidarity in terms of views, positions and political consciousness in accordance with the principle of "keep the old, increase the new."
* Sixth: Participate in the implementation of the policy of diplomacy, peace, independence, friendship and equal cooperation with other countries in the world on the basis of respect for independence, sovereignty, equality and mutual benefit in accordance with the motto of the Royal Government of Cambodia. "Internal reform, build external friends on the basis of independence."
* 7th: The spirit of the 6th General Assembly of the Front must be disseminated more widely to all social circles.
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan has signed a grant to build a new 25-meter-long concrete bridge for the people in O'Mreas commune, Siem Bok district, Stung Treng province, with a budget of 168,276 US dollars.
This assistance was signed by Mr. Taninai Oum Chhitomo, Acting Chargé d'Affaires of the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia, with the Cambodian side consisting of Mr. Prum Chantha, Director of Stung Treng Provincial Department of Rural Development, Mr. Suong Hy, Governor of Siem Bok District and Mr. Soy Kea, Deputy Director. Provincial Department of Rural Development on the afternoon of November 14, 2023 at the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia, Phnom Penh.
This is a grant for a small-scale project, Human Security, to build a new concrete bridge, 25 meters long and 6 meters wide, with a budget of 168,276 US dollars.
The new concrete bridge project is to replace the old wooden bridge, which is rotten, damaged and unsafe due to the large number of trucks passing through, causing landslides, causing many difficulties for local people. In transit to schools, workplaces, hospitals, especially the transportation of agricultural products of the general population.
In an interview with the press, Santo Darmosumarto said that outside Indonesia has promoted many of Indonesia's tourist destinations for Cambodians to get to know Indonesia, Indonesia has also promoted Cambodia to the Indonesian people through social media, showing Cambodia is a peaceful country, the people are friendly, which makes Indonesians want to visit, explore the investment climate and work in Cambodia.
At the same time, he encouraged Cambodians to visit Indonesia, especially the sexy island of Sumatra, because the geographical location of this island is beautiful and multicultural. As for the local food, it tastes good and is easy for Cambodians to eat.
According to the Indonesian Ambassador to Cambodia, from January to November this year, 2023, about 9,300 Cambodians visited Indonesia and expect to have more than 10,000 by the end of this year. He said that number was still small compared to the pre-199 epidemic, reaching 13,000 and hoped that when the economy improved, the number of visitors to Indonesia would increase to about 30,000.
He added that Indonesian tourists are an important market for Cambodia, contributing about 3% to the tourism market in Cambodia.
The bill, which would allow the US government to run until mid-January next year, has now been submitted to the Senate for approval before being forwarded to President Joe Biden to sign new funding for The federal government, while the old budget will expire at midnight next Friday.
The vote to approve the draft interim budget was held by 336 votes to 95.
The interim budget would allow the US government to pay federal officials until 2024 to allow lawmakers more time to draft detailed spending bills that cover everything from military to research. Science. Image from Reuters Peace concept built by the old, inaugurated by the new! This afternoon, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet inaugurated the Koh Nora Bridge
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Wednesday, November 15, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, will officially inaugurate the Koh Nora Bridge.
The Koh Nora Bridge project has a total length of 824 meters and a total width of 24.5 meters. The length of the bridge is 483 meters, the road connecting the head of the bridge on the side of Koh Pich is 249 meters long, the road connecting the head of the bridge on Koh Nora is 92 meters long 25 meters and has a lane for motorcycles to one and one, with a width of 1.25 meters on each side.
The Koh Nora Bridge was built at a cost of US $ 38 million and was built by the Cambodian Overseas Investment Company (OCIC). The bridge will take 35 months to build from October 26, 2020 to October 20, 2023.
Koh Nora Twin Dragon Bridge has a total length of 60 meters, a length of 43 meters, a total width of 26 meters. The road connecting the end of each bridge is 8.5 meters long.
Koh Nora Bridge, as well as Koh Nora Twin Dragon Bridge, was decided by Samdech Moha Bovathipati Hun Manet to allow people to travel temporarily during Pchum Ben to facilitate traffic.
In particular, the bridge has helped people save time traveling and reduce fuel costs. More importantly, it has contributed to the beauty of Phnom Penh under the shadow of peace.
