(Phnom Penh): Japanese investors in Cambodia in the banking and financial sector have expressed confidence in the leadership of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate, hoping that the Cambodian economy will continue to grow and expressed the will to continue to expand. The size of business ventures in Cambodia will be stronger in the future.
Koizumi Yusuke, Assistant Director General of Active Microfinance Plc., Said that although the Cambodian economy has faced some difficulties in the past due to the Kovid 19 crisis and the global economic crisis, the Royal Government of Cambodia has a clear mechanism to Strengthen its economy so far.
He noted that the banking sector, microfinance institutions also maintain a balance, which gives investors in this sector more confidence to invest. He said this at the banquet to thank the partners and relevant institutions who have always supported Active Microfinance Plc.
He said the company is currently expanding its business and developing products such as car installments, motorcycle installments, electronics installments, agricultural machinery installments, land installments and quick loans to contribute to Promote the financial sector for the better.
At present, the company has a total of 29 branches with 600 employees, the number of customers who have used the services of the company to date is more than 350,000 and the total loan balance is $ 300 million.
