This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Attends the 6th General Assembly of the United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Wednesday, November 3, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and Honorary President of the National Council for Homeland Development Cambodia will attend the 6th General Assembly of the United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia, held at the Sokha Hotel.
The General Assembly is designed to review past work activities and set out plans as well as work goals for further implementation.
The United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia, formerly known as the United Front for the National Salvation of Cambodia, was established on December 2, 1978 and issued its 11b statement in the Snuol Liberation Area, Snuol District, Kratie Province. In 2023, the United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia will be 45 years old.
The Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation was formed by the great unity of the people, both inside and outside the country, including Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Samdech Akka Moha Thamma Pothisal Chea Sim, Samdech Akka Moha Padei Techo Hun Sen and the patriotic hero Chea Many more as leaders.
The Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation was organized on the basis of the pure national independence spirit of the Cambodian people. Country as well.
The Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation was formed in the cause of national liberation, rights, freedoms and lives of the Cambodian people from the Democratic Kampuchea regime of Pol Pot genocide.
Starting from the resistance movement and all kinds of sacrifices, even a brave life, the whole of Cambodia was liberated from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, making the people free from suffering, free from slaughter and return to their rights. Full freedom to live, work and earn a living, and livelihoods are gradually improved from year to year under the umbrella of hard-earned peace.
