(Phnom Penh): The General Assembly of the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia on November 14, 2023 elected General Sar Thet, the National Police Commissioner General, as the President of the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia for the fifth mandate.
At the closing ceremony of the General Assembly, which was presided over by Mr. Abhisandiband Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Honorary President of the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia, General Sar Thet made a solemn declaration and expressed his strong commitment after the election. Chairman for this new mandate.
On behalf of the Chairman of the Central Committee of the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia, General Sar Thet made the following responsible commitments:
* First, strive to pay attention to the proper implementation of the statutes of the Friends of the National Police of Cambodia.
* Second: Direct and direct the Central Committee and all local committees and the Friends of Police Magazine Committee to implement strictly and effectively in accordance with the decision of the General Assembly of the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia now.
* Third: Gather the support of the members of the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia by striving to find resources as well as new measures and methods to develop the Association of Friends of the National Police of Cambodia to be quality and more progressive in order to expand. The ability to support, support and resolve the grievances of the members of the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia to a greater extent.
* Fourth: Organize an extraordinary meeting at an appropriate time to amend the statute, amend the composition of the Central Committee and organize the appropriate organizational structure to strengthen the efficiency of the Association to be more progressive in the future.
As of August 2023, the Friends of the National Police of Cambodia has 78,069 members, of which 6,1897 are police officers, 16,170 are retired police officers and volunteer disabled police officers. Chet continues to be a member of the association of 2 people.
