Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia shares knowledge related to investing in legal investment products and knows about fraudulent investment projects
(Phnom Penh): In order to contribute to raising awareness related to investment, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has prepared an article explaining in detail the investment in legal investment products.
The following is the full text of the article by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia:
When investing, investors tend to focus on high returns and personal awareness, not on risk factors, which are important factors for balancing investments.
Based on past data, risk and profit are directly related. The higher the return on a particular investment, the higher the risk.
Generally, to reduce risk, investments should be made on or above the risk line. In addition, investors should choose legitimate investment products.
When investing, investors should check whether the investment project is properly managed, unmanaged or fraudulent. Under-regulated investment products are generally strictly controlled by local regulators. This makes regulated investment products a safer option compared to other investment products.
In general, regulatory investment products are: - Obtained from regulators, - Managed by a licensed fund management company, - Properly documented and informative, and usually documented. By an audit firm accredited by the regulator. Therefore, the risk of investment projects under regulation as fraudulent projects is very low.
* Update on the market for joint ventures in Cambodia
Looking at the potential of the joint venture market for national economic growth, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia (SECC), the regulatory authority for the management and control of the securities market in Cambodia, has set up the infrastructure to operate this market through Establishing a regulatory framework to regulate this market.
In addition, on July 20, 2023, NCCC Also issued a Prakas on "Fund Issuance of Joint Ventures" to define the conditions, procedures for the issuance of fund units of Joint Ventures and the operation of the Fund after the issuance to ensure Order, accountability and transparency in the market to protect stakeholders, including investors in the market.
* Non-regulatory investment products
* Fraudulent or fraudulent investment projects
There are also reports of land investment projects that have sparked outrage and have been accused of fraud. Some operators have been arrested, charged and prosecuted. These fraudulent real estate investment projects always promise high returns. This indicates a lack of transparency about the way in which funds are invested, including the progress and cash flow of the project.
It is important to note the difference between a legitimate investment project that develops into a bad situation and a fraudulent investment project. Every investment must dare to take risks to make a profit. There are many examples of investments that are legitimate but evolve into a bad situation due to bad market conditions and other reasons.
Scams occur when cash collected from investors is not used to invest in a particular project. Instead, profits are created by using cash from new investors to pay off old ones. These projects are known as Ponzi schemes. All those fraudulent operators are not authorized / licensed by the regulator.
Conclusion To find a legitimate investment, investors should consider the following points: - Is the company controlled by the relevant authorities? - Is the investment product approved by the relevant authorities? - Is the investment worthwhile? Will the promised profit? - Does the investment project include scrutiny and verification by lawyers, auditors and other independent experts?
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan, through the Embassy of Cambodia, has signed a grant of US $ 424,907 to three recipients under the Grants for Small-Scale Human Security Project (Kusano) to rehabilitate irrigation systems. In Oddar Meanchey province, the project to build a bridge in Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province and the project to build a bridge in O'Mreah commune, Siem Bok district, Stung Treng province.
The grant agreement was signed on November 14, 2023 by Mr. Taninai Oum Chhitomo, Acting Chargé d'Affaires of the Embassy of Japan in the Kingdom of Cambodia and representatives of the three recipients.
First: Thnal Dach Irrigation Rehabilitation Project in Oddar Meanchey Province (US $ 119,424) Recipient Institution: Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology.
This assistance will be used to restore existing irrigation systems with impaired reservoir function. This area is vulnerable to drought in the dry season due to the irrigation system not being able to store enough water during the rainy season. In addition, due to insufficient water storage capacity, the area is often affected by floods. The road connecting the irrigation system to the area where the people live is in poor condition, which puts a heavy burden on farmers.
Through this grant, the project is expected to benefit about 1,000 local people by improving irrigation systems to ensure a stable water supply for agriculture throughout the year. In addition, it is expected that people's living standards and incomes will improve due to the increase in the amount of rice produced in the area.
Second: Bridge construction project in Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province (budget 137,207 USD) Recipient institution: Department of Public Works and Transport of Kampong Chhnang province.
Third: Bridge construction project in O'Mreas commune, Siem Bok district, Stung Treng province (budget $ 168,276). Recipient institution: Department of Rural Development, Stung Treng province.
The aid will be used to build a new concrete bridge to replace the current dilapidated wooden bridge, as many locals often cross the bridge to get to schools, workplaces and hospitals, as well as transport agricultural products. And unsafe, especially for children and the elderly. In addition, as the number of heavy vehicles is expected to increase, the current bridge may be unbearable and as a result may collapse.
The project is expected to benefit about 2,800 people in four villages by ensuring safe access to the nearest schools, markets and health centers throughout the year. The construction of the new bridge will also facilitate the transportation of agricultural products, which we expect will improve people's living standards and increase agricultural income.
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of a friendly and official visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, General Tea Seiha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, led a high-level military delegation of the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia to pay a courtesy call on Prime Minister Fam Minh Chinh. Of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam on the afternoon of November 13, 2023.
During the meeting, Mr. Pham Minh Chinh congratulated General Tea Seiha on his first visit to Vietnam as Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia. Cambodia paid a successful visit to Vietnam to contribute to the strengthening of cooperation between our two countries and to further develop the friendship between the two countries.
"Our two countries, Cambodia and Vietnam, have a long history of historical ties and have been united in overcoming all difficulties and cooperating with each other in the development goals of each country," said Fam Minh Chinh. To make progress.
In response, General Tea Seiha stated: “The completion of a friendly and official visit to Vietnam is the first and historic visit to further strengthen political and security relations and cooperation with Vietnamese friends in Vietnam. Building a community together, Cambodia-Vietnam.
On that occasion, General Tea Seiha thanked the Vietnamese government, army and people for their constant support to the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces as well as Cambodia as a whole for cooperation in all fields. In fact, during the outbreak of Kovid-19, the Vietnamese side provided a lot of assistance and support, including encouragement and spirit.
This noble gesture further underscores the friendship, solidarity, sentimentality and sincere respect of the whole Vietnamese army and people for the army and the Cambodian people in the spirit of promoting cooperation in all fields.
Senior Minister Sok Siphana: Chinese Investment in Physical Infrastructure Development in Cambodia Contributes to Attracting Foreign Direct Investment, Especially in Manufacturing
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Dr. Sok Siphana, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission, said that China's significant investment in the development of Cambodia's physical infrastructure has contributed to attracting foreign direct investment, especially in the manufacturing sector, which helps to improve. Up Cambodia's competition.
Mr. Sok Siphana's remarks were made on the occasion of leading the Cambodian delegation to the "Global China Economy and Technology Summit 2023" under the theme "Strengthening Technology Growth and Regional Prosperity for Two Days" from November 6-7, 2023 in Shenzhen, China.
The meeting aims to promote economic and trade opportunities among the members of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (AEC) and focus on discussions on the potential of the BRICS to become a major economic force. Influenced in the polar world and learned more about China's role in global power shifts.
Prof. Dr. Sok Siphana said that the Cambodia-China-ASEAN Free Trade Agreement has significantly changed the Cambodian trade landscape by providing new markets for Cambodian agricultural products and commodities.
He highlighted the changing world order and the need for a multilateral system to address the global challenges of the 21st century.
He stressed that the BRICS countries have now become a strategic economic power in the multi-polar world, making China the world's major economic market.
The Bangkok Post reports that the measure aims to support the development of rice quality by providing farmers with 1,000 baht per rai, up to 20 rai per household, or a total of 20,000 baht. The project is expected to benefit 4.68 million Thai families.
On November 7, the Cabinet approved measures to support rice worth a total of 55 billion baht, including loans, to provide farmers with a five-month delay in selling rice with a 25% moisture content. Loans for agricultural cooperatives to intervene in the agricultural sector by buying rice from the market at a reasonable price.
Under a five-month delay in farmers' rice sales, the Thai government will intervene in the market by offering participants 12,000 baht per tonne and an additional 1,500 baht per tonne for storage. .
The National Rice Policy Committee says the Thai government wants to absorb 3 million tonnes of rice under the project.
Mr Phumtham said the latest rice support measures are likely to be submitted to the Cabinet for approval on Tuesday, November 14, and the initial schedule for cash disbursement will run from November to September 30. 2024.
