DPM Sar Sokha Closes the General Assembly of the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia, General Sar Thet Elected President of the 5th Mandate
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of November 14, 2023, Mr. Abhisand Bandith Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Honorary President of the Association, presided over the closing ceremony of the General Assembly of the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia. The ceremony was held at the Ministry of Interior.
The General Assembly of the Friends of the National Police of Cambodia started this morning, chaired by Dr. Mao Chandara, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Interior and Permanent Vice President of the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia.
The General Assembly also elected a new chairman, a member of the Standing Committee for the fifth mandate, with General Sar Thet, the National Police Commissioner, as the president of the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia for the fifth mandate.
These activities show the humanitarian spirit, which is a great contribution to alleviate the hardships in the lives of national police officers as well as their families. The Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia held its first general assembly on March 14, 2002 in its first three-year term, ending its term on March 14, 2005.
During the General Assembly of the third mandate, the association amended the statute to be 5 years in each mandate. In the third and fourth mandates, the Friends of the National Police of Cambodia continued its activities in accordance with the statutes and decisions of the Central Committee to achieve better results.
As of August 2023, the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia has 78,069 members, of which 6,1897 are police officers, 16,170 are retired police officers and volunteer police officers are disabled. Chet continues to be a member of the association of 2 people.
