Woman dies of suspected heart attack in Banlung bathroom
(Ratanakkiri): On the morning of November 14, 2023, a woman died in the bathroom, suspected of having a heart attack, at a rented house, a barber shop in Aphivath village, La Ban Siek commune, Banlung city. Rattanakiri Province.
Immediately after receiving the information, the Banlung City Criminal Police Force, Banlung Criminal Police Force, in cooperation with the Ratanakkiri Provincial Police Technical and Scientific Bureau and the doctors at the Provincial Health Department and village-sangkat authorities arrived at the scene. Examine the body above.
According to the authorities who arrived at the scene, the body was named Pak Srey Mom, alias Lam Yang, 26 years old, a hairdresser. The victim currently resides at the scene and has a husband named Chey Pheak, 27 years old.
Eng Chhay Heng, 34, a co-worker with the victim, described leaving the house and arriving at the barber shop when he heard the sound of water leaking in the bathroom and shouting at Pak Srey Mom, also known as Lam Yang. No response was heard.
With suspicion, Eng Chhay Heng called Mong Srey Mom, Men Srey Mom and another unidentified man decided to break through the bathroom door and see the victim lying face down in the bathroom naked.
Immediately, Mong Srey Mom ran to call a doctor nearby. When the doctor arrived, he found that the victim was dead and had a heart attack.
According to the inspection and conclusion of the Office of Technical and Scientific of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Police and doctors at the Ratanakkiri Provincial Health Department, as well as local authorities in the village - Sangkat confirmed that the victim actually rented in the bathroom died of a heart attack. Indeed, the body was handed over to the family for a traditional Khmer ceremony with grief.
