During a workshop on the status of freshwater giant trout in the Mekong River and the World Record Certification Ceremony on November 14, 2023, Mr. Has Sareth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that this is a source of pride for Cambodia. The Cambodian trout broke the world record for the largest freshwater fish in the world, weighing up to 300 kg.
He said that the fish was nicknamed "Bonmi" by researchers because the fish did not return to the Mekong River on the full moon. According to the research results, Bonmey has been in the canyon that fishermen have caught in the past.
According to a senior official of the Ministry of Agriculture, in 2022, three freshwater giant trout were accidentally caught by fishermen in Koh Preah commune, Siem Bok district, Stung Treng province, the first giant trout weighing 180 kg and the second weighing 143. Kg and the third giant trout weighs 300 kg.
US Ambassador Patrick Murphy said it was "thrilling" that a giant trout caught in Cambodia's Mekong River broke the world record and showed the country's pride. This is a great opportunity to showcase the potential for conservation in the Mekong and Tonle Sap areas, which are rich in biodiversity. In particular, giant trout are really large, and if the mother is this size, the baby may not be small.
Please be informed that since 2020, the Fisheries Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Mekong River Wonder Project has released 16,236 endangered fish species back into the natural waters, including carp, royal fish, cucumber fish. There are three giant trout in it.
Ta Prohm villagers in Prek Eang commune request the authorities to take action to close an unlicensed rooster farm in violation of the agreement, still causing noise and stench
(Phnom Penh): Residents of Ta Prohm village, Sangkat Prek Eang, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh, have filed a new lawsuit against the owner of an illegal rooster farm in violation of the agreement, still causing noise and stench to the surrounding residents.
Please be informed that in the case of the rooster farm that caused the noise and stench, the residents of Ta Prohm village, Prek Eang commune have already complained to the authorities. On the morning of August 9, 2023, the Chbar Ampov district authority and the Phnom Penh Department of Agriculture also held a meeting. After meeting with the people's representatives, the representatives of the chicken business owners and stakeholders, the meeting decided as follows:
1: Let the business owners raise chickens to move to another location far from the town.
2: At this location, the law does not allow the business of raising chickens.
4: Business owners are not allowed to bring other new chickens into this farm location.
5. The owner of the chicken business must be clean and hygienic at the breeding site and avoid noise and odors affecting the neighbors.
However, because the farm owners did not comply with the agreement without any measures to reduce the noise of chickens and the smell from the farm, the people filed a complaint again and asked to close the farm without permission.
