(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has organized an examination to select the composition of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission (NEC) to serve in the 25 Capital and Provincial Election Commissions. For the election of senators for the 5th term in 2024.
According to the master plan, the examination for the composition of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission for the 5th Senate Election 2024 will be held in all capitals and provinces.
In order for this examination to be conducted accurately, transparently and fairly, the NEC has assigned members and leaders of the General Secretariat of the NEC to directly select in the 25 provincial capitals. Separately, for the correct test subject package is also stored securely, no candidate can know the questions before the exam.
Mr. Top Rithy, Director General of the General Department of Legal and Technical Services of the NEC, emphasized that the recruitment of officers to serve is based on the ability to serve the upcoming 5th Senate election in 2024. This.
He said that although the 5th Senate election in 2024 is a non-universal election, the NEC has taken great care to make the election process transparent.
The provinces to be held on November 12, 2023 are 13 provinces, including Pursat, Pailin, Siem Reap, Koh Kong, Kampot, Svay Rieng, Ratanakkiri, Stung Treng, Tbong Khmum, Oddar Meanchey, Preah Sihanouk, Kandal and Preah Vihear.
Separately, the provincial capitals that organized the exam on November 14, 2023, there are 12 provincial capitals, including: Kampong Chhnang, Battambang, Kampong Thom, Kampong Speu, Takeo, Prey Veng, Mondulkiri, Kratie, Kampong Cham, Banteay Meanchey, Kep and Phnom Penh.
Please be informed that on October 10, 2023, the NEC announced the recruitment of 175 NEC members as short-term contract officers to work in the NEC for the election. Appoint a senator for the 5th term in 2024.
The British Joint Chiefs of Staff in Cambodia commends the bravery of Cambodian Blue Hat forces involved in peacekeeping, especially demining cooperation.
On the morning of November 14, 2023, he met with Major General Prak Soth, Deputy Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center, on behalf of General Sem Sovanny, Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center.
He is very proud of the bravery of the Cambodian Blue Hat forces involved in peacekeeping, especially demining cooperation. Not only that, he also expressed support and want to help Cambodia to achieve success in the Cambodia Mine Action Project in 2025.
He also thanked the United Kingdom for sending peacekeepers on a UNTAC mission to Cambodia in 1991-1993 and sacrificing one fighter.
At the National Peacekeeping Center, Major General Prak Soth was very pleased with the encouragement of the British side. The lieutenant general also asked the British side to provide long-term training in addition to demining skills, language control, drones, as well as exchange visits between the two countries.
