Samdech President Hun Manet: The implementation of the social security system for health care is in response to the wishes of the people (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Moha Bovathi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia Health care is in response to the aspirations of the people, especially life support in the event of an accident, health care, pensions, which has never been in the history of Cambodia.
This statement was made by the President on the occasion of the official launch of the "Voluntary Social Security System for Voluntary Health Care for Individuals and Dependents of the Member of the Socialist Party of Cambodia." And "Vocational and Technical Training Program for Youth from Poor and Vulnerable Families" at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh on the morning of November 14, 2023.
The Prime Minister stated that the implementation of the social security system is the main focus of the Royal Government in helping people to receive benefits, especially life support in the event of an accident, health care, pensions. Like public servants, which has never been practiced in the history of Cambodia.
He added that the voluntary contribution to the social security program, which was officially announced today, is applicable to self-employed individuals and their dependents, including husbands or wives. Spouses and dependent children so that the citizens who are self-employed and those in charge of the members of the Socialist Party, such as children under the age of 18 or spouses under the age of 60, can pay health care contributions.
Self-employed persons and members of the Social Welfare Party, including spouses and dependent children, can receive social security for health care by paying 2.6% of the contributed income of 600,000 Riels equal to 15,600 Riel. Participation in the health care union, both compulsory and voluntary, allows workers to receive many benefits.
711 Disaster Search and Rescue Team successfully completes joint training and exercises with Japan
(Nagaoka-Japan): Nine countries conduct joint disaster training and exercises organized by the Japanese side and study tours at the Nagaoka Fire Department at Kogakuin University, Kobe and Miki Fire Department. The 711 Disaster Search and Rescue Task Force of the 70 Lech Brigade from November 8 to 13, 2023, was completed with better-than-expected results.
Participating in Disaster Relief Skills Training This course provides:
* First: New experiences to be used and implemented in Cambodia * Second: Strengthen the spirit of cooperation and professional responsibility when launching rescue operations * Third: Technical knowledge on the use of equipment and Rescue equipment.
The study visit helped to strengthen the spirit of readiness, quality control and maintenance of rescue equipment on a regular basis, and the commitment to the time of the rescue operation and the solidarity and cooperation between the first aid team and the fire brigade.
On November 14, 2023, the 711 delegation left Kobe, Japan for Kansai Osaka International Airport to return to Cambodia.
