The Royal Government of the Cambodian People's Party protects the poor and the private sector in all circumstances.
(Phnom Penh): From the time led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the term of office led by Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, the policy of the Royal Government of the Cambodian People's Party has always given priority to the poor and the private sector.
Through the 19th forum of the Royal Government and the private sector, which was held this morning, November 13, Samdech President Hun Manet continued his policy of protecting the poor and the private sector, as the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen relentlessly.
Samdech Thep Dey has announced that it will continue to collect taxes from small traders on the market, do not tax the family farmland, do not tax the property less than 100 million Riels, do not tax the minimum wage and the minimum wage of workers and do not tax. Lots of others. In general, the government tries to avoid taxing low-income people so as not to affect their livelihoods.
On the contrary, they are the first to receive protection from the government when they face crises such as the Kovid 19 crisis or natural disasters.
As for the private sector, although the Cambodian economy has been negatively affected by the global crises such as the Kovid 19 crisis, the Russian-Ukrainian war, as well as the Israeli and Hamas-Palestinian wars, the government has not left the private sector alone. The Prime Minister has put in place a number of measures to help address the challenges that businesses are facing in order to move the private sector forward.
The poor and beggars in the private sector have applauded the policy of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature, which is still resolute in protecting the private sector, as Samdech Techo, the former Prime Minister, has done unchangingly.
It is this strong policy to protect the poor and the private sector that has won the hearts of Cambodians to vote for the CPP forever, while the private sector has always been actively involved with the Royal Government to develop the country under all circumstances. Cambodia knows as much development as it does today.
