(Banteay Meanchey): Serey Sophorn Municipal Gendarmerie Base Force led by Brigadier General Yan Sovann, Municipal Gendarmerie Commander led an immediate operation to arrest two suspects in a case of money theft and drug involvement at 23:00 November 12, 2023 at Meanchey Park in Village 3, Sangkat Preah Ponlea.
The arrest of the two suspects was made according to the complaint of the victim, Chao Seav Mey, a 30-year-old female, currently residing in Korathan Village, Sangkat O'Ambel, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Colonel Yan Sovann, commander of the Serei Sophorn military base, said that the two suspects were:
Colonel Yan Sovann said that on that day, the suspects stole the victim's wallet and mobile phone while visiting the exhibition at Suon Meanchey. The victim immediately reported to the Armed Forces. There, he led the force directly to search and arrest two suspects immediately and confiscated a motorcycle and the victim's wallet to bring to the military police base in Serei Sophorn for legal action. Way.
After being arrested and interrogated, the suspects confessed that they had stolen their wallets and were using illegal drugs. Based on the suspect's confession, the municipal military base sent to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Lt. Col. Men Phirum, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie, said that the crackdown was carried out under the command of Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie. From Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
The suspect has now been sent to the Provincial Court by the Provincial Gendarmerie Criminal Bureau and this morning, Tuesday, November 14, 2023, the procedure will be followed. The exhibits of the victims were returned to the original owners by the military police.
