On the morning of November 13, General Tea Seiha, accompanied by Lieutenant General Fong Sitin, Deputy Chief of Staff of the Vietnamese People's Army, led a high-level military delegation from the Cambodian Ministry of National Defense to lay a wreath at the Heroes' Monument. Continue to lay a wreath in honor of President Ho Chi Minh in Hanoi.
During the meeting, General Phan Van Chang welcomed General Tea Seiha, who led a high-level military delegation of the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia to pay a friendly and official visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
On behalf of the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense, General Tea Seiha, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, expressed his pleasure at the warm welcome extended by the Vietnamese Minister of Defense to the Cambodian delegation. Officially in the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
General Tea Seiha considers that this visit to Vietnam has brought about the strengthening of friendship, solidarity and good cooperation for a long time between the People's Army and the Government of both Cambodia and Vietnam.
On that occasion, the two Defense Ministers briefed each other on the evolving situation in each country, as well as the national and international situation related to the current regional and global security.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 14, 2023, the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia organized its General Assembly after running for four terms. The General Assembly was chaired by Dr. Mao Chandara, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Interior.
