These activities show the humanitarian spirit, which is a great contribution to alleviate the hardships in the lives of national police officers as well as their families.
The Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia held its first general assembly on March 14, 2002 in its first three-year term, ending its term on March 14, 2005.
During the General Assembly of the third mandate, the association amended the statute to be 5 years in each mandate. In the third and fourth mandates, the Friends of the National Police Association of Cambodia continued its activities in accordance with the statutes and decisions of the Central Committee to achieve better results.
As of August 2023, the Friends of the National Police of Cambodia has 78,069 members, of which 6,1897 are police officers, 16,170 are retired police officers and volunteer disabled police officers. For more than two months, about 2.6 million students and teachers have participated in the "I do not use plastic bags today."
Thus, 15.61% of the population is directly involved in the campaign to reduce the use of plastic. While indirect participation by parents, guardians and relatives is estimated, nearly 50 percent of the nation's population has joined the campaign to reduce the use of plastic.
Cambodia's active participation now not only benefits its people, but also provides a good example of action to share with other countries around the world, demonstrating mobilizing initiatives. People in communities, schools and individuals need to make significant strides in reducing the widespread use of plastic waste.
The Cambodian Ministry of Environment has continued to strengthen its campaign to reduce the use of plastic by implementing practical measures by introducing separate bins in schools and encouraging students to recycle plastic and waste into compost. This major measure is in line with the United Nations Global Initiative to tackle plastic pollution.
