Minister Tho Chetha Conducts a Meeting on Preliminary Study on the Impact and Damage of Floods on Water Work Infrastructure in 2023
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, on the afternoon of November 13, 2023, chaired a meeting on the preliminary study on the impact and damage of floods on water infrastructure in 2023 and finding emergency solutions for floods. Stung Prek Tnaot.
Please be informed that the meeting focused on three points: 1) floodplains due to natural factors on a regular basis, 2) floodplains that can be reduced through the rehabilitation and construction of irrigation infrastructure and 3) floodplain areas. Resulting from the development and strategic plan to address.
On that occasion, the Minister said that the floods and floods of 2023 caused 14 provinces to be affected and damaged water infrastructure, of which 11 provinces assessed the damage to irrigation systems and landslides. River bank or river.
The Minister said that the main water works and irrigation infrastructure in the river basin, such as Ta Sal Reservoir, Peam Lvea-O Tong Reservoir, Reang Leang Chrey Reservoir, O Kon Trom Reservoir, played the important role on January 7. Water storage, management and diversion from Stung Prek Tnaot, which often harass the southern part of Phnom Penh and Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
The Minister instructed the meeting to discuss and take measures to reduce floods at the local level, based on three aspects: legal, technical and socio-economic aspects.
