"The Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the relevant legal norms do not allow foreigners, both physical and procedural individuals, to own land, ie only natural persons or legal entities," he said. Only Khmer nationality has the right to own land. ”
However, Samdech Hun Manet stated that after studying and reviewing the existing legal standards, Cambodia also has a mechanism that allows foreigners to buy and occupy real estate with almost the same rights as Ownership rights through the following three mechanisms:
First, the mechanism through the Cambodian representative by allowing foreigners to buy land through the Cambodian representative, but on the title deed must be named the Cambodian representative and to protect those investors Must have a contract with its representative.
Second, the mechanism through the Board of Governors According to the Law on Public Administration 2019, foreigners can buy land in Cambodia through the Board of Governors who have registered the Board of Governors at the Ministry of Economy and Finance, that is, foreigners can buy property. An administrative company acts as the manager of the property, but the company has no right to resell it without the consent of the foreigner who owns the property.
Third, the investment mechanism for sacred tourism sites, in which the owners of partner sites or sacred tourism can receive incentives such as: (1): Can obtain multiple entry visas or visa waivers or long-term stay in accordance with the law. Determine or be able to use a special entry and exit permit from the Royal Government (2): can get the right to own or use the right to enjoy real estate in the sacred tourist area.
Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet said that after much discussion before today's forum, the Royal Government of the 7th legislature decided to promote the implementation of one more mechanism, the long-term leasehold mechanism, in addition to the above three mechanisms. He stressed that this mechanism is not a new mechanism, which already has Cambodian legal standards, but has not yet been discussed and implemented, and the general public is not yet aware of this mechanism.
