Samdech stated that he wants the private sector to play a role as a mechanism to help strengthen compliance to provide confidence to reduce the need for inspections from relevant ministries and institutions.
Samdech stressed that "All ministries and institutions must ensure that one year to jointly inspect only once for the same purpose, unless there is a complaint from the workers themselves or any incident occurs, please follow the inspection principles. Once a year, let the Ministry promote this work.
Samdech added that all ministries and institutions within the inter-ministerial inspection mechanism must have a mechanism to receive complaints from the private sector to prevent the inspection of any working group.
The Prime Minister's remarks came after he listened to the requests and concerns of the private sector regarding the preparation of past legal standards, some of which overlap and were not comprehensive. Samdech considered this work as one of the priorities of the Royal Government by facilitating and simplifying the implementation mechanism to ensure efficiency and not to overlap.
In order to ensure transparency and efficiency, the preparation and implementation of legal standards, Samdech also set out the principle: "Implementation needs to be widely publicized and a transitional period of at least six months must be set before implementation."
