(Phnom Penh): The Council for the Development of Cambodia issued a press release on the 19th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum, which was held under the chairmanship of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia on November 13, 2023. This is according to a press release obtained by Fresh News.
Key Remarks by Samdech Mani Hun Sen, Opportunity to Meet the Private Sector, Announcing Interventions to Promote Doing Business in Cambodia
In this important meeting, Samdech Hun Sen announced a number of interventions to promote business in Cambodia, respond to crises, as well as maintain the resilience of the Cambodian economy. The forum is being held at the Peace Palace.
The following are some of the key points made by Samdech Mani Hun Manet, who spoke for about 3 hours:
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the new Royal Government has a core role to protect the old achievements and create new achievements. Based on this spirit, the Royal Government dares to listen, dare to take responsibility and dare to operate.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government clearly understands the burden of compliance that the private sector always raises. Therefore, the Royal Government will eliminate and amend some compliance. But the private sector does not have to be irresponsible at all.
* President Hun Manet stated that without compliance, the market economy would become anarchy.
* President Hun Manet encouraged the private sector to address compliance issues without regard to compliance as a barrier. But the government will try to address some of the compliance burdens.
* President Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government is not afraid to give up some revenue if that abandonment facilitates and supports the private sector to grow.
* President Hun Manet stated that the private sector has raised complex issues and overlap of some legal norms.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet advised that the drafting of legal documents should be done in consultation with the private sector and widely disseminated, with a transition period of at least 6 months before implementation.
* Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet stated that in a year, the relevant ministries and institutions must conduct joint inspections only once in factories, unless there are complaints from workers.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that in the 7th legislature, the Royal Government of Cambodia did not create a new tax and the existing tax did not increase the tax rate.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government does not have to pay taxes for people selling baskets.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the property tax is applied in 14 districts in Phnom Penh and 27 cities across the country.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the unused land that is required to pay tax is from 5 hectares up. Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the land tax is not used to avoid taking the land to be left unused for economic purposes.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the other 5 crops are not taxed, including: Mien, Pailin, Svay, hydropower, animal husbandry and local palm oil products.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that Cambodia currently has three tire factories, while another Chinese company plans to invest in the production of tires with a capital of about $ 500 million.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the presence of these tire factories has helped rubber plantations in Cambodia.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet announces exemption from customs duties on exported / imported goods worth less than $ 1,000.
* Prime Minister announces overtime to customs officers at dry ports at night to speed up work and provide decent wages.
* Samdech Mani announced that the state does not want to act as a police with the private sector, but the state wants to be a supporter
Samdech urged the relevant ministries and institutions to strictly enforce the ban on the import of food or food that is defective or of poor quality that affects health, whether it is pork, frozen chicken, eggs and illegal to Cambodia.
* Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet announced to the Ministry of Public Works to study to amend the law to limit the weight of 40 to 45 tons
* Samdech Mani Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government can not reduce the tax rate for the import of trucks
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet announced that the Royal Government has decided to launch a strategy to visit Siem Reap 2024 to promote tourism activities in Siem Reap.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet encourages tour operators to jointly promote tourism in Cambodia and not to compete with each other.
* President Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government is considering giving border cards to people near the Cambodian border to expand their tourism in the border provinces and neighboring provinces.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government has decided to provide a loan of $ 50 million to tour operators in Siem Reap.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet announces the designation of Phnom Kulen as a natural tourism site.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet advised banking and financial institutions to prepare loans for tourism in Siem Reap and loans for real estate.
* Samdech Manibodi Hun Manet encourages banking institutions to reorganize for buyers of land and houses affected by the economy.
* Samdech Mani President Hun Manet announces additional stamp duty exemption on the transfer of ownership or possession of all types of housing in the form of Borey and the value of more than 70,000 USD, allowing the withdrawal of 70,000 USD from the tax base Seal.
* Samdech Mani Hun Manet stated that houses worth less than $ 70,000 in the Borey will be exempted from paying stamp duty until 2024.
* The Prime Minister has announced a mechanism to allow foreign investors to obtain long-term visas.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet instructed the relevant ministries to work hard to promote the measures set out above with a sense of responsibility.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet instructed the Council for the Development of Cambodia to monitor the implementation of the intervention measures outlined above.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet decided to establish a working group in another field, namely the Digital Economy and Society Working Group.
