In this important meeting, Samdech Hun Sen will announce a number of interventions to promote business in Cambodia, respond to crises, as well as maintain the resilience of the Cambodian economy. The forum is being held at the Peace Palace.
The Royal Government Private Sector Forum was established in 1999 under the auspices of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, then Prime Minister of Cambodia. The forum is recognized by the World Bank as the most effective public-private dialogue mechanism and has received the highest performance rating of more than 20 other countries.
This forum is held almost every year. The 18th forum was organized in 2019 under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister of Cambodia. The Royal Government of Cambodia, the sixth legislature of the National Assembly, planned to hold its 19th forum in 2020, but it has been postponed until now because Cambodia, as well as the world, is facing the crisis of Kovid-19.
From time to time, the forum mechanism has expanded its scope from seven working groups to 14 sectoral working groups for the 19th forum.
It should also be noted that the Royal Government-Private Sector Forum is considered an open Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers. In this sense, all decisions of the forum will have the effect of the decision of the Council of Ministers.
