Interior Ministry Spokesperson: The appointment of Rong Chhun as National Party Advisor is in violation of a court order requesting the party to reconsider the appointment.
(Phnom Penh): The spokesman of the Ministry of Interior, Mr. Khieu Sopheak, told Fresh News this morning, November 12, 2023, that the appointment of Mr. Rong Chhun as an adviser to the National Forces is illegal because Rong Chhun is currently serving his sentence and is under the legal supervision of a court that is not yet qualified to be the chairman, vice chairman or advisor of any political party.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Interior also asked the National Forces Party to consider re-appointing Rong Chhun because people could also sue to dissolve the party if the party violated the law.
It should be informed that the National Forces Party issued a press release on November 12, which also confirmed the appointment of Mr. Rong Chhun as the party's advisor.
On the other hand, according to the reply letter of the Minister of Justice to Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the Election Committee in May 2023, it is stated that Mr. Rong Chhun has not fully regained his legal status as the five-year period has not expired. Years from the date of execution, and there are not enough conditions to apply for rehabilitation in court in accordance with Articles 534 and 535 of the Code of Criminal Procedure.
The verdict further stated that Rong Chhun must implement the following control measures:
* The convict must obey the summons of the prosecutor or of the person authorized by the prosecutor.
Prisoners must come to be examined by a person authorized by the prosecutor.
* The convict must be handed over to the prosecutor or to the person to whom the prosecutor has authorized all the documents for verification of reintegration into society.
Prisoners must notify the prosecutor of any change of address or occupation.
Prisoners must obtain permission from the prosecutor before traveling abroad.
Please be informed that after the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal issued this decision, Rong Chhun appealed to the Supreme Court and the Supreme Court upheld the Criminal Judgment No. 110 KR "R" dated November 12, 2021. Remains the same as achieved above.
Rong Chhun was charged with "inciting to cause social unrest" after being arrested on July 31, 2020 after committing a crime of inciting Chaos during the visit to the Cambodian-Vietnamese border in Tbong Khmum province. While visiting the provincial border, Mr. Rong Chhun issued a statement to the public that the new border post between Cambodia and Vietnam had entered Cambodian territory about 500 meters.
