(Siem Reap): Wat Svay Romeat, in cooperation with relevant authorities, organized a two-day traditional boat race at Teuk Thla Baray to celebrate the Solidarity Kathina Festival and remind the people to take care of the land and to love and respect the earth, the Ganges and the land. Both to participate in cleaning the environment clean.
Preah Noach Vuthy, Chief Bishop of Wat Baray Mohan Ti Ratanaream, also known as Wat Svay Romeat, Siem Reap City, said that this traditional boat race will be held for two days from November 11 to 12, 2023, and 17 pairs of boats will participate in the race. There are 3 women's boats and 6 players in each boat, including 10 pairs of 20 plate players. In total, there are 236 players.
Priest Noum Vuthy also said that this ceremonial ceremony is now accompanied by a ceremony of floating lanterns to worship the moon and Ok Ambok, which is associated with Buddhism, to worship the glass chin of the Buddha. At Phu Chong Neak and to commemorate the bodhisattva rabbit.
Preah Noch Vuthy confirmed that this celebration and the Khmer ceremonies all express the gratitude of the ancestors who are the Khmer people, the builders of Angkor and the precious Khmer culture.
Mr. Son Chamnan also thanked and thanked the Chief Inspector and all the committees for their efforts to organize this event, which is to continue to maintain our good culture and traditions to be stable and stable. Give a lot of fun to the people in this area, as well as people who come from far away to fulfill the merit and watch the happy ceremony.
