(Phnom Penh): 2023 is the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Japan and Cambodia, which began in 1953. In 1954, one year after the establishment of diplomatic relations, Cambodia relinquished its right to claim World War II damages from Japan.
First, Cambodia and Japan are important partners in many areas, and many Cambodians have gone to study, stay and work in Japan, and many Japanese people are living in Cambodia. Both governments have supported regional and international contributions.
The people of Cambodia and Japan have a lot of respect, love and understanding. In fact, as the Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, when he travels, he is welcomed by many Cambodians. This is a good feature of the excellent bilateral relations between the two countries.
Cambodian-Japanese relations were strained during the 1970s and 1980s due to the civil war in Cambodia. What shaped the direction and sharpening of positive relations between Cambodia and Japan was Cambodia's active participation in peace building and rehabilitation in Cambodia in the 1980s and 1990s.
With this diplomatic relationship, Japan sent its experts to repair and decorate some temples in the Angkor resort area.
Japan has contributed significantly to the socio-economic development of Cambodia, in fact, many Japanese investors have invested in Cambodia. Japan is also a major country in providing infrastructure development assistance in Cambodia, in particular the construction of the Chroy Changvar Bridge, Kisona Bridge, Neak Leung Bridge, a major river bridge in Cambodia.
Cambodia has supported Japan's policy, including at the UN Security Council, the two countries have also supported each other in the international arena. He also praised the Cambodian government for supporting Japan's policy and recently supported the issue of radioactive water from the Fukushima nuclear power plant in the international agenda.
In particular, the two countries also supported the participation in resolving the issue between Russia and Ukraine. Japan and Cambodia have also provided deminers training to Ukraine.
Second, in terms of security and defense, Cambodia and Japan have developed bilateral relations rapidly through the building of military capacity, in which the Japanese army also traveled to Cambodia and signed a memorandum of understanding between the two armies. Both. In addition, the Japanese Self-Defense Forces also docked at the port of Sihanoukville to celebrate the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries.
Third, Japan has always supported and respected Cambodia's independence and foreign policy position. In connecting and cooperating with other countries in the world, Japan would like to appreciate and thank Cambodia for its support to Japan as a long-term friendship to reach a comprehensive partnership. Recently.
Fourth, people-to-people exchanges, culture and culture of the two countries have carried out many practical events to celebrate the 70th anniversary between the two countries, Cambodia and Japan have organized many events as well. The Japanese government has provided many scholarships to many Cambodian students through various programs.
