The National Bank of Cambodia and JICA publish the book "Dollarization in Cambodia: Policy Relations in Financial Sector Development for Least Developed Countries"
(Phnom Penh): On November 10, 2023, the National Bank of Cambodia and the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) published a book entitled "Dollarization in Cambodia: Policy Relations in Financial Sector Development for Developed Countries. "Little" officially with the participation of Dr. Chea Chanto, Honorary Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, Dr. Chea Serey, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia.
The book "Dollarization in Cambodia: Policy Relations in Financial Sector Development for Least Developed Countries (LDCs)" is a joint work between the National Bank of Cambodia and the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA). World famous.
This book is the result of a joint research collaboration between the National Bank of Cambodia and the Research Institute of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA), using data collected from households, enterprises and financial institutions across the country.
In the article entitled "Dollarization in Cambodia: Policy Relationships in Financial Sector Development for Least Developed Countries (LDCs)", the author highlights the history of dollarization in Cambodia and macroeconomic aspects, as well as in-depth analysis. About the influence of dollar circulation in economic activities and the payment system that helps increase the use of the riel.
The authors point out that dollarization in Cambodia has become an important case study for developing countries, and that the Bakong payment system is a model for reducing dollar circulation. In addition, the National Bank of Cambodia has unveiled plans to implement new financial services to encourage the public to use the riel more widely.
She said that although high dollarization has limited the implementation of monetary policy, as the size of the Cambodian economy has grown, the lack of full access to monetary policy has made the economy more vulnerable, resulting in a reliance on fiscal policy. Taxes.
"Almost every country now has a narrow fiscal space due to repeated crises, and countries around the world are increasingly relying on monetary policy to restore economic growth," she said.
"I am confident that this book will be of great benefit to readers, such as policy makers, researchers and students working in the areas of dollarization and economics," he said.
The content of the articles in this book is important for the study and understanding of the evolution and current state of dollarization in Cambodia, as well as the key policies to support economic growth.
