(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the Cambodian-Japanese diplomatic relations for the past 70 years have left a lot of sweet, sticky and bitter taste.
Dr. Sok Touch made this statement on November 10, 2023, on the occasion that the Royal Academy of Cambodia organized a special discussion on Cambodia-Japan relations to celebrate the 70th anniversary of Cambodia-Japan diplomatic relations. Khmer Veteran Conference Hall of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
According to Dr. Sok Touch, in 1941, Japan used French and Thai colonial forces to drive Cambodian and Thai troops out of Cambodian territory in Battambang and Oddar Meanchey provinces.
Dr. Sok Touch also reminded that after Japan lost World War I and withdrew from Cambodia at that stage and the sweetness was lost, but the Royal Government of Cambodia did not demand compensation when Japan came to control Cambodia instead of France because But Cambodia understands the well-being of Japan because it lost the war and fell into poverty.
The sweetness As the Japanese economy grew, Japan forgot about Cambodia, the Japanese government provided a lot of assistance to Cambodia. The Japanese government helped build the first bridge across the Tonle Sap River in Cambodia, the first Chroy Changvar bridge, with a total length of 709 meters, in Phnom Penh, connected to National Road 6A. This bridge was built in 1963 during the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era.
Japan helped build the Kizuna Bridge, a bridge across the Mekong River in Kampong Cham city of Kampong Cham. The bridge was inaugurated in 2001 and is the first bridge to be built across the Mekong River in Cambodia.
In addition, Japan also continued to build the Neak Leung Bridge, a type of highway bridge across the Mekong River connecting Kandal to Prey Veng and to Svay Rieng.
Dr. Sok Touch considered that the three bridges that Japan helped to build were symbolic of the triangular ties, a symbol of great power.
Dr. Tha Japan was also a signatory to the end of the crisis in Cambodia and sent its peacekeepers to defend the 1993 Cambodian election process.
The President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia stated that the Cambodian people now have a strong relationship with Japan, believing in everything that Japan has in Cambodia.
It should be noted that Cambodia and Japan first established official diplomatic relations in 1953, and 70 years later, in 2023, the two countries have raised the level of bilateral relations to the level of "comprehensive strategic partnership", the highest level of strategic partnership. Of relations between these two Asian countries.
Under the good relations and cooperation, Cambodia and Japan have established a lot of political cooperation with each other. Cambodia has supported a number of Japanese policies, such as: active contribution to peace and dialogue.
Samdech Hun Sen said that the modernization of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the field of national defense, which has three points, including: modernization of infrastructure, modernization of training and modernization of equipment.
"The modernization of the army, we must focus on three main tasks, including: modernization of structure, second: modernization of training and third: modernization of equipment," said the Prime Minister.
In which, the President further explained:
* For structural modernization, it is necessary to regularly evaluate and revise the structure to respond to current and future task requests, because every era, risks and challenges are different. All of this requires all national institutions, especially the security forces, to continue to pay attention to assessing and adjusting the structure to respond.
* For modernization, training must focus on strengthening and modernizing schools, strengthening training programs and lessons, and strengthening modernization of facilities and facilities, including training grounds. Human resources without real skills do not guarantee operational and responsiveness, so training is the key to paying more attention, and when it comes to training, focus on strengthening the school.
For equipment modernization, additional equipment must be provided to assist in the operation and rescue in the event of a disaster.
It should be informed that regarding the modernization in the field of defense, Samdech Hun Sen has been gradually introduced and implemented since he was the Commander of the Army, including the strengthening of professional training and Equipped with equipment that serves the operation as well.
France Continues Support for Budget and Accounting Reform in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance and the French Agency for Development (AFD) on the morning of November 10, 2023 held a signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding on the implementation of the project to support the budget and accounting reform phase. 3.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Chou Vichit, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Representative of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, and HE Jacques PELLET, Ambassador of the French Republic to Cambodia.
Notably, in the field of green finance, France was the first country to develop and use environmental impact assessment instruments in its budget and was also one of the first countries to issue green securities.
Reform of the public financial system and financial principles based on green principles is an important topic, and the French Agency for Development (AFD) is pleased to share knowledge and experience related to this topic to professional officials of the Ministry of Economy. And finance as well.
This technical assistance project is a good gesture to show the continuous growth of relations and stronger cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the French Republic for the common benefit of both countries.
