Taiwan considers the United Kingdom an important democratic partner, despite the lack of formal diplomatic relations.
Due to diplomatic isolation and pressure from China, Taiwan, the chipmaker, has few formal foreign trade agreements, although the island is a member of the World Trade Organization (WTO) and has a trade agreement. Free trade with Singapore and New Zealand.
