The meeting was held for two days from 09-10 November 2023 in order to: (1) Review the implementation of the action plan in the ASEAN framework implemented in 2023 and set the direction, policy and plan. Action for implementation in 2024; and (2) review the action plan implemented in 2023 and approve the action plan for implementation in 2024 with development partners including: ASEAN-China, ASEAN-Japan, and ASEAN-Korea.
The 29th Plenary Meeting of the ASEAN Transport Ministers discussed the strengths, weaknesses, challenges and solutions in all areas of transportation, including: (1) land transport, (2) water and road transport. Sea (3) Air transport, (4) Transportation facilitation and (5) Sustainable transportation.
At the Plenary Meeting on November 9, 2023, Mr. Peng Ponna addressed the development of the transport and logistics sector in Cambodia, which has made a significant contribution to connecting Cambodia with its neighbors. And Cambodia's connection within the regional framework.
