Philippines to launch five Coast Guard vessels with Japanese assistance to strengthen maritime patrol capabilities
MANILA, Nov. 9 (Xinhua) - The Philippines will launch five Coast Guard ships worth half a billion dollars through a loan from the Japanese government to strengthen its capacity, a senior official said on Thursday. Its in patrolling disputed waters in the South China Sea. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on November 9, 2023.
The Philippines has been modernizing its maritime security assets and strengthening ties with allies to counter China's aggressive behavior in the South China Sea, which includes the two neighboring countries' disputed areas.
"The project will allow the Coast Guard to ensure the safety of key maritime links in the western Philippine Sea," he said. "It will also help the Philippine Coast Guard fight illegal activities and strengthen maritime law in Philippine waters," he added.
Japan's official development assistance has played an important role in improving the capacity of the Philippine Coast Guard. In recent years, Tokyo has financed the purchase of two 97-meter patrol vessels and 10 44-meter patrol vessels.
