The King issues a Royal Decree appointing General Chea Dara as Secretary of State for the Ministry of National Defense
General Chea Dara is known as one of the most talented people in the field of defense, having graduated from the field of defense in France. This battle contributed greatly to the cause of the motherland.
Especially in the border war with Thailand in 2008, General Chea Dara was a front line commander who was constantly stationed in the hot battle direction of the Temple of Preah Vihear, waiting to respect and implement the orders of General Phkay Meas 5 Samdech Techo Hun Sen out of number in defeating the enemy, defending the territory, defending the nation and the Khmer temple.
The courage and heroic example of General Chea Dara is left in the respect, love and remembrance of the commanders, officers, deputies and soldiers who joined the battle to defend the motherland. Based on the many merits in the cause of the nation, the motherland and the people, General Chea Dara received the trust and confidence of the Royal Government and the trust of the King, and was continuously appointed and given the rank and rank by the King.
In the old legislature, General Chea Dara was appointed by the King to be the Minister to accompany the Prime Minister as an advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen with the same rank as Senior Minister.
Here is the King's decree: China can achieve economic growth target for 2023 (Video inside) (Beijing): The governor of the People's Bank of China said on Wednesday that China expects to achieve the growth target of domestic production. This year, the superpower must change its economic growth model to continue to achieve high quality and sustainable growth.
Pan Gongsheng, governor of the People's Bank of China, was quoted by Reuters as saying in a statement posted on the central bank's website that the pace of economic growth has recently improved. Consumption has been steadily recovering and employment rates and consumer prices have remained stable.
Beijing has set a growth target of about 5 percent for 2023.
"Our country's economy needs a reasonable growth rate, but more importantly, we need to achieve high-quality and sustainable development," Pan said. "Changing the economic growth model is more important than finding a high growth rate," he added.
Pan said without elaborating that the People's Bank of China will maintain reasonable credit growth, maintain adequate cash flow and "operate the financial resources held inefficiently and streamline the use of funds."
Chinese leaders have pledged to allocate more financial resources to support technological innovation, modern production and green development. According to Reuters.
