The National Bank of Cambodia, in collaboration with the JICA Research Institute, authored a book on dollarization in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia has collaborated with the Research Institute of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) to write a new economic book entitled "Dollarization in Cambodia: Policy Relations in Financial Sector Development for Least Developed Countries. (LDCs) ”.
This book is the result of a joint research collaboration between the two institutions, using data collected from family units, enterprises and financial institutions across the country.
The analysis articles in this book are important for studying the evolution and current state of dollarization in Cambodia, as well as highlighting key policies that support economic growth. The authors highlight that the case of dollarization in Cambodia has provided significant experience for countries with similar problems, such as countries in Africa and Central Asia.
The outreach program will be presented by economists from the National Bank of Cambodia and development partners to explain in detail the latest discoveries in this book. General Knowledge: Who was the first to travel around the world?
