(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan, through its Embassy in Cambodia, has provided $ 348,919 to three donors under the Humanitarian Security Small Grants Project (Kusanoni Grant) for the construction of school buildings. Primary schools and installation of water supply systems in rural Cambodia in Kampong Speu, Kampong Thom and Mondulkiri provinces.
The Grant Signing Ceremony was held at the Embassy of Japan under the chairmanship of Mr. Ou Nou Atsushi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia and Representatives of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Kampong Speu, Kampong Thom and Mondulkiri Water Supply Departments on the afternoon of the 8th. This November 2023.
* First: Project for construction of school building at Sre Kin Primary School in Oral District, Kampong Speu Province (US $ 92,425).
* Second: Construction of a school building at Russey Doch Primary School in Prasat Balang District, Kampong Thom Province (US $ 100,344) Recipient: Department of Education, Youth and Sports, Kampong Thom Province
In this project, a 6-room school building equipped with furniture and a hand-washing place will be built at Russey Douch Primary School in Kampong Thom province. Currently, the students at this school have difficulty studying because the current wooden school building and wooden furniture are in a state of disrepair. Not only that, the environment is not very clean due to the lack of hand washing facilities.
The project aims to provide a safer and more comfortable learning environment and is expected to benefit 162 students and 8 teachers by improving the quality of education.
* Third: Water Supply System Installation Project in Sen Monorom City, Mondulkiri Province (US $ 156,150) Mondulkiri Water Supply Authority
Japan's Kusanoni Grant was launched in Cambodia in 1991 to support Cambodia's efforts to develop and rebuild the country at the grassroots level.
