(Kampong Thom): Mr. Eng Chea San, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, in the morning of November 8, 2023, brought 54 tons of fragrant rice seeds for the Royal Government to provide to 541 families. From 4 communes in Stong district, Kampong Thom province to restore rice farming after flooding caused by rain in the past.
On that occasion, Mr. Eng Chea San instructed the farmers to study the season, geographical location and weather conditions very precisely before planting non-seasonal rice to avoid any impact, especially flooding due to floods as well as Stung Stong flood to enable rice farming and other crops, especially non-seasonal rice to get the desired yield.
He advised farmers to rehabilitate as soon as possible according to the season, especially when the water has receded, and to maintain water sources and use water properly and economically. Modern agriculture will also respond to current climate change and adaptation.
Mr. Eng Chea San further confirmed that the distribution of fragrant rice seeds is the high attention of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister, who always pays attention to the well-being of the farmers who have been affected by the floods. Last rainy season and the economic recovery of families to respond to poverty reduction in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate.
It should be noted that the fragrant rice seeds distributed at this time are 54 tons and 100 kilograms, a non-seasonal reserve variety, which is given to farmers who have a biological scarcity affected by the floods during the previous rainy season and have water sources. Adequate irrigation of 541 families from 4 communes in Stong district will cover 340.34 hectares.
