He added that what the APSARA Authority has done so far is only a partial contribution to encourage students to gain knowledge about participating in the protection, preservation and conservation of the nation's heritage.
Poy Saro, principal of Krabei Riel Primary School, said that during the 11 months of teaching, heritage education programs and student internships are very important because these are the best foundations for them to explore. The future as a successor to the traditional Khmer cultural heritage.
He thanked the APSARA Authority, the Khmer Cultural Heritage Organization, as well as the relevant authorities for their support in teaching the heritage education program from the beginning to the end of the training.
Health Minister reveals key solutions to leadership issues and innovation to nearly 2,000 staff members
(Phnom Penh): Professor Chheang Ra, Minister of Health, presented the key to solving the problem to nearly 2,000 staff officers under his supervision.
