This training to continue to implement one of the three priority strategies that the Ministry has set out is to strengthen institutions through leadership training to help leaders have clear decision-making skills.
This week's lesson is the second key to solving problems in line with the five main objectives:
1: Distinguish between pre-defined reform approach with a problem-solving approach
2: Raising and prioritizing issues that need to be addressed
3: Breaking down the most important of the small issues into key components
4. Identify the people or potential individuals involved in those issues, including determining which individuals are most important.
5. Be able to measure the size of the problem to come up with strategies that may persuade some leaders to pay more attention.
