MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russia on Wednesday announced the inclusion of another International Criminal Court (ICC) judge on its list of wanted individuals as the court seeks to arrest the president. Russia, Vladimir Putin involved in the war crisis in Ukraine This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, November 8, 2023.
In March this year, the International Criminal Court (ICC) in The Hague, the Netherlands, issued an arrest warrant for Putin on war crimes charges involving the forcible removal of children from Ukraine during the war. Invasion of Moscow. The ICC has also issued an arrest warrant for Maria Lvova-Belova, Russia's child rights officer, on similar charges.
Russia, a non-member of the ICC, has argued that the arrest warrant against Putin is invalid. However, the order restricts Putin's travel abroad, as ICC member states are obliged to comply with the tribunal's ruling. The Russian president missed the BRICS summit in South Africa in August and the G20 summit in India in September.
