In particular, the Certificate in Front Office Skills and Food and Beverage Service Skills also opens the door for young people to acquire basic and level 2 vocational skills, enabling them to pursue higher education.
According to Mr. Chuob Ratana, after this consultation workshop, in the future, the Ministry of Tourism will have another workshop to validate these documents before giving them to vocational training schools to use for training.
