(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on the evening of November 7 issued a press release on the writing process of the Higher Secondary Diploma (Bakdup) Exam Session: November 6, 2023.
Higher Secondary Diploma Examination Exam Session: 06 November 2023 There were 137,412 candidates registered for the exam, 73,278 females divided into 227 examination centers with 5,543 rooms. The total number of judges and commissions in the writing process is 29,525, including 4,126 at the Ministry and 25,355 in the provincial capital. A total of 3,040 leaders, officials and observers of the Anti-Corruption Unit participated.
A total of 2,328 absent candidates, 934 females, equivalent to 1.69% of the total registered candidates (of which 1,814 absent candidates, 749 females). Candidates had 85 cases of health problems, of which 5 candidates had health problems and could not continue the exam. In addition, all candidates who had health problems resumed the exam as usual after the symptoms improved and under care. Take care of the medical team.
In each examination center, the operation was good, calm and well-organized, and the guidelines of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports were followed. Although it rained in some provinces, it did not affect the candidates' writing process.
Nationwide Subcommittee, National Subcommittee, Subcommittee Assistant, District Vice Chairman, Central Committee, Building Inspection Committee and Conservation Committee, have worked diligently and responsibly and with good cooperation from the Anti-Crime Unit. Corruption of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, health agencies, forces and relevant authorities.
The Ministry emphasizes that, "Overall, the writing phase of the Higher Secondary Diploma Examination, Examination Period: November 6, 2023, was conducted in accordance with the principles of law, justice, transparency and acceptable results, and in accordance with the principle of" those who know ".
