(Phnom Penh): The quick reaction team of the Anti-Drug Department of the General Commission of the National Police on November 8, 2023 came out to reject the fabricated information that was re-posted by an anonymous Facebook user named Lavy. To confuse the law enforcement authorities with the intention of causing social insecurity and defaming the authorities.
The statement of the Quick Reaction Team of the Anti-Drug Department of the National Police General Commission is as follows:
The Quick Reaction Team of the Anti-Drug Crime Department of the National Police is honored to inform the public that this video posted by Lavy on Facebook is an old video that was posted by TMN in early August 2023. It has just been reposted by anonymous Facebook user Lavy to attract attention with the intention of causing social insecurity and defamation of the authorities.
The Anti-Drug Department's Rapid Reaction Team strongly rejects the posting of fabricated slanderous information and strongly condemns this misinformation, which leads to a misunderstanding of law enforcement authorities with the intent to cause Insecurity in the national society.
To dispel this confusion, the Quick Reaction Team of the Anti-Drug Department of the General Commission of the National Police quoted TMN on Facebook on August 3, 2023 as follows:
1- On July 30, 2023, after receiving information and requests from the people on the illegal distribution of drugs in Russey Keo school, the expert team (A5) of the department went to search and crack down during the visit. The perpetrators ran away and detained only two young men and brought them to the department for questioning.
After questioning, it was found that the two young men actually used drugs, especially e-cigarettes. Authorities have stopped educating people about the dangers of using drugs and using e-cigarettes, which they mistaken for illegal. Subsequently, the department invited the guardians to ensure that they were educated and taken back to the community for treatment according to the procedures.
2. The images and audio recordings included in this broadcast are not related to the operation of the department, which is the malicious intent of the Facebook owner named TMN in order to deceive the public, discredit the authorities and protect the perpetrators only.
3. Facebook owner TMN should consider professional ethics and revise its broadcast. The Anti-Drug Department is happy to meet the Facebook owner and thank the public from all walks of life for their participation. Improve and cooperate in the prevention and suppression of drug offenses in line with the "3 Do 1 Report" slogan.
The following is the explanation of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes in August 2023:
