Phnom Penh Armed Forces Celebrates the 70th Anniversary of the Birth of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces
(Phnom Penh): November 9 is the day that Cambodia celebrates the 70th anniversary of the National Independence Day (November 9, 1953-November 9, 2023), which Cambodia gained independence from French colonialism in conjunction with the 70th anniversary. The year of the establishment of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces as well.
On the morning of November 7, 2023, the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, with the guidance of General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Royal Cambodian Gendarmerie, Organize a celebration to join the celebration under the presidency of Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie as Commander of the Phnom Penh Gendarmerie.
The ceremony was attended by the Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Deputy Chief of Staff, Chief-Deputy Director of the Department, Chief of Office, the Commander-Deputy Commander of the 14 Khan Military Base, the Commander-Deputy Commander of the Battalion and officers of the Royal Gendarmerie. Many more in Phnom Penh.
During the ceremony, Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang also distributed gifts, including rice, pure water, orange juice and budget to a total of 23 representatives of veterans and the families of soldiers who sacrificed their lives. Promote the implementation of key measures to reform public administration at the Peace Palace
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 8, 2023, Samdech Moha Bovathi Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, chaired a meeting of the National Committee for the Implementation of Key Measures for Public Administration Reform of the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly. At the Peace Palace.
In this new legislature, in order to promote more effective public administration reform, the Royal Administration has decided to prepare a new Royal Decree on the organization and functioning of the Public Administration Reform Committee with 21 articles. The new Royal Decree on the organization and functioning of the revised Public Administration Reform Committee was promulgated by the King on October 25, 2023.
The main points that have been revised are the composition of the CJCC. In addition, the chairmen of the four sub-committees of the CCC And representatives of the 25 Capital and Provincial Governors as members, as well as the four sub-committees of the CCC. Contained in the old Royal Decree in accordance with the type and scope of work for which the Public Administration Reform Committee is responsible.
The four sub-committees of the CCC These include: 1) Sub-Committee on Public Service Innovation and Innovation, 2) Sub-Committee on Public Service Excellence, 3) Sub-Committee on Human Resource Management, Institutions and Salaries, and 4) Sub-Committee on Capacity Building for Officials.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, on the afternoon of November 7, 2023, handed over 150 computers, 150 desks and chairs and set up an ICT Lab to the National Defense University, represented by General Professor Chea Dara, Rector of the National Defense University.
On that occasion, the Minister stated that the materials provided at this time are to meet the needs of the National Defense University in order to promote the training of military officers in military information technology.
The minister added that the 150 computers provided now are high-capacity computers to meet the complex technology learning requirements of each subject.
The Minister praised the National Defense University for its active contribution to enhancing the capacity of the Armed Forces to have real knowledge, skills and professionalism in taking responsibility for the protection of territorial integrity, peace, development and livelihood. Peace of the people all over the country under the wise leadership of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet as Prime Minister.
In response, the General thanked the Minister for his contribution to the development of human resources in Cambodia, especially in the field of military information technology, and in contributing to the building of a digital government in line with the Royal Government's first pentagon strategy. Promote governance and digital technology.
Please be informed that the National Defense University is a leading higher education institution of the Ministry of National Defense in the field of military science research, study of social sciences and languages, real science and vocational training, which is nationally recognized and International.
