Cambodian Human Rights Officer, UN Child Rights Officer and UNICEF Representative in Cambodia Meet to Discuss Establishment of National Human Rights Institutions in Cambodia and Draft Law on the Protection of Children
The purpose of this meeting was to discuss two main agendas: Establishment of the National Human Rights Institution (NHRI) in Cambodia; and Discussions on child-related topics include: the draft law on the protection of children, the ratification of the Third Supplementary Protocol on the Complaint Procedures of the Convention on the Rights of the Child, the exploitation of children and child labor.
Regarding the second agenda related to the draft law on child protection, the ratification of the third supplementary protocol on child and child labor exploitation procedures, Senior Minister Keo Remy informed the delegation in charge of children's rights. The United Nations says these jobs are under the authority of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
Responding to the President of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, the delegation of the United Nations Commission on the Rights of the Child believes that all the work of international conventions related to children's rights, women's rights, disability rights and the fight against torture are Under the field of human rights, because these works are related to the role and responsibilities of this committee.
After receiving this recommendation, Senior Minister Keo Remy stated that the Cambodian Human Rights Committee will continue to work with the relevant ministries to examine the feasibility and discuss various factors related to the request of the Committee on the Rights of the Child of the United Nations. Nation.
The delegation also noted and expressed appreciation for Cambodia for its positive progress on the implementation of the Convention on the Rights of the Child.
