The following is a statement condemning: The Royal Government of Cambodia and a Chinese company celebrate the one-year anniversary of the launch of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway.
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, the first expressway in Cambodia, has been in operation for a year. On the afternoon of Tuesday, November 7, 2023, the Royal Government of Cambodia and Chinese companies investing in the expressway held a celebration to mark the one-year anniversary of the expressway.
The one-year anniversary of the official opening of the first expressway in Cambodia was presided over by Mr. Sun Chanthol, Deputy Prime Minister and First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, High Representative of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia. And Wang Wintian, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Peng Po Na, Minister of Public Works and Transport, leaders of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, leaders of Chinese companies, as well as government officials, students and people living in the area of the expressway.
The Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, the newest and first expressway in Cambodian history, connects Phnom Penh to the tourist city and the largest seaport, Sihanoukville, with a total length of 187.05 km. March 22, 2019 Connected from Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh to Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province, passing through Kandal, Kampong Speu and Koh Kong Provinces.
Travel to Sihanoukville, which used to take four to five hours on National Road 4, has now been reduced to about two hours, indicating that the expressway has been completed. And is playing an important role in bringing new travel experiences, reducing time consumption and improving travel efficiency for people.
