This confirmation by the Doctor of Economics comes after the Royal Government of Cambodia announced the training of targeted youth groups from poor and vulnerable families, which the head of government plans to announce on November 14.
For this economist, the training will turn the labor force into a highly skilled and high-income workforce. This factor will make Cambodia more attractive for foreign investment, because Cambodia has already prepared its professional forces.
The popular former Cambodian prime minister added that if no ceasefire were reached, the Gaza Strip would become the world's largest massacre site.
This appeal was made on November 7, 2023. The Chairman of the Supreme Council of the King and President of the Ruling Party of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, stated:
"Without a ceasefire, the Gaza Strip would become the world's largest massacre and graveyard. There have been calls from the international community for a ceasefire in the Gaza Strip, but it has been rejected by the Israeli prime minister, who has said that "there will be no ceasefire without the release of hostages."
If the words of the Israeli prime minister are exactly what the media reports, I see it as a way out for a ceasefire if Hamas agrees to release hostages in exchange for a ceasefire.
I call on the Secretary-General of the United Nations and all parties concerned to begin negotiations, starting with the release of hostages by Hamas and Israel's promise of a ceasefire if the hostages are released.
