A statement from Russia's Foreign Ministry said: "As of 00:00 on November 7, 2023, the procedure for Russia's withdrawal from the CFE Treaty, which was suspended by our country in 2007, has been completed. It is complete. ” Russia suspended its accession to the treaty in 2015, and in 2023, Moscow announced its intention to withdraw.
The CFE Treaty was signed in 1990 by NATO and the former Warsaw Pact and entered into force in 1992. The treaty was created with the aim of balancing the two military alliances by limiting the number of weapons and military equipment that both sides were allowed to deploy.
