Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet Celebrates the 20th Anniversary of the Royal Ballet of Property in the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity
On the morning of November 7, 2023, Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, posted a message congratulating the 20th anniversary of the Royal Ballet on the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity (November 7, 2003-November 7). 2023).
It should be reminded that the Royal Ballet was inscribed on the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity on November 7, 2003 in Istanbul, Turkey.
This ancient Khmer dance or royal dance is a form of sacred dance: it is famous for its gentle gestures that are admirable and have a shimmering appearance.
The Royal Ballet, a traditional Khmer dance, is a type of dance in which the dancers skillfully use movements, gestures, and emotions according to the evolution of the story, which is confirmed by the lyrics of the chorus, and will be performed by the Pin Peat Orchestra Give this dance as well.
This morning, Samdech Thipdey Hun Manet met with more than 15,000 workers in Prey Nob District, Preah Sihanouk Province.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, November 7, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, met with about 15,194 workers. There are 482 pregnant workers. The meeting took place at the Cambodia Jejang GGZ Special Economic Zone in Prey Nob District, Sihanoukville Province.
Currently, Sihanoukville has a total of 623 factories and enterprises, with a total of 80,000 workers, earning a total of more than 238 million US dollars per year. Of these, 58 garment factories employ a total of 20,000 workers, earning more than $ 62 million a year.
The policy of creating jobs for the people is one of the priority policies of the Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party in both the old and new mandates. Immediately after the formation of the new Royal Government, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet arrested workers in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags industry for the first and subsequent public meetings.
In the last meeting, Samdech President presented the policy of the Royal Government in the new legislature, especially the Pentagon strategy - the first phase, which is a strategy to focus on job growth and improve people's lives, especially Six priority tasks for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to be implemented effectively in 2023 include:
2: Prepare urgent legal documents to prepare for the implementation of the social security system for health care through voluntary contribution for those in charge of the members To help ease the burden of health care costs for workers and their families quickly and widely disseminated to workers, as well as create a convenient mechanism for workers to participate in this program.
3. Organize vocational training programs for approximately 1.5 million young people from poor and vulnerable families across the country, and coordinate with stakeholders to allow workers to learn vocational skills. To increase productivity in the workplace, organize training sessions at night or on weekends.
4: To promote the full implementation of apprenticeship obligations in accordance with the Labor Law, including internships, internships, skills development and skills reorganization by encouraging the private sector to participate in the training of workers and provide Additional training for working workers to improve their skills, productivity and affordability.
5: Pay attention to the implementation of cash support programs for pregnant women, both before, during and after childbirth, better and more convenient. Also ensure that pregnant women and people with disabilities leave work 15 minutes early.
6: Establish a competition program on the theme of harmony in the workplace to turn an enterprise into a peaceful community from 2024 onwards.
The Prime Minister also introduced the action plan for the next two years to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to focus on the implementation of four priority tasks, including:
1. Collaborate with the Ministry of Women's Affairs, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, representatives of employers and workers' representatives to jointly study the possibility of establishing community nurseries and kindergartens in the factory area with the support of employers and stakeholders.
2. Collaborate with stakeholders to promote the improvement of the dining area or canteen in the factory that is operating in a way that is suitable for the workers and requires the preparation of the canteen or canteen for the new factory to be established.
3. Cooperate with stakeholders to study mechanisms to support and encourage the gradual change of means of transport of workers in accordance with technical standards and more comfortable by 2027.
4: Promote the skills recognition test program, which is an opportunity for both local and foreign workers to have a certificate of skill recognition to show their ability and skill level.
Under the coordination and attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia at the end of September, the minimum wage of workers in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags industry was announced to increase in 2024, which is low. At most $ 204 per month, an increase of $ 4 compared to 2023, despite the global economic crisis.
