Samdech Hun Sen said that Cambodia and Japan will work together to expand the deep-sea port in Sihanoukville to appear. While the current port of Sihanoukville can only accommodate 9.50 meters of cargo containers, the port of Sihanoukville receives only more than 18 percent of the cargo.
Samdech President Hun Manet also announced his ambition to turn Sihanoukville Port into a transfer point. If the first phase of the deep-sea port expansion is successful, the deep-sea port will be able to handle about 93 percent of the container space, which will reduce the cost of shipping by between $ 400 and $ 500. Only $ 200 per container.
In addition, the Prime Minister of Cambodia emphasized that if in the future Cambodia can expand the deep water port in the second or third phase, in the future, the port will be able to receive more containers carrying goods through, which will provide more job opportunities. More to the people, especially to boost the national economy.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that the expansion of the deep-sea port in Sihanoukville must always go ahead because it is the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party.
When the deep-sea port is completed by 2025, it will be able to allow ships with a capacity of more than 4,000 containers to dock, at which time about 93% of ships in Asia will dock in Cambodia. Provide a lower shipping cost, which is estimated to be less than $ 200 per container.
