The Public Administration Regulation and the Bar Association Collaborate to Raise Public Awareness of Public Administration in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Regulatory Authority for Public Administration (NWRC) and the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia on November 6, 2023 held a signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding on "Cooperation on "Increase public awareness and knowledge sharing."
The signing ceremony was presided over by Mr. Sok Dara, Director General of the Public Administration Regulatory Commission and Mr. Ly Chantola, President of the Bar Association of Cambodia, and was presided over and witnessed by the Royal Government Delegation in charge of the Director General of the Securities Regulator. Cambodia at the Office of the Financial Services Authority, not the bank.
The signing of this Memorandum of Understanding aims to raise public awareness and disseminate the law and regulations more widely, as well as provide cooperation to share knowledge related to the field of public administration to the members of the Bar Association. Kingdom of Cambodia as well.
Mr. Sok Dara said that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding is a new step in the process of developing the civil service sector in Cambodia, as well as promoting the development of the legal sector in Cambodia.
Mr. Sok Dara emphasized that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding focused on three main activities:
First, the dissemination and promotion of public awareness of laws and regulations related to the field of public administration
Second: Cooperation in organizing programs related to workshops and discussion programs related to the field of public administration in Cambodia.
Third, to contribute collaboratively on the study of the legal aspects and relevant superiorities in the field of public administration between the Regulatory Authority and the Bar Association of Cambodia.
At the same time, Mr. Ly Chantola said that the establishment of formal cooperation between the two institutions is an important strategy to promote the public administration sector to further progress.
Mr. Ly Chantola said that lawyers are an important player in providing legal advice to represent and prepare legal documents for investors and business people, both national and international in the profession of lawyers.
