The Prime Minister's remarks were made on the occasion of presiding over the inauguration of the huge building of the Ministry of Interior this morning, November 6, 2023.
His Excellency Hun Manet emphasized that this huge building of the Ministry of Interior is a testament to the importance of the role and responsibilities of the Ministry of Interior in the Royal Government, which is the backbone and important staff of the Royal Government in the implementation. Government policy, especially the provision of administrative services and protection of public security to the people.
According to Hun Manet, the Ministry of Interior also acts as a bridge between national policies set out by the Royal Government to practice, mostly by sub-national administrations and directly related to local issues.
"Of course, the policy will only be on paper if there is no one to implement it, and that implementation will not be successful without a joint institution as a facilitator," he said. In this sense, in addition to providing administrative services and public security protection to the people, the Ministry of Interior has played another important role as a government agency in promoting government policies into practical activities that benefit the people. Citizens
In this regard, Samdech Hun Sen also praised and appreciated the officials at all levels of the Ministry of Interior, both national and civil police, who have worked hard to serve the nation and the people in all circumstances in the past. This is an important factor in turning government policies into tangible results for the people.
He added that the participation of officials at all levels, both the National Police and the civil service of the Ministry of Interior, will continue to be an important factor in the effective implementation of other policies going forward. Under the leadership of Mr. Abhisandibandit Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, Samdech fully believes that the Ministry of Interior will be able to meet this expectation.
