Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet sets out six recommendations for the Ministry of Interior to implement to serve the people more effectively (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Set out six important work recommendations for leaders and officials of the Ministry of Interior to implement to serve the people more effectively.
This recommendation was made on the occasion of the official inauguration of the Ministry of Interior.
The Prime Minister set out six important work recommendations, including the following:
1. Strengthen the capacity of officials, especially officials who are close to the people, to have a clear conscience, ethics and professionalism, as well as the competent ability of the people, strengthen the evaluation of the appointment of both civil servants and police clearly.
2. To strengthen cleanliness, especially to strengthen its internal control mechanisms to prevent inactivity, especially the illegal use of power, and to take strict action if this happens.
3. Interpret the efficiency and convenience of its public services to ensure that there are no procedures that cause difficulties and unnecessary to the people.
4. Strengthen the OWSO and focus on organizing public services in technology systems such as CamDX, by giving priority to providing public services that people need or need frequently, such as registration rates, business license applications. And commercial services.
5. To work with relevant ministries and institutions to ensure the effective distribution of resources to the sub-national level to ensure that the sub-national level can fulfill the functions and tasks that have been successfully delegated.
6: To strengthen the monitoring and evaluation of all policies that the national level has set out for the sub-national level to implement in order to strengthen the linking of the policy to the actual implementation in order to ensure the best possible service to the people. With high efficiency and professionalism.
At the same time, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet praised the officials of the Ministry of Interior for their efforts to implement all the policies of the Royal Government in the past, and Samdech hoped that the officials of the Ministry of Interior will continue to fulfill all the policies. Of the Royal Government to be more effective.
