President of China Institute of Education encourages Chinese-ASEAN investors to invest in Cambodia's agricultural sector and push for more tax incentives
(Zhengzhou, China): Dr. Ky Sereywat, President of the Chinese Studies Institute of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, encourages Chinese-ASEAN investors to invest in Cambodia's agricultural sector and push for more tax incentives.
He made the remarks at the Guangzhou-Cambodia-ASEAN New Silk Road Development Forum 2023 held on November 3 in Chengdu, Henan Province, China.
"As Cambodia is at the center of ASEAN, I believe that Cambodia can become a trading center for Henan to increase their international trade by exchanging capital goods and services with ASEAN countries," he said. "If Cambodia becomes a business hub, I think Chengdu's investment and trade with ASEAN members can be expanded through Cambodia."
On that occasion, Dr. Ky Sereywat also highlighted the significant increase in the volume of bilateral trade between Cambodia and China, which has been directly affecting economic cooperation between the two countries.
"We are also striving to process the highest quality mangoes, namely dried mangoes or mango candies," he said. We know that in Henan Province, China, there are many places where mangoes can be grown, but the quality is different because Cambodian mangoes are tastier, which is a golden opportunity for Chinese investors to import mangoes. From Cambodia with the use of less capital and full support from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
"We also hope that China will facilitate preferential tariffs, especially the reduction of non-tariff barriers for Cambodian exports to China, including chemicals and pesticides," he said. Insects and so on.
Accompanying the forum, the Cambodian delegation also visited the Wanbang International Agricultural Products Transport Center. Traders at the center expressed confidence that under the coordination and joint efforts of the Cambodian-Chinese Ministry of Commerce and the Chinese Customs Department, they hope to get the green light on certification of fruit imports from Cambodia next year, which allows Let the Chinese side import fresh fruits directly from Cambodia.
According to data from the Ministry of Commerce, in the first nine months of 2023, Cambodia-China trade volume reached 9,099 million US dollars, of which Cambodia's exports to China amounted to 1,059 million US dollars, an increase of 18% compared to the same period last year. At the same time, 2022. Cambodia's imports from China amounted to 8040 million US dollars, an increase of more than 1 percent compared to 2022.
Cambodia's exports to China include clothing, footwear, leather, fur, machinery, pistons, rice, rubber, bananas, cassava, cashew nuts, shoes, suitcases, etc. Imports from China include investment and production products such as cotton, textiles, textiles, cotton, metal, construction materials, appliances and electronics, plastics, aluminum, furniture and paper and cardboard.
