Bangladesh arrests nearly 8,000 opposition activists in one week as elections approach
Dhaka: Police in Bangladesh have arrested a total of nearly 8,000 activists and opposition politicians in a large-scale crackdown that began after a series of riots, local media reported on Sunday. One in the capital Dhaka a week ago. This was released by the AFP news agency on Sunday, November 5, 2023.
The mass arrests come as general elections take place in January 2024. Bangladesh's largest opposition party, the BNP, and its allies have staged a series of mass protests in recent months to demand the resignation of Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina and allow an interim neutral government to take over. Responsibility for the electoral process.
Under Hasina's 15-year rule, the South Asian country has seen remarkable progress, but she has been accused of leading Bangladesh with an iron fist. The United States has sanctioned some of the top leaders of Bangladesh's police force for alleged human rights abuses.
