Cambodia's exports to China include clothing, footwear, fur, machinery, pistons, rice, rubber, bananas, cassava, cashew nuts, shoes, suitcases, etc. Imports from China include investment and production products such as cotton, textile, cotton, metal, construction materials, appliances and electronics, plastics, aluminum, furniture and paper and cardboard.
Cambodia and China are currently implementing the Free Trade Agreement (FTA), which entered into force in January 2022, simultaneously with the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP).
