"The establishment of this training course on economic information skills is in line with the need for economic journalists who have an understanding of the Digital Economy, or so-called expert economic journalists," he said. "Because in the past, previous economic journalists wrote news or just quoted data obtained for publicity."
In order to keep up with the development of technology and the global economy, understanding of the Digital Economy, also known as the Economist, is an important part of contributing to the economic development of people's income through economic information. This is a further confirmation from Mr. An Sithav.
The three key factors that must be addressed by leading economic journalists in the 21st century in the era of digital economy, which will be taught in the FTC curriculum, are: 1. To be able to understand the skeleton of our Cambodian economy in general 2: Be aware of the techniques used to support his information and the skeleton of economic information. Third: the connection between the economic skeleton and the structure of social media.
The course on "Fundamentals of Economic and Business News Writing" is taught by Mr. An Sithav, an economic information expert with over 15 years of experience in the field of journalism, such as newspapers, radio and television in Cambodia. In addition, An Sithav has received economic information training and economic information research from countries such as Australia, Japan, Singapore, the Philippines and Thailand.
The course focuses on three main points: First: the scope of economic information sources in Cambodia, second: the key to becoming a professional business economist, and third: trends and needs of economic information in daily life.
