(Oddar Meanchey): The administration of Trapeang Prasat district, Oddar Meanchey province, on November 4, 2023, started to organize a boat race to float lanterns and worship the moon god to make people happy.
According to the notification letter of Trapeang Prasat district administration, it is as follows: Chbar from November 4-5, 2023, including local boat sports in the six communes and other institutions to participate.
Separately, on the morning of November 4, 2023, the Trapeang Prasat District Boat Race Organizing Committee also organized a Krong Pali Sacrifice Ceremony to ask for happiness from the landowners to the “E” boat players as well as the people who participated. .
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Kong Kanarith, Deputy Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, Mr. Van Kosal, Chairman of the District Council, Mr. Haing Meng, Governor of Trapeang Prasat District, as well as the leaders of the three Armed Forces and many other working groups.
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province and Chairman of the Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, on the morning of November 4, 2023, led the working group to bring humanitarian donations of the Cambodian Red Cross to distribute to the affected Cambodian business people. A fire broke out in a stall in Chong Cham Market, Thailand, near the Cambodian border recently.
On that occasion, Mr. Pen Kosal sent a message of greetings from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia to the business community present here with remembrance and condolences. As for the fire that caused the fire in "Chong Cham" market, it damaged a lot of your shop equipment.
"Upon receiving this information, Samdech Kittipritthbandit, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, instructed the Red Cross branch officials in Oddar Meanchey to bring gifts to distribute immediately to alleviate the suffering for a while," said the provincial governor. "Even though the gift did not meet the demand for the actual damage, it did help some of the victims to share some of their livelihoods."
He said that natural disasters always happen eventually, but if caused by fire, you must be very careful and regularly prevent fires from happening, because the old saying goes, "Su die, do not die. "Sink the boat in the middle of the river, not just the house on fire."
The provincial governor also called on the general public to be very careful before leaving their homes or businesses to turn off the switch, turn off the electricity, check the fire in the stove, incense - candles when the fire is extinguished. Properly to prevent casualties and property damage, as in the case of fire.
Please note that "Chhong Cham" market is a market in Kab Cheung district, Surin province, Thailand, bordering O'Smach international border crossing in Samrong city, Oddar Meanchey province. The market caught fire at 9 pm on October 27, 2023 and was extinguished at around 1 am when the fire at Chhong Cham Market was caused by a power outage.
During the firefighting operation at "Chong Cham" market, 20 fire trucks (1 O'Smach Casino) were used, using about 50 water trucks. The fire damaged a total of 320 stalls with 203 owners, including 196 Cambodian and 7 Thai traders, with a total damage value of approximately 178,056,000 baht. .
