(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, has ordered the appointment and conferment of 145 leaders and members of various political parties as delegates to the Supreme Advisory Council.
The Royal Decree ordering the appointment and promotion was made on October 31, 2023.
The same article also states that political parties that do not participate in the election but are legally registered on the political party can also apply to join the Supreme Advisory Council by formally applying and must have Decision from the Prime Minister.
The Royal Decree also states that in carrying out the duties of the delegates of political parties as members of the Supreme Advisory Council, they have the full right to monitor the implementation of laws and policies of the Royal Government in order to help detect inactivity and irregularities. Corruption and abuse of power by individuals, officials or authorities at all levels and levels.
In carrying out this work, the members of the Supreme Advisory Council use their role as advisors to the Royal Government in order for the work process to be effective.
