(Phnom Penh): On November 3, 2023, the AIDS and Drug Commission held a meeting to evaluate the effectiveness of the implementation of Prakas No. 086, No. 194 and Guideline No. 008 with the support of the ILO.
The meeting was attended by representatives of ministries, institutions, the National AIDS Authority, the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, the Department of Labor and Vocational Training: the 25 provincial capitals, representatives of employers, unions and other relevant partner organizations.
Mr. Tun Sophorn, Representative of the ILO, stated that the implementation of Prakas No. 086, No. 194 and Guideline No. 008 is very important for the health and safety of the workforce.
On behalf of Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training: On that occasion, Dr. Huy Hansong, Secretary of State and Chairman of the AIDS and Drug Control Committee of the Ministry of Labor, thanked all parties to the AIDS and Drug Commission for jointly implementing Proclamation 086, 194 and Guideline 008. Aims to fight HIV / AIDS for workplace safety.
On that occasion, Dr. Hui Hansong said, urging the establishment of HIV / AIDS working groups or commissions in all factories to the maximum to continue to address the issue of HIV / AIDS in the workplace, ensuring that all workers have adequate information in Reducing the risk of HIV / AIDS and non-discrimination.
As a result, based on the tasks and plans of the AIDS Commission and the Ministry of Labor Inspector, the implementation of Prakas 086, 194 and Guideline 008 has been strengthened and promoted through continuous inspection and dissemination until now, but the implementation of the factory Enterprise is still limited. Overall, the number of factories that have complied with the prakas is about 13%, which is still low.
As for the entertainment services sector, the implementation has not achieved significant results due to the epidemic of Kovid 19, which has closed almost completely and a large number of reopening will take time. Czech pledges to strengthen and expand cooperation to support the priorities of the Ministry of Health, especially human resource training
Mr. Martin Vávra also said that it will help expand the scope of Cambodia-Czech bilateral cooperation in the field of health, including the provision of scholarships and joint training programs, associate degree in biomedical engineering between two major training institutions in Cambodia, the University of Health Sciences. And the Institute of Technology of Cambodia.
At the same time, the Ambassador also informed about the project to provide equipment at the National Children's Hospital and the University of Health Sciences in 2024.
On that occasion, the Minister thanked the Government of the Czech Republic through the Czech Embassy in Cambodia for always supporting the development of Cambodia in all areas, especially the health sector through the Maternal and Child Health Project at the National Children's Hospital in Phnom Penh. Phnom Penh and infrastructure assistance of Kampong Chhnang and Takeo Provincial Hospitals.
Please be informed that in this work discussion and courtesy call, the Ambassador congratulated the Minister on the occasion that he received the trust from the Royal Government of the seventh mandate to be appointed Minister of Health.
Mr. Hun Many Presides Over the Official Launch of "Clean Phnom Penh Campaign 2023"
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hun Many, Minister of Public Works and Co-Founder of Clean Project on November 3, 2023, presided over the official opening ceremony of the Clean Phnom Penh Campaign 2023 at Phnom Penh International University (PPIU).
In 2023, the "Clean Phnom Penh Campaign" has launched four major action plans under the slogan "Our morality, our Khmer tradition is transparent" to contribute to the promotion of waste management from Phnom Penh.
Under this new direction, Clean Project has developed four major action plans, including:
First: My heart is beautiful, Khmer is beautiful, a presentation by Kou Sopheap to young people, young women and students in the sense of cultivating good thinking as children, grandchildren, brothers, sisters, relatives, friends, good citizens and good students, good youth
Second: My work is clean, Khmer Clean is a program to discuss and increase friendship with factory workers in the concept of cultivating good thinking as a good citizen, good staff, increase work efficiency with a clean environment and good hygiene in the workplace.
Third: I am a beautiful, beautiful Khmer vine "is an activity to visit and share to students in educational institutions and private schools to educate and understand more about proper garbage disposal.
Fourth: Our business is clean, Khmer is clean "which is a forum for business owners and entrepreneurs to discuss to find appropriate ways in order to increase participation in sanitation by reducing plastic waste in the business and promote Develop sustainable business in accordance with the policies of the Royal Government and the legal standards in force.
In addition, the "Clean Project" also receives cooperation and support from relevant ministries, government institutions, private companies, associations, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions from secondary to higher education, both public and private, as well as many members of the public.
