At the Annual Summit on Cambodia Climate Change 2023 (CCCS23) in Siem Reap on the morning of November 3, 2023, the Minister of Environment stated that it is clear that climate change is a serious threat. And increasingly to the world.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth also announced the new Environmental Chakra Strategy 2023-2028, which will be launched on November 15, 2023.
"We need to focus not only on policy and strategy, but also on practical action to support the needs of people affected by climate change," said Eang Sophalleth. We need to work together to protect our environment and ensure a sustainable future for all Cambodians. ”
"Climate change is one of the biggest threats we are facing," said Justin Wyatt, Australia's ambassador to Cambodia. "This summit is an opportunity to discuss practical actions to adapt to the effects of climate change and achieve a carbon neutrality by 2050."
He added that Australia is stepping up cooperation and action on climate change in Cambodia. Through the CAPRED program, we will connect clean electricity to villages without access to electricity, increase water safety by increasing access to clean water in rural Cambodia, and support a waste-free business model in agriculture.
"We work together to improve our coordination and co-operation in supporting Cambodia's strategy to achieve carbon neutrality," he said.
Oknha Sear Rithy, Chairman of the Council of the MFI, said that the Summit highlighted the common understanding that tackling the challenges of climate change is inseparable from the foresight of the nation's future. And the world.
Markus Bürli, SDC Country Director for Cambodia, said: "We need to make sure that the technologies and services that are developed to help reduce and adapt to climate change are implemented." Senior officials of the Ministry of Public Works held a meeting to discuss plans and techniques on maintenance, repair, construction and inspection to assess the strength of the old road infrastructure.
