At the meeting, Australia acknowledged the importance of open dialogue between the public and private sectors and reaffirmed its commitment to supporting the Government-Private Sector Forum as an important forum for coordination. Dialogue between stakeholders in the public and private sectors.
"Cambodia's private sector has great potential to support Cambodia's economic development," said Justin Wyatt, Australian Ambassador to Cambodia. "This forum is a valuable way to strengthen the capacity and expand the potential of the private sector by promoting close cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and all working groups to address the challenges of the private sector."
Australia's support comes through Australia's largest economic development program, the Cambodia-Australia Partnership for Sustainable Economic Development (CAPRED). CAPRED is providing technical support in order to develop better work practices and ensure inclusive participation in this forum between the government and the private sector.
The 19th plenary session of this forum will take place on November 13, 2023 at the Peace Palace under the chairmanship of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
