(Kampong Chhnang): The administration of Kampong Chhnang province on the morning of November 3, 2023 celebrated the National Independence Day, November 9, the 70th anniversary of Cambodia's full independence from French colonization.
National Independence Day, November 9, 2023, was presided over by Mrs. Ke Chanmony, Member of Parliament for Kampong Chhnang Constituency, Mr. Siv Run, Chairman of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Council and Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province. Sub-provinces, ladies and gentlemen, leaders of departments around the province, government officials, the armed forces, teachers, students and a large number of people.
The provincial governor said that His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the King Father of Independence, territorial integrity and national unity of Cambodia, had sacrificed his body and intellect to fight within the framework of the Royal Crusade to demand independence. Cambodia was liberated from French colonization and declared independence on November 9, 1953.
This brave heroism is a good example for the next generation of Cambodians to build, protect the integrity and develop the nation to be more prosperous in the future, the people expressed their joy and happiness for the national pride that should not be Nothing can disturb the peace and peace of Cambodia.
Phnom Penh Capital Administration Introduces All Relevant Authorities to Strengthen Security and Order to Ensure Smooth Bankruptcy Examination, Sending Motorbikes Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): For two days, on November 6-7, 2024, the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority instructed all law enforcement forces, especially the forces of the 14 Khan Police Inspectorates in Phnom Penh to deploy traffic facilitation forces to strengthen Security and order to ensure that students go to the high school diploma exam on time.
This is the instruction of Mr. Keut Chhe, Acting Governor of the Board of Governors of Phnom Penh in the meeting on the measures to prepare for the Higher Secondary Diploma Examination this morning, November 3, 2023 at the Capital Hall, which was attended by the opposition unit. Corruption (ACU) and representatives of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, as well as the authorities and forces of the 14 districts.
Mr. Keut Chhe instructed the authorities as well as all the armed forces to increase security at all examination centers to make sure that there is no shock during the exam. In addition, the district authority must inspect the administration of any examination center where people live in the school and recommend to the Department of Health to put a team of doctors to treat as well as rescue when any candidate has a health problem.
Regarding the return of motorcycles, Mr. Keut Chhe advised not to take money during the two-day exam, all these expenses are paid by the Phnom Penh Capital Administration. For the police force of the 14 district police inspectorates is to suspend the force to tighten the road traffic law in order to facilitate the circulation of students to go to the high school diploma exam in time.
(Preah Sihanouk): On the morning of November 3, 2023, Dr. Mong Reththy, Senator and Preah Sihanouk Provincial Authority, led by Mr. Vong Naphat, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, attended the planting of 1,000 palm seedlings. As the first step in 10,000 projects.
