(Phnom Penh): Workers and unions have supported the social security system of voluntary health care for self-employed individuals and their dependents. The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, announced the push for this policy. For workers and self-employed, this policy will help reduce household expenses on health care.
The President of the National Union of Trade Unions, Mr. Fasali, emphasized that the establishment of a social security system for health care through voluntary contribution to self-employed individuals and their dependents. This is what workers and unions are looking forward to, as the regime will help ease the burden on families when one of their dependents becomes ill.
He said: "On behalf of me, the union representing workers, I am happy when workers' wages go up at the same time, if there is no mechanism to reduce costs to our workers, the wages they receive are not left. "No, because we have to support our families, including the high cost of health care."
In addition, worker Chim Saron expressed support for the government's policy to establish a voluntary contribution to the social security system for health care, as it has helped ease the burden on families.
Similarly, another worker, Chim Saren, is extremely happy because this policy will save her family a lot and reduce the cost even more because of free medical treatment and costs only 15,600 riels.
"For my family, he is very sick. Nowadays, my family's livelihood is in short supply. Going to the doctor one by one, happy and supportive when there is a regime, will help alleviate a lot of family expenses," she said.
