(Phnom Penh): Defendant Hak Udom, who was arrested for falsifying the King's message and cheating as a relative, was sentenced to prison on November 2, 2023.
I Rin, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, told Fresh News that Investigating Judge Hok Pov on the afternoon of November 2, 023, remanded Hak Udom in custody after the end of the prosecution. Investigated and charged with fraud, forgery of public documents and use of forged public documents under Articles 377, 378, 629 and 630 of the Penal Code.
Please be informed that recently, a fake royal message was shared on social media, with that message inviting Chan Mony to recite the Dharma during the King's Kathin Ceremony. Angkor Chey District, Kampot Province.
Later, the Ministry of the Royal Palace came out to reject the message, and the National Police Force cooperated with the relevant authorities to launch a series of searches to find the source who falsified the message.
After conducting a search until October 29, 2023, specialized forces proceeded to arrest a suspect who was a forgery of the King's message, named Hak Udom.
At the same time, the General Commission of the National Police also called on the public to be careful about sharing unidentified information that causes them to become a stepping stone to the schemes of fraudsters and to be responsible for the law.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth: The Royal Government has ambitions to reform the agricultural sector for better development to ensure food stability and boost exports
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, stated that the Royal Government has ambitions to reform Cambodia's agricultural sector to ensure better food security in the country and boost product exports. Agriculture to international markets.
The speech of General Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth was made at the launching ceremony of the "Joint Procedures for the Cambodian Food Reserve System" on November 2, 2023 at the Sofitel Hotel.
At the same time, the General Secretary urged the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, provincial administrations and relevant institutions to guide and disseminate widely to farmers on the methods and methods of smart farming through the use of existing water potential. Depending on the location, the use of rice varieties should be in accordance with the location and time of harvest, and research and dissemination of weather-resistant rice varieties and planting in all seasons.
He added that while Cambodia is a country rich in natural water resources and a multi-lane irrigation network, sub-national administrations and relevant units must continue to take the necessary measures to maintain and store as much water as possible for farmers. Farmland, that is, to use the potential of local water sources to the fullest extent possible.
He said that in the past, the Ministry has always managed to provide a short period of time to provide seeds to farmers when there are various disasters to improve rice production in Cambodia.
Minister of Water Resources chaired a meeting to prepare an action plan for the management and development of water resources and meteorology in 2024
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, in the morning of November 2, 2023, chaired a meeting to prepare an action plan for the management and development of water resources and meteorology in 2024 and a strategic plan and action plan. 3 years (2025-2027).
Please be informed that this planning meeting will be held for two days from November 2 to 3, with the participation of the Permanent Secretary of State, the leadership and the director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of all capitals and provinces.
The Minister also recommended to review the performance of duties in the past and reflect the strengths and weaknesses, as well as the challenges ahead to think together to solve in a timely manner, especially to make arrangements. The 2024 Action Plan and the Three-Year Strategic Plan and Action Plan (2025-2027) have been successful and comprehensive.
On that occasion, as the Chairman of the Commission, the Minister also announced the validity of the Commission and the Sub-Committee on drafting and updating laws, policies, master plans, strategic plans and legal documents of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology established by Decision No. 148, dated October 4, 2023.
Please be informed that Resolution 148 is divided into 5 sub-committees to review and draft and update laws, policies, master plans, strategic plans and legal documents of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology in order to strengthen the legal efficiency of the Ministry.
The Minister requested the Secretary of State, who is the chairman of each sub-committee, to arrange a meeting of his sub-committee as soon as possible to carry out the tasks set out in the decision. The Minister emphasized that the priority is to revise the draft sub-decree on the organization and functioning of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, reviewing the functions and duties of the Ministry in line with the first phase of the Pentagon strategy.
In this meeting, there were also a series of presentations by the leaders of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology from provinces such as Kampong Chhnang, Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Battambang, Pailin and Takeo.
