239 Families Affected by Floods in Serei Sophorn City and Mongkul Borei District Receive Donations from Dr. Sar Sokha and Lok Chumteav Ke Suon Sophy
(Banteay Meanchey): On the evening of November 1, 2023, at Stung Sen Restaurant, Kbal Spean Village, Sangkat Preah Ponlea, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province, 239 flood victims from Serei Sophorn City and Mongkul Borei District received donations from Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Director Minister of the Ministry of Interior and Lok Chumteav Ke Suon Sophy.
One family received food and supplies of 50,000 Riels, 1 bag of rice equal to 10 kg, 1 box of noodles, 1 can of fish sauce, 1 can of soy sauce, 1 can of fish. The donation ceremony was attended by Mr. Oum Rath, Provincial Governor, Deputy Governor of the three units, Mr. Sreng Sophal, Governor of Serey Sophorn City, Ms. Chat Sochea, Chief of Preah Ponlea Sangkat and many other relevant officials.
The worst floods were in two districts:
* Mongkul Borei district: affected 1,131 families in 8 communes, evacuated 68 families, affected 2,587 hectares of crops, 7 schools, 1 pagoda, flooded 60 roads, equal to 46,890 meters long * Serei Sophorn Affected the houses of 746 families, evacuated 124 families to safety. One city and six districts are indirectly affected.
During the flood, all the people were evacuated by the three authorities together with the authorities to evacuate all the people to a safe place, some people can stay at home temporarily and also distribute food for a while. Chea Hoher, too.
(Bangkok): Dr. Chea Serey, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, led a delegation to the 4th Meeting of the UNESCAP Macroeconomic Policy Committee on Poverty Reduction and Development Financing (UNESCAP) in Bangkok. Thailand.
Dr. Chea Serey stated that the National Bank of Cambodia has been working to ensure that the banking system in Cambodia can play an important role in mobilizing funding to support the Royal Government of Cambodia's goals to achieve the terms of the Paris Agreement. On climate change.
It should be noted that the National Bank of Cambodia has developed a number of initiatives to develop a sustainable financing support mechanism, including the development of a roadmap for promoting sustainable financing, and the establishment of a support cycle. Capital flows, setting out a framework for reporting and capacity building.
Dr. Chea Serey called on vulnerable countries to step up their efforts to increase funding to support resilience and adapt to the effects of climate change.
She and her counterparts agreed on key points in boosting capital inflows to increase green and sustainable investment in developing countries. Therefore, investors need to check their conditions and needs in accordance with the actual situation and possibilities of those countries.
The French Embassy in Cambodia issues a press release on the 70th anniversary of Cambodia's independence: 1953 A new beginning in French-Cambodian relations
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the 70th anniversary of Cambodia's National Independence Day, the French Embassy and the French Institute in Cambodia, in collaboration with the Museum of Economy and Currency, Isanvarman (SOSORO) and the Research Institute for Development (IRD), will hold events to celebrate A special bond that connects the two countries through exhibitions, conferences and film screenings.
On November 8, another exhibition will be inaugurated on the fence of the French Embassy entitled "Cambodia Sees the Space of 70 Years of Cooperation". This exhibition is organized by the Research Institute for Development (IRD) based on the work done in partnership with Cambodia's major university institutions.
Through aerial and satellite imagery taken over the last 70 years, the exhibition will highlight the changing landscape and evolution of Cambodia. It also shows how Earth observation techniques can better respond to the challenges of sustainable development.
For the film, from November 8 to 11, the French Institute in Cambodia will screen four French-language films related to the independence of Cambodia and other countries of former French Indochina. Screenings of these films will take place in the presence of director Philippe Fréling, who is currently based in Phnom Penh.
The Royal Government has implemented a joint procedure for the Cambodian food reserve system to promote the distribution process to the affected people more effectively, as of October, nearly 300,000 tons of food and seeds have been distributed to the people
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Economy and Finance, has announced the implementation of the "Joint Procedures for the Cambodian Food Reserve System", which reflects the Royal Government's consideration for the provision of food reserves to the poor. As of the end of October, the government had distributed nearly 300,000 tons of food and seeds to farmers.
At the same time, the Royal Government has the ambition to reform Cambodia's agricultural sector to ensure better food security in the country and promote the export of agricultural products to international markets.
In addition, the Royal Government has considered and paid close attention to the provision of food to help the poor and vulnerable people who may need food. Especially when a disaster or natural disaster occurs.
Dr. Vong Sandab, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, said that the two reforms of the Cambodian food reserve system to ensure that the Cambodian food reserve system can help people affected by food and crop disasters (rice and vegetables) in a timely manner. And enough. The first was conducted in 2016, modifying the sale of sorghum seeds with a 50% discount to poor and vulnerable farmers free of charge.
