(Preah Sihanouk): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court has decided to temporarily detain a Deputy Commander of the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie and a local commander of the Phnom Sruoch District Gendarmerie, as well as a total of six members of the Royal Gendarmerie. The effects of drug offenses.
An official of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court told Fresh News on the afternoon of November 2, 2023 that the officer of the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie has been remanded in custody by an investigating judge. On November 1 yesterday.
Please be informed that a Deputy Commander of the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie and a Commander of the Phnom Sruoch District Gendarmerie, as well as a total of six members of the Royal Gendarmerie, were arrested by the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Gendarmerie after being found involved in a case of bribery. Drug offenses.
Brigadier General Eng Hee, spokesman for the National Gendarmerie, told Fresh News this morning, October 31, 2023, that this operation was carried out in accordance with the order of General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander-in-Chief. Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie.
Brigadier General Eng Hee confirmed that on October 26, 2023, the Sihanoukville Provincial Gendarmerie cracked down on drug offenses and continued to search and find some relevant individuals. The specialized force also extended the jurisdiction to Kampong Speu province according to the procedure by reporting to the prosecutor of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court and according to the hierarchy.
From October 27 to 29, 2023, the Judicial Police Force of the National Gendarmerie and the Sihanoukville Provincial Gendarmerie listened to the interrogation of 6 individuals involved in the crime, who are officers of the Provincial Gendarmerie. Kampong Speu. According to the confession, all six individuals may be involved in cases of benefiting from drug offenses.
He said that according to the results of drug tests, the six suspects did not contain drugs as some media reported. Judicial police officers have been building procedures to refer to the Sihanoukville Provincial Prosecutor's Office and to comply with the "Confidentiality of Investigation" provisions.
Brigadier General Eng Hee asserted that under the leadership of Brigadier General Sao Sokha, Commander of the National Gendarmerie, individuals suspected of crimes must comply with the law sent to court, adhering to the slogan "The country must be protected. For the people must serve the law, must respect the crime must be suppressed.
It should be informed that the officers of the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie who were arrested were: First: Colonel Tith Vannak, Deputy Commander of the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie, Second: Colonel Yos Dina, Commander of the Phnom Sruoch District Gendarmerie and the Gendarmerie Under the advice of 4 others, a total of 6 people.
He added that the operation found and destroyed a total of 68,350 landmines and unexploded ordnance. 400,496 families directly and indirectly benefited.
In the first 9 months of this year, CMAC and the Voluntary Mine Action Network conducted 18,401 mine awareness and mine risk education campaigns to target groups, equivalent to 914,551 houses, with a total of 1 participant. 418 863 people.
In particular, there were 24 cases of landmines and explosive remnants of war, with a total of 27 victims, including 4 dead and 23 injured.
The Ministry of Agriculture will not allow fishing with heavy barriers near canals to catch fish in Kampong Chhnang province from the 2023 season.
Mr. Chhim Chhoeun, a representative of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Community Federation Commission, confirmed to Fresh News that fishing with fishing nets, canals or other ditches to catch the above fish has been approved by the law. The Ministry of Agriculture, where he allows the community to fish for three fish per season to make fish prahok to distribute to people in the community.
However, from the 2023 season onwards, the Ministry of Agriculture will no longer allow fishing with barricades, canals or ditches to catch fish in Kampong Chhnang province. He also stated that the number of canals and ditches, which are places for fishing that used to be done in previous years, if you count the small and large, there are about 30 places throughout Kampong Chhnang.
In that, he also put a strict plan to the Fisheries Officers of Sangkat, Sangkat and Khan to be responsible in each section, if Sangkat and the division under its control have the above fishing offenses, must be responsible before the law. Respectively.
He added that for some time, some canals have been set up to set up barricades to catch some fish, such as in Kampong Tralach and Chulkiri districts, but our district officials there have also instructed the people. Those fishermen should be dismantled immediately. Therefore, the case of fishing with the construction of a canal in Kampong Chhnang province from 2023, he will not allow it to happen.
On this occasion, he also called on professional officers, especially fishing communities to participate in the implementation of the guidelines of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to jointly prevent and prevent all kinds of fishing offenses, especially the barrier. Close canals or other ditches in the bases, asking not to happen at all.
Australian Ambassador to Cambodia seeks more processing of Cambodian agricultural products and integration of high quality Cambodian products into international markets
(Siem Reap): Justin Wyatt, Australian Ambassador to Cambodia, has stated that Australia wants to see more agricultural processing in Cambodia, which will help create more jobs in Cambodia, and see links to high quality Cambodian products. Go to the international market.
This statement was made by Justin White at the inauguration of the first fish ladder in Cambodia, worth nearly $ 100,000 and to be built under research and funding from the Australian Center for Research. International Agriculture (ACIAR) and the Australian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade (DFAT) are located in Sleng Dam, Sleng Village, Kralanh District, Siem Reap Province.
The Australian Ambassador to Cambodia said that through the cooperation between Cambodia and Australia, Australia is preparing to build a very important fish ladder as a vehicle for fish to travel up and down the river to the spawning grounds to help fish. Go through various obstacles.
This will increase the number of fish and the community will get more nutrition. It can be said that the whole community has a better life and access to better agriculture, especially healthy rivers.
"This cooperation is part of Australia's long-standing and comprehensive partnership with Cambodia in the agricultural sector," he said. Australia is implementing a number of agricultural programs in Cambodia. Agriculture is building a climate-resilient agricultural system, and what we want to do for Cambodia, for example, is to create rice varieties that are resistant to floods and droughts.
He recalled that last year Australia announced the use of Champis rice varieties that can be grown several times a year. This new rice variety can withstand drought. "What we want to do is try to help Cambodia increase the value of its agriculture so that Cambodia can export more agricultural products."
(London) - At the invitation of the United Kingdom Department of Foreign Affairs, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, led a delegation from the ASEAN Secretariat to pay a working visit to the United Kingdom on the morning of November 1, 2023. He met with representatives of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the United Kingdom Ministry of Business and Trade in London.
On that occasion, all parties discussed the priorities of Dr. Kao Kim Hourn in the term of the Secretary-General of ASEAN as well as the preparations for Laos to chair ASEAN in the future.
During the meeting, the two sides discussed the upcoming ASEAN-UK Economic Integration Program and strengthening economic cooperation in key ASEAN priority areas such as digital transformation, green change, supply chain, resilience and services. Finance and so on.
On the same day, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn attended the ASEAN-UK Business Council Private Sector Roundtable. During the talks, the ASEAN Secretary-General thanked the ASEAN-UK Business Council for its contribution to strengthening economic ties between the ASEAN-UK business community, as well as for exploring new possible collaborations. Go between ASEAN and the UK.
On the afternoon of November 1, 2023, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn met with Professor Sir Steve Smith, the British Government International Academic Champion. During the meeting, the two sides discussed ways to further engage between ASEAN and UK educational institutions through scholarships, as well as the exchange of professors and researchers.
During the visit, on the afternoon of November 1, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn paid a courtesy call and discussed with British Deputy Prime Minister Oliver Dowden. During the meeting, the two sides discussed in-depth ASEAN-UK partnership and explored new opportunities for future cooperation.
The first large-scale export to the Indonesian market was carried out by Green Trade of the Ministry of Commerce in collaboration with the Cambodian Rice Federation.
During the rice handover program, the Indonesian side inspected and praised the quality of Cambodia's long grain white rice as good quality and promised to continue to support Cambodia.
The Minister of Commerce, Cham Nimmol, encouraged Green Trade and the Cambodian Rice Federation to work hard to open up the rice market to Indonesia and requested that this activity be continued for other markets.
The Minister also mentioned the progress on market expansion, especially with China, where the Ministry of Commerce is negotiating the procedure for signing the 7th MoU for a further 20% increase for 2023-2024. .
The Minister expressed her support for the plan to expand the Cambodian rice market to the Indonesian market by at least 100,000 tons by 2024, with additional recommendations including:
* Green Trade, together with the Cambodian Rice Suction Federation and all exporters, must continue to work regularly with Indonesian importers to jointly promote Cambodian rice in the national market to stimulate and increase demand for consumer acceptance. More Cambodian rice.
* Request the Indonesian side to encourage investors as well as local rice importers to invest and receive more Cambodian rice imports, as Cambodian rice tastes as good as rice that has won the World Cup five times. Recently won a gold medal for fragrant rice made in China recently.
* The Ministry of Commerce, all Consular Departments, and Trade Attachments are always ready to support trade facilitation and promotion for the growth of the Cambodian rice market. The King transfers and appoints 13 Secretaries of State and Undersecretaries of State of the Secretariat of Border Affairs
