Congratulations on the 70th Anniversary of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces! Troops in Intervention Division 3 volunteer to donate blood to save patients' lives
(Preah Vihear): Officers, deputies and soldiers of the 3rd Intervention Division on November 1, 2023 volunteered to donate blood to the Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department for humanitarian activities to save the lives of patients in need of blood. Necessary as well as to celebrate the 70th anniversary of the birth of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
In particular, Mr. Kim Rithy praised the heroism of the officers, deputies and soldiers of the 3rd Intervention Brigade and the 3 Intervention Brigades who volunteered to donate blood to save the lives of all people. All ranks, all classes, non-racist, with heartfelt love.
He said that the current donation of blood to the Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department by officers, deputies and soldiers is also to celebrate the 70th anniversary of the birth of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (1953-2023).
Please note that the blood donation program "Give love" is one of the topics in the blood donation campaign in cities and districts throughout Preah Vihear province, initiated by Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear province in order to contribute to meeting the blood needs of the department. Referral doctor on January 16 who has been facing anemia to help victims and patients who need blood every day.
Commander-in-Chief: "At all stages, retirees and disabled fighters have made significant contributions to the protection of territorial integrity and peacekeeping."
(Phnom Penh): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, stated that at all stages of history, retirees and disabled fighters have made significant contributions to the protection of territorial integrity and the building of peace, social stability, which is the foundation for Develop the nation.
This statement was made by the Commander-in-Chief during a ceremony to equip ranks and medals for retired soldiers to be transferred from the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces 2023 on the morning of November 2 at the 70th Brigade Headquarters. .
The General expressed his deep gratitude and gratitude to all the retirees and disabled veterans who have spent valuable time in their lives to contribute to the reconstruction, defense and development of the nation at all stages of history.
He stated that the current retirement and transfer of disabled soldiers from the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces is in accordance with the provisions of the law, which is applied every year, and the Royal Government, the Ministry of National Defense and the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces continue. Take care of the well-being, love, and brotherhood on behalf of ex-combatants.
He highlighted the merits of retired and disabled soldiers left for the society, including: Participation in the overthrow of the genocidal regime, participation in the implementation of Samdech Techo's win-win policy brings peace and national unity, participation in maintenance Security, peace, stability, social order, contribution to training of human resources, strengthening the defense sector and the reform of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to be strong.
The Commander-in-Chief instructed the retirees and disabled fighters to continue to maintain the noble spirit of heroism and dignity as the outstanding citizens of the motherland to continue to be a good example in the society and the Royal Government and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces will always remember the sacrifices and merits. A large number of retirees and the disabled to the motherland in the past.
At the same time, the Commander-in-Chief also instructed the leaders at all levels and relevant units to continue to support the retirees and disabled fighters, especially those in need, by adhering to the spirit of solidarity, helping each other and jointly defending peace. The Royal Government for the development of the nation to grow further.
