Dr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that this morning's meeting was attended by 653 pregnant workers. These 29 factories include: 20 garment factories, 3 travel bags and bags factories, 2 shoe factories, 2 laundries, 1 garment embroidery, 1 garment printing.
Kandal currently has 477 factories and enterprises, employing a total of 152,000 workers, earning a total of more than 469 million US dollars per year. Of these, 166 garment factories employ a total of 130,000 workers, earning more than $ 408 million a year.
