Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration will take the strictest legal action without exception for anarchists and ringleaders who try to encroach on state land
(Preah Sihanouk): The Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration will implement the strictest legal measures, without exception, for anarchists and ringleaders who try to encroach on state land. This is according to the press release received by Fresh News on November 1, 2023.
According to the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration, anarchists have recently invaded the forest and built six huts on a 1-hectare plot at O'Damrei (Otaveng) group. 22nd, Village 3, Sangkat 1, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province, in the sustainable use area of Prek Toek Sap Kbal Chhay, which borders the community.
After receiving this information, in May 2023, the ranger of the Sihanoukville Provincial Department of Environment went to educate and instruct them to voluntarily dismantle themselves. To this day, the anarchist group not only refuses to dismantle as instructed, but also continues to build huts and erect fences to occupy state land.
According to Article 62, point 1 and article 56, point 4 of the "Law on Protected Areas", this act of encroachment on forest land is illegal and punishable by 5 to 10 years in prison. And a fine from fifteen million riels to one hundred and fifty million riels, and in case of non-recidivism, the sentence shall be doubled.
The Sihanoukville provincial administration will take the strictest legal action, without exception, for anarchists and ringleaders who try to encroach on state land and bring them to justice.
In this regard, in order to avoid legal penalties, the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration once again calls on all relevant parties to stop all activities as described above by dismantling buildings and other works and leaving the site. Handed over to the competent authorities and institutions.
