(Phnom Penh): Cambodia's white rice in the amount of 3,500 tons exported the first leg to Indonesia on November 2, 2023, after Cambodia agreed to supply rice to Indonesia.
Oknha Chan Sokheang, president of the Cambodian Rice Federation, said that Cambodia would continue to ship two more tonnes of white rice to Indonesia for a total of 10,000 tonnes.
It should be noted that during the meeting between Mr. Joko Widodo, President of Indonesia, and His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia in Jakarta, Cambodia agreed to supply about 250,000 tons of rice per year to Indonesia to maintain food security and consumption. Country.
The agreement to import 250,000 tonnes of rice a year from Cambodia comes after India stopped exporting rice to Indonesia. Indonesia initially planned to import 1 million tonnes of rice from India, but the proposal was rejected.
Pen Sovicheat, secretary of state and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, recently told Fresh News that the agreement to supply about 250,000 tonnes of rice a year to Indonesia was for four years.
