29 houses collapsed and roofs opened due to strong winds in Svay Rieng province
(Svay Rieng): At least 29 houses in Svay Rieng province were damaged by collapse and open roofs caused by rain and strong winds, but this case did not cause any danger to human or animal life.
According to Svay Rieng provincial authorities, at 4:30 a.m. on October 31, 2023, heavy rain and strong winds caused the collapse of 29 houses and the opening of roofs in Svay Rieng province, including four in Chantrea district and One in Svay Teap district, 24 in Kampong Ror district, 20 in Svay Yean commune, four in Kampong Ror district and four in Khseth commune, but no one was injured.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, last October, accompanied by Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet, attended the "Belt and Road" forum in Beijing, China. Continue to visit some other big Chinese companies to seek investment from those companies to Cambodia.
During his visit from October 20 to 24, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol met with 12 major Chinese companies. In meeting with these companies, the Deputy Prime Minister explained the investment policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia. In particular, the political support and encouragement from Samdech Hun Sen to invest in Cambodia, both domestic and foreign investors.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol also highlighted the potential and favorable conditions for investment in Cambodia.
On the last day of the visit, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol attended a ceremony to commemorate the 10th anniversary of China's Four Principles in Beijing. The ceremony was presided over by Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, during the visit, a large Chinese company decided to invest in Cambodia after hearing an explanation of policies related to potential investment and other opportunities. Determined by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said the Chinese giant planned to invest about $ 500 million and was considering investing in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone or in the Svay Rieng Special Economic Zone.
