(Siem Reap): The fish ladder is a fish passage that allows fish to swim across to the upper part of the dam. In fact, under the research and funding of the Australian Center for International Agricultural Research (ACIAR) and the Australian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade (DFAT), the first fish ladder in Cambodia was built in Sleng village, Sranal commune, Kralanh district, Siem Reap province. .
The Sleng Fish Ladder is expected to increase fishing income to 5,000 families and help conserve more than 100 local fish species, making it an important step towards a sustainable future. Fisheries and fishing communities of Cambodia.
According to Lok Vuong, chief of Sranal commune, Kralanh district, as the commune chief, he was very happy to receive the fish ladder, and this fish ladder is very important for all kinds of fish to be able to spawn. Various areas. In particular, this fish ladder is very important for the people in this community.
"Our community is very happy after the construction of this fish ladder and would like to thank the Royal Government, relevant ministries, institutions and development partners for their support, especially the conservation of natural resources, especially fisheries, which makes the commune of "I have more fish resources to feed the local people."
The Sranal commune chief confirmed that after receiving the fish ladder, the commune authority will set up a committee to manage the fish ladder to conserve fish in the river that flows through Sranal commune.
"We hope that through the construction of this fish ladder will increase the local fishery resources, especially the endangered species, it can be revived. "When I set up a committee to manage fish ladders and conservation, we have to be determined by fisheries experts to identify protected areas and fishing grounds."
Sleng village chief Bing Ban was overjoyed to receive the first fish ladder, and this was the first time he had seen a fish ladder in his area. He believes that through the explanations of the white experts, the fish ladder is very important to the local people, as this fish ladder will be an important path for other fish species to climb. Spawning in other areas.
Mr. Bing Ban confirmed that the fish ladder location will also be a tourist attraction in the area by visiting the location because his people want to see the fish ladder, which is the first fish ladder to be built in Cambodia.
Ms. Kan Saloeung, a resident of Sleng village, thanked the Australian Government, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and relevant institutions for building a fish ladder in her locality, which will increase the number of fish through this ladder. Original.
Ms. Kan Saloeung confirmed that this is the first time that she, along with local people in Sranal commune, Kralanh district, as well as people in other areas, have known what is called a fish ladder. Through the fish ladder, her area will be rich in fish, especially contributing to local poverty reduction.
