BEIJING, Oct. 31 (Xinhua) - General Tea Seiha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Defense, paid an official and friendly visit to the People's Republic of China (PRC) on the afternoon of October 31, 2023. The National Defense Council led a bilateral meeting with General He Weidong, Vice Chairman of the Central Military Commission of the People's Republic of China.
During the meeting, He Wei Tung welcomed General Tea Seiha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia, to pay an official and friendly visit to the People's Republic of China and hoped that through this visit, the two armies would strengthen Expand cooperation and cooperation with each other for continuous development and progress.
General Tea Seiha further stated that the friendly relations between Cambodia and China are good and lasting. Currently, Cambodia is developing the country under the shadow of peace.
The Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia mentioned the cooperation between the two armies in continuing the Golden Dragon Exercise and the Peace Angel Exercise, which in the past has led to the strengthening of the capacity of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
