According to a preliminary statement from the International Monetary Fund's Article IV mission, the increase was due to the recovery of tourism and the growth in exports of solar panels and components, which were the main drivers of growth. However, garment exports remain weak, showing little sign of recovery in recent months. The construction sector, on the other hand, has shown a slow recovery.
Inflation rebounded to 3.8% in September 2023 due to higher food and fuel prices. For the full year 2023, inflation is projected at an average of 2.3 percent and could reach 3 percent by 2024 due to rising commodity prices.
The current account deficit narrowed in 2022 and is expected to gradually narrow further due to the strong recovery in non-garment exports, tourism and remittance flows. International reserves are expected to remain stable.
Public debt is projected to increase moderately over the last decade and the risk of a debt crisis remains low.
The IMF said structural reforms should focus on diversifying trade partners, investing in new growth factors and boosting investment in climate change mitigation. Recent diversifications, such as the production of solar panels and electrical components, are encouraging in this context. Strengthening public governance and transparency will be important in attracting more foreign direct investment and ensuring macroeconomic stability.
The IMF will continue to provide technical assistance to help improve statistics and other areas of capacity development.
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications will support the Ministry of Information and the Ministry of Tourism in the internal digital revolution.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications will support the Ministry of Information and the Ministry of Tourism in the internal digital revolution in line with the Digital Government of Cambodia 2022-2035 and the fifth pentagon of the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Posts.
The signing of the agreement focuses on three main objectives: cooperation in the establishment of verify.gov.kh, verification of documents, infrastructure and internet connection, and the provision of digital skills training for civil servants under the Ministry of Information.
The signing ceremony was attended by about 250 leaders and officials of the three ministries. The ceremony was held on the morning of October 31, 2023 at the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
Based on the contents of the Memorandum of Understanding signed today, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications will support the Ministry of Information and the Ministry of Tourism in the internal digital revolution in line with the Digital Government of Cambodia 2022-2035 and the Fifth Pentagon. Of the first phase of the pentagonal strategy, for example:
Today's signing ceremony is the sixth time that the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has organized a signing ceremony of a memorandum and agreement on cooperation in the establishment of a verify.gov.kh verification nursery and digitalization within the ministry. Government institutions and higher education institutions.
Please also note that the verify.gov.kh file verification nursery is a nursery of the Royal Government developed by KPT. And is intended to eliminate document fraud, provide ease of use and authentication of documents, provide confidence, save time and reduce costs, as well as promote digital transformation in line with international practice.
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Yim Lat, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that saving money with official institutions is a contribution to economic development and an important and necessary financial challenge because saving money with financial institutions is As a source of capital to meet the financial needs of local investors.
Mr. Yim Lat made this remark during a dissemination workshop on "ASEAN Savings Day" under the theme "Saving habits for you and your family" in Kampong Thom province on October 31, 2023.
He said that saving money is an important financial need and necessary to meet future urgent financial needs to ensure financial stability. At the same time, today's savings options are also abundant, in addition to saving at home, you can also save money with official banking and financial institutions, as it offers both security and interest.
"Furthermore, when saving money with a formal institution, it means contributing to economic development because the public's savings with a formal institution are an important source of capital to meet the financial needs of investors in the country," he said. .
Ms. Dith Nita, Vice Chairman of the Board of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, stated that MFIs have participated in changing this mindset and promoting the institutional savings habits of the institution among the local and rural people by making it easier for the people. In depositing deposits, providing innovative and easy-to-use services and raising awareness of the importance of savings, especially among low-income citizens.
(Phnom Penh): A fire broke out in a house of a villager at 8:40 am on October 31, 2023, along the concrete road, Damnak Sangke village, Sangkat Prek Kampus, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh. .
Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Fire Prevention and Rescue Office, told Fresh News that in accordance with the order of Major General Chuon Narin, Deputy National Police Commissioner and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner. Instructed the specialized force of the Office of Fire Prevention, Rescue and Rescue to pay close attention to the rescue operation in a timely manner.
Upon receiving this order, Colonel Prohm Yorn led the direct command of the fire brigade stationed at the target of Dangkor District Hall and the target in front of Wat Botum Vat to intervene and spray water in time to prevent the fire from continuing. Residents' houses nearby.
In the above operation, the specialized police force used 10 fire trucks, including 3 fire trucks of the Phnom Penh Capital Office, using 3 trucks with 12 cubic meters of water, and a number of auxiliary vehicles from the Cambodian Beer Company. One truck consumes 1 cubic meter of water and 6 airport cars consume 20 cubic meters of water per truck.
Colonel Prohm Yorn confirmed that in the case of the fire above, the wooden structure on the stone, 5 meters by 8 meters, completely burned a house and did not cause the fire to spread to the neighbor's house. Professional police forces took full control at 9:30 a.m. on the same day. No one was injured in the incident, which was caused by an electric shock.
Government officials and agricultural students applaud Australian Government's initiative to build Cambodia's first fish ladder
(Siem Reap): Sleng village in Siem Reap's Kralanh district, the first site in Cambodia, was built under research and funding from the Australian Center for International Agricultural Research (ACIAR) and the Australian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade (DFAT). ).
This innovative solution is especially important for Cambodia as hydropower and irrigation development are critical to economic growth.
The Sleng Fish Ladder helps restore fish migration and reconnect the good waterways between the Tonle Sap Lake and local communities along the river and fishing trails, which benefits them both socially and economically. The fish ladder will help reduce the impact of irrigation development, such as dam regulators, on fish migration.
With Australia's project to provide a solution to Cambodia's fisheries problem, Khun Savoeun, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Chair of the Ladder Working Group, expressed support for the ladder project and is committed to participating. Cooperate in the implementation of this project in the future.
Mr. Khun Savoeun said that the Ministry of Agriculture expects the fish ladder project to have more active participation from relevant ministries and institutions to make this work possible.
According to Ms. Hung Sotheanika, a third year student of Natural Resource Management and Development at the Royal University of Phnom Penh, she said that the visit to the construction site of the fish ladder was unique and the first time for Cambodia, especially the fish ladder. Makes it easy to move out to the upper reaches of the river to other spawning grounds without endangering the fish.
The agricultural student expressed hope that if Cambodia builds more stairwells, it will be part of increasing the number of fish stocks. In particular, it will improve the livelihood of fishermen to another level through increased fish production in rivers, lakes and streams.
For Ms. Yim Pich Molika, a student from Kampong Cham National School of Agriculture, said that by visiting the location of the fish ladder in Sleng village, Kralanh district, Siem Reap province, she and other students have a better understanding of the importance of the fish ladder. In particular, better understand the biological geography of other fish species that are present in Cambodia.
Please be informed that the Australian Government has joined the representatives from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Fisheries Administration, local authorities and the people on November 1, 2023 to inaugurate the newly built fish ladder in Sleng village in Kralanh district. Siem Reap.
