In fact, in 2024, the Royal Government, headed by the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Hun Manet, has planned to budget about 165 million US dollars to help poor and vulnerable families.
According to the draft law on finance for management 2024, which was fully approved by the Cabinet last weekend, the planned budget of 674.5 billion riels, equivalent to about 165 million dollars to serve. Establishment of a national social assistance program for poor families, vulnerable groups in poor households and vulnerable households in times of economic crisis and emergency.
Please be informed that according to the confirmation of the National Council for Social Protection, in the first 9 months of 2023, the Royal Government of Cambodia has spent 1,542,066 232,000 Riels or equivalent to 385,516,558 USD on the implementation. Social assistance programs and social security systems to provide protection to citizens, especially poor and vulnerable families across the country.
More than $ 385 million will be spent in the first nine months of 2023 to provide protection to people, especially poor and vulnerable families across the country, on the following programs:
1: Cash support program for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19 in the amount of 1,152,027,390,400 riels. In the last month, there were approximately 701,452 beneficiaries, equivalent to 2,760,085 people. From the time of implementation in March 2020 to October 2023, the Royal Government of Cambodia has spent about 4,850 billion riels or 1,212.69 million dollars. This sponsorship program is still ongoing.
3: Social assistance program in cash for vulnerable families who were severely affected by the flood 31,998,808,000 Riels, with 99,169 target families, equivalent to 372,859 people, received subsidies from this program. This program has already been completed.
4: Cash subsidy program for vulnerable families during the inflationary pressure of 139,487,196,600 Riels, with a total beneficiary of 500,000 families or about 1.8 million people. This program has already been completed.
6: Additional allowance program for female workers at childbirth in the amount of 22,439,600,000 Riels, which provided benefits to 383,075 female workers in and out of the system during childbirth. This sponsorship program is ongoing.
8: Social security system for health care for public servants, veterans and youth rehabilitation of 35,619 525,000 Riels, which covers about 428,755 public servants and about 125,349 veterans and youth rehabilitation. This sponsorship program is ongoing.
9: Occupational Social Security Regime on Public Risk for 3,155,685,000 Riels, which provided occupational risk protection to approximately 240,117 public servants. This sponsorship program is ongoing.
11: School feeding program using agricultural products in the community of 12,809,250,000 Riels. The School Feeding Program has a total of 300,000 beneficiaries in the 1,113 target schools, which includes a school-based feeding program using community agriculture with 110,645 beneficiaries. This sponsorship program is ongoing.
