Analysis: Sino-US summit shows positive signs
BEIJING (Reuters) - A visit to the United States by Wang Yi, a member of the Politburo of the Communist Party of China (CPC) Central Committee and Chinese Foreign Minister, was hailed as "hopeful for improving relations," the Associated Press reported. China and the United States. "
"Both sides have agreed to make joint efforts to achieve a meeting between the two heads of state in San Francisco," which has caused widespread interest. Analysts say there is no doubt that this is a clear sign that people have reason to remain optimistic, but also to be honest about the development of Sino-US relations in the future.
The United States has also shown a positive attitude in this regard, emphasizing that the US side hopes that relations between the two countries will be stable and sustainable. Faced with the pressure of the 2024 US presidential election, the current US government needs more points in diplomacy. During the China-US summit, the US side showed an active and realistic change of direction, as well as estimates.
The development direction of Sino-US relations is important for itself and the world. The positive signs that the Sino-US summit shows show that everyone has a reason to be optimistic, but also to be honest about the development of Sino-US relations, and expect the US side to be brave and wise. Fully wise to follow the direction with China.
