Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet issued five recommendations for the Capital-Provincial Administration to strengthen the provision of public services and solve problems (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The province strengthens its public services and solves local problems effectively for the seventh-term government.
This recommendation was made on the occasion that the Prime Minister presided over the inauguration of the new administration building and achievements in Kampong Speu province and declared the province of Asmin on the morning of October 30, 2023.
Samdech Thipdey's five recommendations for this capital-provincial administration include the following:
1. Capital-provincial administrations must participate in strengthening the recruitment of officials to work with merit, transparency, fairness, environment and efficiency, that is, to ensure that officials serve the people with high ability, ethics and professionalism.
2. The Capital-Provincial Administration shall set up a mechanism to report or receive complaints about any issues from the people easily and in a timely manner and to respond to the people quickly and efficiently. Capital and provincial administrations must also cooperate and provide support to the National Authority for Out-of-Court Dispute Resolution
3. Capital-provincial administrations must make sure to provide the best public services to the people and absolutely must not complicate these public services and cause additional burden on the people.
4. Capital-provincial administrations must follow the national policy of the Royal Government and must always be ready to do the work that must be delegated effectively, gain authority and responsibility.
And 5: Capital-provincial administrations must strengthen their cleanliness, especially to avoid the illegal use of power to the detriment of the interests of the people, the Royal Government will take the strictest action if cases of abuse of power occur. The Royal Government will assist the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Administration to have the ability and capacity to fulfill their duties better.
