The Prime Minister stated that the resolution of disputes outside the court system will help reduce congestion in the court system, and the final decision in this dispute resolution mechanism has the same weight as the final verdict of the court.
The speech of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet was made on the occasion of presiding over the inauguration of the new administrative building and achievements in Kampong Speu province and declaring it as a demining province on the morning of October 30, 2023.
"What is special about this out-of-court dispute resolution mechanism is that it helps to reduce congestion in the courts, because disputes that have already been resolved within the framework of the new authority must be considered resolved without a complaint," he added. "The court, with the authority's agreement to end the dispute, has the same force as the final verdict of the court."
At the same time, the Prime Minister also instructed the relevant authorities to disseminate to the people to understand the mechanism of dispute resolution outside the court system so that they can benefit from the new mechanism of the Royal Government.
Please be informed that on the morning of October 27, 2023, the Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers fully approved the draft Royal Decree on the establishment, organization and operation of the National Authority for Dispute Resolution.
The National Dispute Resolution Authority (NACC) is headed by a Deputy Prime Minister with four deputies, of which the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice is a permanent deputy and has seven members.
Samdech President Hun Manet considered the establishment of the National Authority for Dispute Resolution outside the Judiciary as an urgent task and must be expedited as soon as possible.
