(Phnom Penh): The problem of lack of capital, access to low interest rate loans is still a challenge for many entrepreneurs in Cambodia, as the owners of small and medium enterprises (SMEs) often raise the difficulty of doing business and expanding production. .
In response, the Small and Medium Enterprise Bank of Cambodia (SME), a state-owned bank, has decided to reduce its annual interest rate by an additional 0.25% to alleviate the difficulties faced by SME owners. Get a low-interest loan to stabilize your business and expand your business.
This additional 0.25% annual interest rate discount is only for member enterprises of associations or partner institutions, including: Cambodian Women Entrepreneurs Association, Cambodian Water Suppliers Association, Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association, Cambodian Cashew Association, Cambodian Food Producers Association, Cambodian Association. Small and Medium Enterprises of Cambodia, Cambodian Entrepreneurs, Listtech Companies, EGG (Cambodia) MK and CEO Masters Club.
"SME Bank is a state-owned enterprise, so the goal of profitability is not the bank's bond, what we want is to contribute to the growth of the economy by helping businesses," he said. "Small and medium enterprises in Cambodia, because SMEs are an important driving force in promoting sustainability and economic growth."
He said the association will continue to cooperate more so that all 31 cashew processing enterprises can access loans.
The president of the Cambodian Cashew Association also said that so far, there are 31 enterprises in the association, some of which have been approved for $ 2.5 million at an interest rate of 5.5% per annum.
However, the association urges banks to ease some unnecessary conditions and increase service delivery a little faster so as not to exceed the cashew harvest in 2024.
"If we are late, the flow of raw cashew nuts will flow from country to neighboring countries," he said. And if we can not afford to buy, Vietnamese traders will lower the price of raw materials of Cambodian farmers at will. "Therefore, to help Cambodian farmers, only provide the right conditions for local cashew processing enterprises so that they can afford to buy raw materials stockpiled to supply the international market."
Ms. Keo Mom, President of the Cambodian Women Entrepreneurs Association, said that SME banks always consider women entrepreneurs who provide loans at low interest rates so that women entrepreneurs have capital to organize and expand their business.
"The interest rate reduction indicates that the Ministry of Economy and Finance, especially the Royal Government, is always paying attention to help expand the business, so this interest rate reduction allows entrepreneurs to get loans at interest rates," she said. Low can be used to expand the business as well.
At the same time, SME Bank has been studying to increase the loan amount to $ 3 million, because in the past, SME Bank has provided the highest loan capital at only $ 500,000 and will increase to $ 1 million in 2023. However, the increase in the loan amount to $ 3 million is only for some businesses, not general.
SME Bank currently has branches in Battambang, Tbong Khmum and Phnom Penh. To facilitate customers more easily, the bank aims to expand the network of 3 more branches in Kampot, Banteay Meanchey.
Please be informed that SME Bank provides loans with interest rates between 5.88% and 6.88% per annum for priority sectors and loans with fixed interest rates of 7.5% for regular sectors. Lending with the most concessional interest rate of 5.5% for small and medium enterprises with female owners if they are properly registered and in the priority areas.
By 2024, more than $ 800 million is planned to support six priority policy programs and the implementation of five key government measures.
(Phnom Penh): Six priority policies have been announced and implemented by the 7th legislature of the Royal Government led by Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
At the same time, five priority challenges have been set by the Royal Government to address key issues, including: public administration, health services, education, safe villages and communes, and the justice system.
To support the six priority policies and the implementation of five key measures by 2024, the Royal Government plans to budget more than $ 800 million to implement these priorities.
According to the summary of the draft budget for 2024 published by the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the budget for 2024 is also designed to support six priority policy programs and the implementation of five key measures for addressing priorities. Of the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly as follows:
* Six priority policy programs include:
1: Expansion of health care services towards global health coverage is provided with a total budget of 340.4 billion Riels, equivalent to approximately $ 83 million
2: Vocational and technical training for young people from poor and vulnerable families throughout the country was provided with a total budget of 146.6 billion Riels, equivalent to approximately $ 36 million.
3: Establishment of the National Social Assistance Program for Poor Families, Vulnerable Groups in Poor Families and Vulnerable Families in Times of Economic Crisis and Emergencies is planned to have a budget of 674.5 billion Riels equivalent. Will be about $ 165 million
4: Implement the strategy on the development of the informal economy to be able to participate in the economy in the system and be able to benefit from the formal social protection system. In case there is a need for funding for this program, the Royal Government can review the budget of approximately 410 billion Riels, equivalent to approximately $ 100 million prepared for the new policy.
5: Coordination mechanism and financing program to increase production, market and maintain the price of important agricultural products at a reasonable level is planned to be 410 billion Riels, equivalent to about 100 million USD
6: Deployment of agricultural technical officers to all communes with agricultural activities throughout the country to promote agricultural productivity and assist farmers' families in promoting their agricultural products and establishing agricultural associations in rural areas. The budget is 16.9 billion riels, equivalent to about 4 million dollars.
* Implementation of 5 key measures, including:
1: Strengthening the capacity of public administration, focusing on strengthening the quality, efficiency, and achievements of officials and institutions, a budget of 492 billion Riels, equivalent to approximately 120 million USD
2: Improving the quality of education by focusing on improving the quality of public schools from kindergarten to secondary school is planned with a budget of 419 billion riels, equivalent to about 102 million dollars.
3: Improving the quality of health services by focusing on strengthening the capacity to provide primary health services at the local level, with a budget of 241 billion Riels, equivalent to approximately $ 59 million.
4: Strengthening the implementation of the "Safe Village-Commune-Sangkat" policy, focusing on reducing and leading to the elimination of drug trafficking and use in the community is planned budget 38.1 billion riels, equivalent to about 9 million dollars
5. Strengthening and improving the quality and efficiency of the justice system is planned at a budget of 10.3 billion Riels, equivalent to approximately $ 2.5 million.
