The Royal Government plans to issue $ 108 million in state securities in 2024 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): In 2024, the Royal Government plans to issue $ 440 billion in state securities, equivalent to approximately $ 108 million. This is according to the summary of the draft law on finance for management in 2024, published by the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
A summary of the draft law states that the issuance of 440 billion riels, equivalent to approximately $ 108 million, is to repay the principal and interest of state securities issued last year and to finance investment projects. Can provide revenue directly to the Royal Government and provide quick results to ensure investment efficiency and sustainability of public debt management and the national budget.
By 2024, the Royal Government will need financing of 4.70% of GDP, which will be supported by domestic financing through the issuance of state securities and 4.39% of foreign financing. Of GDP, equivalent to more than $ 2 billion to boost economic development.
Please be informed that the Royal Government will start issuing the first public securities in 2022 in the amount of 300 million dollars through the issuance mechanism of the National Bank of Cambodia. In 2023, through the National Budget Law, the Royal Government announced the issuance of 200 million US dollars in securities.
Ministry of Water Resources announces weather conditions in Cambodia for October 29, 2023, with moderate to moderate rain
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a weather forecast in Cambodia for October 29, 2023.
The Ministry states that the Kingdom of Cambodia is affected by low pressure in the South China Sea. On October 29, the high pressure system over Thailand and the South China Sea weakened. Winds from the southwest and south bring moisture from the Gulf of Thailand to the coast, while winds from the east and southeast bring moisture from the South China Sea. Come to Cambodia.
From October 30 to November 2, there will be another high pressure system from China covering the northern part of Thailand extending to the South China Sea. Meanwhile, the northerly and northeasterly winds will intersect with the southeasterly winds, which will carry moisture from the South China Sea, forming a rain cloud over Cambodia. :
On October 29, in some provinces in the coastal and central lowlands, including Phnom Penh, there will be moderate to moderate rain mixed with thunder and gust covering 40% to 50% of the land area. .
Some provinces in the highlands will receive light to moderate rainfall, covering 30% to 40% of the land area. From October 30 to November 2, there will be light to moderate rain mixed with thunder and gusts over the coastal and highland areas, covering 30% to 40% of the land area.
