(Kampong Thom): Ms. Khuon Khundy, Senator and Mr. Sous Yara, Member of Parliament for Kampong Thom Constituency, on the afternoon of October 27, 2023, visited a group of 224 “E” boat players in Kampong Svay District and encouraged them to stay healthy. Well done.
Ms. Khuon Khundy stated that the purpose of organizing this Water Festival is to commemorate the merits of our Cambodian ancestors, especially thanks to the glorious Navy of the great metropolis that fought wars and won over enemies everywhere. .
She continued that under the leadership of the Royal Government, led by Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister continues to connect and care for all of you and maintain peace, sympathy with you is still the same. Therefore, all of you must understand and trust our leadership.
Ms. Khuon Khundy also urged all "E" boat players to take good care of their health because it is the first priority and if we neglect it, it will affect the upcoming game, even if the game Win or not, we did our best, and all these allowances and materials were kept for each boat.
She sincerely hopes that all the players will remain united to win and have a chance to go to the next national competition to compete for the national title.
Kampong Thom Military Chief Inspects Flood Situation and Conversation with Families of Veterans Living on Social Land Concessions in Santuk District
(Kampong Thom): Major General Som Sun, Commander of Kampong Thom Military Operation Area and Chairman of the Kampong Thom Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on October 28, 2023, led his colleagues and female soldiers on the Gender Working Group of the Military Operation Area Command. Kampong Thom inspects the flood situation that is flooding some houses and infrastructure of veterans living on social land concessions in Dang Kda village, Kraya commune, Santuk district.
Lt. Gen. Som Sun instructed the families of the veterans and the troops stationed on the social land concession to inspect the body of garbage and other objects in each drainage system so that the water can flow quickly down from the village. Veterans' ranks. For the situation of the size of the narrow drain that can not release water in time and must report to the relevant professional institutions for improvement in the future.
He urged the families of all veterans to be careful and advise their children to avoid danger due to the floods and to live in good hygiene to avoid various diseases during the floods.
On this occasion, the President of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province brought precious gifts from Samdech Hun Sen and Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony to support the families of 15 flood-affected veterans. Each family receives 25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of soy sauce and 1 stick of canned fish.
It should also be noted that 141 families of disabled veterans and victims of poor veterans were given a social land concession by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia, for a family of one and a half hectares and a new house for Live to build a new life in the society. The Cambodian Association of Surgeons, Oral and Maxillofacial Surgeons runs a training course on first aid and emergency in the field of dentistry.
(Phnom Penh): In order to promote the field of dentistry in Cambodia and provide services to people with high quality and safety, the Cambodian Association of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgeons has opened a training course on first aid and emergency in the field of dentistry. At Preah Ang Duong Hospital on October 27, 2023.
The training was chaired by the Director of Ang Duong Hospital, Associate Professor Lou Ly Kheang, and was attended by well-known speakers and experts in Cambodia.
On the occasion of the opening of the training course, which took place throughout the day, the director of Preah Ang Duong Hospital encouraged all the doctors in the association to work hard to learn the cream from the senior Ream as a speaker and to be united. Find new, high-tech tips to ensure the provision of high-quality face and jaw surgery health services to the people.
Professor Luli Kheang said, "After completing this training, all of our doctors can continue to share their experiences with each other, which is practical, if there is a gap at any point can ask. Find solutions through networking. In addition, encourage doctors, the next generation of resources to work together in solidarity to support the field of dentistry to grow more in the future.
In response, Dr. Phan Sandeth, President of the Cambodian Association of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgeons, expressed his deep gratitude to the Director of Preah Ang Duong Hospital for always providing opportunities and good advice that made the process of The association has grown to this day.
Dr. Phan Sandeth said that for today's participation, there are doctors from 16 provinces and cities from private clinics and public institutions, this is the first training, so only 80 people will be limited. There is also a series of training sessions.
He emphasized that this training is both theoretical and practical, presented by our famous Cambodian national speakers according to each section and skill from first aid and emergency, safe and secure. High efficiency.
At the same time, he called on all doctors in Cambodia to strengthen as well as develop personal knowledge to be effective and safe in practice in the clinic so that our people receive a service of the same quality as the people. Neighbors and grow well. In particular, jointly promote the health sector, such as dentistry in Cambodia.
