Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crime instructs officers to apply their knowledge, skills and experience effectively to prevent and suppress drugs
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath, Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes, instructed law enforcement officers to apply their knowledge, skills and experience effectively to participate in the prevention of all types of drug crimes.
This instruction was made on the occasion of the Lieutenant General representing General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, and General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General for Anti-Drug Planning, to close the refresher course on drug crime investigation and money laundering, procedures. And the Law on Drug Control at the Anti-Drug Department of the General Commission of the National Police on the afternoon of October 27, 2023.
According to the report of Colonel Hong Vanrith, Deputy Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes, the five-day study from October 23 to 27, 2023, the participants paid attention to listen to the trainers. And gain good and intermediate knowledge.
Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath said that the trainees who completed the course had to use their knowledge, skills and experience as law enforcement officers of the Anti-Drug Department to serve the interests and effectiveness of the Office aimed at eliminating production, trafficking and distribution. And the illegal use of drugs of any form and form.
The lieutenant general said that this refresher course will be available for law enforcement officers or open courses for capital-provincial police commissioners as well.
