(Phnom Penh): At least 75 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on October 27, 2023 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on October 28, 2023.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 75 suspects, 64 were arrested in 30 criminal cases and 11 were arrested in five drug offenses.
Two Japanese nationals with outstanding achievements in the field of education and the strengthening of Cambodia-Japan friendship received letters of commendation from the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan handed over a letter of commendation to two Japanese nationals who have contributed to the promotion of Japanese language education in Cambodia, especially to further strengthen the ties between the two countries.
The Japanese nationals who received letters of commendation from the two Japanese Foreign Ministers include:
Onihu Fumi, President of the Japan-International Cultural Institute, contributes to the promotion of Japanese language education in Cambodia. In 1995, Oni Hifumi established the Hifumi Japanese Language School in Siem Reap, and she has been working on Japanese language education and cultural exchange for almost 30 years.
The school provides not only Japanese language education but also human resource development and job search support for uneducated or unemployed young people. The number of students enrolled has steadily increased to more than 3,000 so far. Most of the students are active in areas such as tourism, nursing and education.
The Japanese Ambassador extended his congratulations to Onihi Fumi and Fukudato Mofiko on the occasion of receiving a letter of commendation from the Japanese Foreign Minister in 2022.
Ms. Oun has also made a significant contribution to improving the quality of Japanese language education in Cambodia by organizing Japanese language education workshops for Cambodian Japanese language experts and teachers and planning the Angkor Japanese Language Competition. Wat and so on. In addition, she also acts as a representative of karate and judo training venues, as well as working to promote and raise awareness of Japanese culture.
Mr. Fukudato Mofiko in 1997 was sent to work at the Royal University of Phnom Penh as a Japanese language teacher through the JICA Japan Overseas Cooperation Volunteer (JOCV), where he worked. In promoting and developing Japanese language education in Cambodia after being suspended due to the civil war since 1974.
Mr. Oueno Atsushi expressed the hope that Japanese language education in Cambodia will continue to grow and through his activities, many students will become a bridge of friendship between Japan and Cambodia and mutual understanding. More deeply.
The Ambassador of Japan affirmed that their many years of success in Cambodia, especially the careful and friendly teaching of children and students, not only helped to increase the level of Japanese language education in Cambodia and promote Understand not only Japanese culture, but also greatly contribute to the further development of bilateral relations.
The Japanese Foreign Minister's letter of commendation is given to individuals or groups who have made outstanding achievements in the international field in recognition of their contribution to the promotion of friendly relations between Japan and other countries.
