The NEC will officially launch the Citizenship Statistics Management Program to manage polling station and polling station locations in 2024
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has modernized and plans to officially launch the Population Statistics Management Program to manage polling station and polling station locations in 2024 to serve Annual voter list review and registration.
In order to ensure that the annual voter registration and voter registration process is successful in the preparation phase, the NEC shall compile population statistics, estimate and determine the number and location of voter registration and polling stations for implementation. Annual voter registration and voter registration plan.
The purpose of this census is to determine and estimate the number of people over the age of 18 who have not yet registered to vote, the number of voters who will be removed from the voter list as a basis for determining the number of polling stations and the number of polling stations. Register the ballots to be used as well as determine the location of those polling stations.
However, through the program that all the trainees received today, it is even more convenient for the CEC to manage and compile the statistics of the estimated population, manage the location of the polling station and the location of the polling station at In its provincial capital.
