(Banteay Meanchey): Cambodia and Thailand jointly eliminate human trafficking through the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Rehabilitation and Rehabilitation Center, located in the center of Poipet, not far from Poipet Referral Hospital.
This project is a development cooperation between the Royal Government of Thailand and the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the General Department of International Cooperation, the Thai Ministry of Foreign Affairs in collaboration with the Thai Ministry of Social Development and Human Security, and the Thai Embassy in Cambodia. The construction process will be completed in August 2023.
Thai Prime Minister Setha Thavisin officially handed over the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Rehabilitation and Rehabilitation Center to Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet during his official visit to Cambodia on September 28, 2023.
The Center for Rehabilitation and Rehabilitation was established with the aim of helping to address human trafficking in Cambodia and in the region, with joint vocational training and mental health rehabilitation for victims to integrate during repatriation. Retire and be free from sustainable human trafficking.
On October 20, 2023, the General Department of International Cooperation led a delegation of International Cooperation Partners in Thailand inspected the construction process of Poipet Referral Center and Referral Hospital in Banteay Meanchey Province.
Delegates from the International Cooperation Partnership to Thailand include the Australian Embassy in Thailand, the United States Agency for International Development, the Asia Regional Office, the JICA Office in Japan and the French Office for Development, and Mr. Hun Saroeun, Cambodian Ambassador to Thailand. Both representatives of the Sa Kaeo Provincial Health Department.
The inspection was warmly welcomed by senior officials of the Cambodian side, including: Mr. Nhek Vannara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Mr. Ngor Mengchruon, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province and Ms. Chhea Manit, Director of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Detention Center.
